elated to the malignancy which would limit full compliance with the study. \nReceived radiation to more than 10% of bone. \nPrior treatment with topotecan or gemcitabine. \nHypersensitivity to camptothecin or nucleoside analogues. \nUse of an investigational agent within 30 days.       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nWomen [AND] of child-bearing potential [AND] that do [NOT] not practice adequate contraception. \nPregnant [OR] or lactating. \nReceived more than one primary chemotherapy regimen. \nConcomitant [OR] or previous malignancies with the exception of adequately treated basal cell [OR] or squamous cell skin cancer, [OR] in situ cervical cancer, [OR] incidental carcinoid, [OR] or other cancer from which the patient has been disease [NOT] free for 5 years. \nActive uncontrolled infection requiring antibiotics. \nConcurrent severe medical problems unrelated to the malignancy which would [NOT] limit full compliance with the study. \nReceived radiation to more than 10% of bone. \nPrior treatment with topotecan [OR] or gemcitabine. \nHypersensitivity to camptothecin [OR] or nucleoside analogues. \nUse of an investigational agent within 30 days.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Women [AND] of child-bearing potential [AND] that do [NOT] not practice adequate contraception. 
Pregnant [OR] or lactating. 
Received more than one primary chemotherapy regimen. 
Concomitant [OR] or previous malignancies with the exception of adequately treated basal cell [OR] or squamous cell skin cancer, [OR] in situ cervical cancer, [OR] incidental carcinoid, [OR] or other cancer from which the patient has been disease [NOT] free for 5 years. 
Active uncontrolled infection requiring antibiotics. 
Concurrent severe medical problems unrelated to the malignancy which would [NOT] limit full compliance with the study. 
Received radiation to more than 10% of bone. 
Prior treatment with topotecan [OR] or gemcitabine. 
Hypersensitivity to camptothecin [OR] or nucleoside analogues. 
Use of an investigational agent within 30 days.
