Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nAre pregnant or lactating. \nHave participated in any other studies involving investigational products within 30 days prior to entry into this study. \nAre undergoing an acute withdrawal syndrome from drugs or alcohol. \nHave an Axis I diagnosis of Schizophrenia, Schizoaffective Disorder, Schizophreniform Disorder or Bipolar I Disorder as diagnosed by the Structured Clinical Interview for DSM-IV Axis I Disorders (SCID-I), and pertinent subsequent for ruling out exclusionary diagnoses. \nHave an unstable medical disorder as determined by physical examination or laboratory testing. The primary investigator will be responsible for making this judgment based on the above. \nHad an unsatisfactory response to a previous adequate trial of quetiapine as judged by a study investigator. \nPatients cannot begin psychotherapy during the study period, but may continue if started prior to the study. \nPatients who are currently receiving quetiapine therapy may not undergo a washout period and then restart quetiapine in the study.       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nAre pregnant [OR] or lactating. \nHave participated in any other studies involving investigational products within 30 days prior to entry into this study. \n Are undergoing an acute withdrawal syndrome from drugs [OR] or alcohol. \n Have an Axis I diagnosis of Schizophrenia, [OR] Schizoaffective Disorder, [OR] Schizophreniform Disorder [OR] or Bipolar I Disorder as diagnosed by the Structured Clinical Interview for DSM-IV Axis I Disorders (SCID-I), and pertinent subsequent for ruling out exclusionary diagnoses. \n Have an unstable medical disorder as determined by physical examination [OR] or laboratory testing. The primary investigator will be responsible for making this judgment based on the above. \n Had an unsatisfactory response to a previous adequate trial of quetiapine as judged by a study investigator. \nPatients [NOT] cannot begin psychotherapy during the study period, [AND] but may continue if started prior to the study. \nPatients [AND] who are currently receiving quetiapine therapy may [NOT] not undergo a washout period and then restart quetiapine in the study.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Are pregnant [OR] or lactating. 
Have participated in any other studies involving investigational products within 30 days prior to entry into this study. 
 Are undergoing an acute withdrawal syndrome from drugs [OR] or alcohol. 
 Have an Axis I diagnosis of Schizophrenia, [OR] Schizoaffective Disorder, [OR] Schizophreniform Disorder [OR] or Bipolar I Disorder as diagnosed by the Structured Clinical Interview for DSM-IV Axis I Disorders (SCID-I), and pertinent subsequent for ruling out exclusionary diagnoses. 
 Have an unstable medical disorder as determined by physical examination [OR] or laboratory testing. The primary investigator will be responsible for making this judgment based on the above. 
 Had an unsatisfactory response to a previous adequate trial of quetiapine as judged by a study investigator. 
Patients [NOT] cannot begin psychotherapy during the study period, [AND] but may continue if started prior to the study. 
Patients [AND] who are currently receiving quetiapine therapy may [NOT] not undergo a washout period and then restart quetiapine in the study.
