V diagnosis; DSM-IV criteria for body dysmorphic disorder, [OR] bipolar affective disorder, [OR] schizophrenia, [OR] psychotic disorder, current alcohol/ [OR] substance abuse.\nA previous adequate trial of topiramate\nComorbid major depressive disorder diagnosis which predates OCD diagnosis\nCognitive behavioural therapy [OR] or additional psychotherapy in past four months\nAllergy [OR] or hypersensitivity to topiramate\nBMI < 20\nHistory of kidney stones<|eot_id|>']
