depressants.\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nOutpatient [AND] with primary DSM- IV OCD\nCompletion of a 14-week open label trial of one the following SRI\'s: fluoxetine 80 mg/day, [OR] paroxetine 60 mg/day, [OR] fluvoxamine 300 mg/day, [OR] clomipramine 250 mg/day, [OR] sertraline 200 mg/day, [OR] citalopram 60 mg/day, [OR] escitalopram 30 mg/day [AND] and demonstrating a [NOT] non [OR] or partial responses to SRI treatment (CGI-I of 3 or 4, Y-BOCS reduction of < 35%)\nStable (8 wks or longer) concurrent medications including benzodiazepines, [OR] sedative hypnotics, [OR] antipsychotics, [OR] and antidepressants.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Outpatient [AND] with primary DSM- IV OCD
Completion of a 14-week open label trial of one the following SRI's: fluoxetine 80 mg/day, [OR] paroxetine 60 mg/day, [OR] fluvoxamine 300 mg/day, [OR] clomipramine 250 mg/day, [OR] sertraline 200 mg/day, [OR] citalopram 60 mg/day, [OR] escitalopram 30 mg/day [AND] and demonstrating a [NOT] non [OR] or partial responses to SRI treatment (CGI-I of 3 or 4, Y-BOCS reduction of < 35%)
Stable (8 wks or longer) concurrent medications including benzodiazepines, [OR] sedative hypnotics, [OR] antipsychotics, [OR] and antidepressants.
