Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nAdequate performance status: \nBreast - Karnofsky score > 50; \nOvarian, endometrial or cervical - Gynecologic Oncology Group (GOG) performance score ≤2 \nIf female and of childbearing potential, are willing to use adequate contraception (hormonal, barrier method, abstinence) prior to study entry and for the duration of study participation. \nNormal organ function within 14 days of study entry \nDiagnosis of one of the following malignancies: \nMetastatic breast cancer (BR) \nMetastatic ovarian cancer (OV) \nMetastatic endometrial cancer (EM) \nMetastatic cervical cancer (CX) \nMeasurable metastatic disease (>1cm) in at least one site other than bone-only \nProgression on or failure to respond to at least one previous chemotherapy regimen for metastatic disease \nProgression on prior therapy with a hormonal agent if estrogen receptor or progesterone receptor positive, and/or with trastuzumab if HER2-neu positive. If patient has progressed through hormone or trastuzumab therapy only, must have received one chemotherapy regimen. \nMeasurable metastatic disease as defined by Response Evaluation Criteria in Solid Tumors (RECIST) \nPrimary tumor must have been diagnosed histologically as either epithelial ovarian cancer, fallopian tube cancer, or primary peritoneal cancer (not borderline or low malignant potential epithelial carcinoma). \nSubjects must have failed at least two previous chemotherapy regimens. Paclitaxel must have been a component of one or both regimens and cisplatin or carboplatin must have been a component of one or both regimens. \nMeasurable metastatic disease \nHistologically proven recurrent or persistent endometrial cancer that is not amenable to curative treatment with surgery and/or radiation therapy AND has failed 2 previous treatment regimens \nMeasurable metastatic disease \nHistologically proven recurrent or persistent squamous cell carcinoma, adenosquamous carcinoma, or adenocarcinoma of the cervix that is not amenable to curative treatment with surgery and/or radiation therapy AND has failed 2 previous treatment regimens. \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nAdequate performance status: \nBreast - Karnofsky score > 50; \nOvarian, [OR] endometrial [OR] or cervical - Gynecologic Oncology Group (GOG) performance score ≤2 \nIf female [AND] and of childbearing potential, [AND] are willing to use adequate contraception (hormonal, [OR] barrier method, [OR] abstinence) prior to study entry [AND] and for the duration of study participation. \nNormal organ function within 14 days of study entry \nDiagnosis of one of the following malignancies: \nMetastatic breast cancer (BR) \nMetastatic ovarian cancer (OV) \n Metastatic endometrial cancer (EM) \n Metastatic cervical cancer (CX) \nMeasurable metastatic disease (>1cm) in at least one site other than bone-only \nProgression [OR] on or failure to respond to at least one previous chemotherapy regimen for metastatic disease \nProgression [OR] on prior therapy with a hormonal agent [AND] if estrogen receptor [OR] or progesterone receptor positive, [OR] and/or with trastuzumab [AND] if HER2-neu positive. If patient has progressed through hormone [OR] or trastuzumab therapy only, must have received one chemotherapy regimen. \nMeasurable metastatic disease as defined by Response Evaluation Criteria in Solid Tumors (RECIST) \nPrimary tumor must have been diagnosed histologically as either epithelial ovarian cancer, [OR] fallopian tube cancer, [OR] or primary peritoneal cancer ([NOT] not borderline [OR] or low malignant potential epithelial carcinoma). \nSubjects must have failed at least two previous chemotherapy regimens. Paclitaxel must have been a component of one or both regimens [AND] and cisplatin [OR] or carboplatin must have been a component of one or both regimens. \nMeasurable metastatic disease \nHistologically proven recurrent [OR] or persistent endometrial cancer [AND] that is [NOT] not amenable to curative treatment with surgery [OR] and/or radiation therapy [AND] AND has failed 2 previous treatment regimens \nMeasurable metastatic disease \nHistologically proven recurrent [OR] or persistent squamous cell carcinoma, [OR] adenosquamous carcinoma, [OR] or adenocarcinoma of the cervix [AND] that is [NOT] not amenable to curative treatment with surgery [OR] and/or radiation therapy [AND] AND has failed 2 previous treatment regimens.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Adequate performance status: 
Breast - Karnofsky score > 50; 
Ovarian, [OR] endometrial [OR] or cervical - Gynecologic Oncology Group (GOG) performance score ≤2 
If female [AND] and of childbearing potential, [AND] are willing to use adequate contraception (hormonal, [OR] barrier method, [OR] abstinence) prior to study entry [AND] and for the duration of study participation. 
Normal organ function within 14 days of study entry 
Diagnosis of one of the following malignancies: 
Metastatic breast cancer (BR) 
Metastatic ovarian cancer (OV) 
 Metastatic endometrial cancer (EM) 
 Metastatic cervical cancer (CX) 
Measurable metastatic disease (>1cm) in at least one site other than bone-only 
Progression [OR] on or failure to respond to at least one previous chemotherapy regimen for metastatic disease 
Progression [OR] on prior therapy with a hormonal agent [AND] if estrogen receptor [OR] or progesterone receptor positive, [OR] and/or with trastuzumab [AND] if HER2-neu positive. If patient has progressed through hormone [OR] or trastuzumab therapy only, must have received one chemotherapy regimen. 
Measurable metastatic disease as defined by Response Evaluation Criteria in Solid Tumors (RECIST) 
Primary tumor must have been diagnosed histologically as either epithelial ovarian cancer, [OR] fallopian tube cancer, [OR] or primary peritoneal cancer ([NOT] not borderline [OR] or low malignant potential epithelial carcinoma). 
Subjects must have failed at least two previous chemotherapy regimens. Paclitaxel must have been a component of one or both regimens [AND] and cisplatin [OR] or carboplatin must have been a component of one or both regimens. 
Measurable metastatic disease 
Histologically proven recurrent [OR] or persistent endometrial cancer [AND] that is [NOT] not amenable to curative treatment with surgery [OR] and/or radiation therapy [AND] AND has failed 2 previous treatment regimens 
Measurable metastatic disease 
Histologically proven recurrent [OR] or persistent squamous cell carcinoma, [OR] adenosquamous carcinoma, [OR] or adenocarcinoma of the cervix [AND] that is [NOT] not amenable to curative treatment with surgery [OR] and/or radiation therapy [AND] AND has failed 2 previous treatment regimens.
