Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nOther tumor type than adenocarcinoma \nCentral nervous system (CNS) metastases or prior radiation for CNS metastases \nGastric outlet obstruction or intestinal obstruction \nEvidence of gastrointestinal bleeding \nThe patient has bony lesions as the sole evaluable disease. \nPast or concurrent history of neoplasm other than stomach cancer, except for curatively treated non-melanoma skin cancer or in situ carcinoma of the cervix uteri \nPregnant or lactating women, women of childbearing potential not employing adequate contraception \nOther serious illness or medical conditions \nUnstable cardiac disease despite treatment, myocardial infarction within 6 months prior to study entry \nHistory of significant neurologic or psychiatric disorders including dementia or seizures \nActive uncontrolled infection \nOther serious underlying medical conditions which could impair the ability of the patient to participate in the study \nConcomitant administration of any other experimental drug under investigation, or concomitant chemotherapy, hormonal therapy, or immunotherapy \nconcomitant drug medication; The following drugs cause drug interaction with S-1. \ni. Warfarin, phenprocoumon: increase bleeding tendency ii. Increase blood concentration of phenytoin iii. sorivudine: inhibit DPD -> increase toxicity according to fluoropyrimidine iv. allopurinol : decrease activity of S-1       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\n  -  Histologically confirmed diagnosis of locally advanced or metastatic gastric adenocarcinoma\n  -  At least one evaluable lesion according to the RECIST version 1.1 standard\n  -  15 mile catchment area to facilitate overseeing systemic chemotherapy administration\n  -  Concomitant systemic chemotherapy with S-1 regimen\n  -  Neutrophil count on or just before chemotherapy due date of >1.5\nExclusion Criteria:\nOther tumor type than adenocarcinoma \nCentral nervous system (CNS) metastases [OR] or prior radiation for CNS metastases \nGastric outlet obstruction [OR] or intestinal obstruction \nEvidence of gastrointestinal bleeding\nThe patient has bony lesions as the sole evaluable disease. \nPast [OR] or concurrent history of neoplasm other than stomach cancer, except for curatively treated [NOT] non-melanoma skin cancer [OR] or in situ carcinoma of the cervix uteri \nPregnant [OR] or lactating women, [OR] women [AND] of childbearing potential [NOT] not employing adequate contraception \nOther serious illness [OR] or medical conditions \nUnstable cardiac disease [AND] despite treatment, myocardial infarction within 6 months prior to study entry \nHistory of significant neurologic [OR] or psychiatric disorders including dementia [OR] or seizures \nActive uncontrolled infection\nOther serious underlying medical conditions which could impair the ability of the patient to participate in the study \nConcomitant administration of any other experimental drug under investigation, [OR] or concomitant chemotherapy, [OR] hormonal therapy, [OR] or immunotherapy \nconcomitant drug medication; The following drugs cause drug interaction with S-1. \ni. Warfarin, [OR] phenprocoumon: increase bleeding tendency ii. Increase blood concentration of phenytoin iii. sorivudine: [NOT] inhibit DPD -> increase toxicity according to fluoropyrimidine iv. allopurinol : decrease activity of S-1<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
  -  Histologically confirmed diagnosis of locally advanced or metastatic gastric adenocarcinoma
  -  At least one evaluable lesion according to the RECIST version 1.1 standard
  -  15 mile catchment area to facilitate overseeing systemic chemotherapy administration
  -  Concomitant systemic chemotherapy with S-1 regimen
  -  Neutrophil count on or just before chemotherapy due date of >1.5
Exclusion Criteria:
Other tumor type than adenocarcinoma 
Central nervous system (CNS) metastases [OR] or prior radiation for CNS metastases 
Gastric outlet obstruction [OR] or intestinal obstruction 
Evidence of gastrointestinal bleeding
The patient has bony lesions as the sole evaluable disease. 
Past [OR] or concurrent history of neoplasm other than stomach cancer, except for curatively treated [NOT] non-melanoma skin cancer [OR] or in situ carcinoma of the cervix uteri 
Pregnant [OR] or lactating women, [OR] women [AND] of childbearing potential [NOT] not employing adequate contraception 
Other serious illness [OR] or medical conditions 
Unstable cardiac disease [AND] despite treatment, myocardial infarction within 6 months prior to study entry 
History of significant neurologic [OR] or psychiatric disorders including dementia [OR] or seizures 
Active uncontrolled infection
Other serious underlying medical conditions which could impair the ability of the patient to participate in the study 
Concomitant administration of any other experimental drug under investigation, [OR] or concomitant chemotherapy, [OR] hormonal therapy, [OR] or immunotherapy 
concomitant drug medication; The following drugs cause drug interaction with S-1. 
i. Warfarin, [OR] phenprocoumon: increase bleeding tendency ii. Increase blood concentration of phenytoin iii. sorivudine: [NOT] inhibit DPD -> increase toxicity according to fluoropyrimidine iv. allopurinol : decrease activity of S-1
