Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nPatients who have taken either morphine with daily dose more than 120mg or Fentanyl with daily dose more than 50ug/hr \nPatients with significant abnormalities in hepatic or renal function which would, in the opinion of the investigator, prevent the patients involvement in the study \nPatients with significant clinical abnormalities in CNS, respiratory or cardiovascular function, which in the investigators judgement prevents participation in the study \nPatients who have taken antidepressants or anti-epileptic drugs, sedative hypnotics, selective serotonin reuptake inhibitor, short-acting analgesics, topical medications and anesthetics and/or muscle relaxants when taking Tramadol/Acetaminophen       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nPatients who have taken either morphine [AND] with daily dose more than 120mg [OR] or Fentanyl with daily dose more than 50ug/hr \nExclusion Criteria:\nPatients with significant abnormalities in hepatic [OR] or renal function which would, in the opinion of the investigator, [NOT] prevent the patients involvement in the study \nPatients with significant clinical abnormalities in CNS, [OR] respiratory [OR] or cardiovascular function, which in the investigators judgement [NOT] prevents participation in the study \nPatients who have taken antidepressants [OR] or anti-epileptic drugs, [OR] sedative hypnotics, [OR] selective serotonin reuptake inhibitor, [OR] short-acting analgesics, [OR] topical medications [OR] and anesthetics [OR] and/or muscle relaxants when taking Tramadol/ [OR] Acetaminophen<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Patients who have taken either morphine [AND] with daily dose more than 120mg [OR] or Fentanyl with daily dose more than 50ug/hr 
Exclusion Criteria:
Patients with significant abnormalities in hepatic [OR] or renal function which would, in the opinion of the investigator, [NOT] prevent the patients involvement in the study 
Patients with significant clinical abnormalities in CNS, [OR] respiratory [OR] or cardiovascular function, which in the investigators judgement [NOT] prevents participation in the study 
Patients who have taken antidepressants [OR] or anti-epileptic drugs, [OR] sedative hypnotics, [OR] selective serotonin reuptake inhibitor, [OR] short-acting analgesics, [OR] topical medications [OR] and anesthetics [OR] and/or muscle relaxants when taking Tramadol/ [OR] Acetaminophen
