Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nHLA-A2 melanoma patients with : \neither loco-regional or lymph node metastasis \ntransit nodules not surgically resectable \nmeasurable cutaneous or visceral metastasis \nPatients\' tumor express Melan-A/MART-1 antigen. \nNo chemotherapy treatment (except for Deticene used before the first T cell clones infusion) or radiotherapy or immunotherapy in the last 4 weeks before infusion. \nNo other melanoma treatment during the protocol. \nLife expectancy should be greater than 6 months. \nGeneral state with Karnowsky greater than 80, ECOG = 0, 1 or 2. \nPatient should be negative for HIV and B and C hepatitis. \nBiological parameters at the beginning of the study: leucocytes ³ 2000 elements per mm3, hemoglobin ³ 10.5g/dl, platelets ³ 100 000 per mm3, phosphatases alcalines transaminases £ 1 time 1/2 compared to the normal. \nSigned informed consent \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nHLA-A2 melanoma patients with : \neither loco-regional [OR] or lymph node metastasis \ntransit nodules [NOT] not surgically resectable \nmeasurable cutaneous [OR] or visceral metastasis \nPatients\' tumor express Melan-A/ [OR] MART-1 antigen. \n[NOT] No chemotherapy treatment (except for Deticene used before the first T cell clones infusion) [OR] or radiotherapy [OR] or immunotherapy in the last 4 weeks before infusion. \n [NOT] No other melanoma treatment during the protocol. \nLife expectancy should be greater than 6 months. \nGeneral state with Karnowsky greater than 80, ECOG = 0, 1 or 2. \nPatient should be negative for HIV [OR] and B [OR] and C hepatitis. \nBiological parameters at the beginning of the study: leucocytes ³ 2000 elements per mm3, hemoglobin ³ 10.5g/dl, platelets ³ 100 000 per mm3, phosphatases alcalines transaminases £ 1 time 1/2 compared to the normal. \nSigned informed consent<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
HLA-A2 melanoma patients with : 
either loco-regional [OR] or lymph node metastasis 
transit nodules [NOT] not surgically resectable 
measurable cutaneous [OR] or visceral metastasis 
Patients' tumor express Melan-A/ [OR] MART-1 antigen. 
[NOT] No chemotherapy treatment (except for Deticene used before the first T cell clones infusion) [OR] or radiotherapy [OR] or immunotherapy in the last 4 weeks before infusion. 
 [NOT] No other melanoma treatment during the protocol. 
Life expectancy should be greater than 6 months. 
General state with Karnowsky greater than 80, ECOG = 0, 1 or 2. 
Patient should be negative for HIV [OR] and B [OR] and C hepatitis. 
Biological parameters at the beginning of the study: leucocytes ³ 2000 elements per mm3, hemoglobin ³ 10.5g/dl, platelets ³ 100 000 per mm3, phosphatases alcalines transaminases £ 1 time 1/2 compared to the normal. 
Signed informed consent
