Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nNo positive HIV 1 or HIV 2 test at screening \nno history of significant skin disease such as, but not limited to rash or eruptions, drug allergies, food allergy, dermatitis, eczema, psoriasis, or urticaria \nno history of allergy to drugs such as, but not limited to, sulphonamides and penicillins \nno previously demonstrated clinically significant allergy or hypersensitivity to any of the excipients of the investigational medication administered in this trial \nno female subject of childbearing potential without use of effective nonhormonal birth control methods, or not willing to continue practicing these birth control methods for at least 30 days after the end of the treatment period \nno positive pregnancy test or breast feeding at screening       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nNo positive HIV 1 [OR] or HIV 2 test at screening \n [NOT] no history of significant skin disease such as, but not limited to rash [OR] or eruptions, drug allergies, [OR] food allergy, [OR] dermatitis, [OR] eczema, [OR] psoriasis, [OR] or urticaria \n [NOT] no history of allergy to drugs such as, but not limited to, sulphonamides [OR] and penicillins \n [NOT] no previously demonstrated clinically significant allergy [OR] or hypersensitivity to any of the excipients of the investigational medication administered in this trial \n [NOT] no female subject [AND] of childbearing potential [NOT] without use of effective [NOT] nonhormonal birth control methods, [OR] or [NOT] not willing to continue practicing these birth control methods for at least 30 days after the end of the treatment period \n [NOT] no positive pregnancy test [OR] or breast feeding at screening<|eot_id|>']
Response: No positive HIV 1 [OR] or HIV 2 test at screening 
 [NOT] no history of significant skin disease such as, but not limited to rash [OR] or eruptions, drug allergies, [OR] food allergy, [OR] dermatitis, [OR] eczema, [OR] psoriasis, [OR] or urticaria 
 [NOT] no history of allergy to drugs such as, but not limited to, sulphonamides [OR] and penicillins 
 [NOT] no previously demonstrated clinically significant allergy [OR] or hypersensitivity to any of the excipients of the investigational medication administered in this trial 
 [NOT] no female subject [AND] of childbearing potential [NOT] without use of effective [NOT] nonhormonal birth control methods, [OR] or [NOT] not willing to continue practicing these birth control methods for at least 30 days after the end of the treatment period 
 [NOT] no positive pregnancy test [OR] or breast feeding at screening
