mmunologic, dermatologic, neurologic, or psychiatric disease \nSubjects who have used any drugs or substances known to inhibit or induce cytochrome (CYP) P450 enzymes and/or P-glycoprotein (P-gp) within 28 days prior to the first dose and throughout the study \nDrug allergies to quinine sulfate or rosiglitazone       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nRecent participation (within 28 days) in other research studies \nRecent significant blood donation [OR] or plasma donation \nPregnant [OR] or lactating \nTest positive at screening for human immunodeficiency virus (HIV), [OR] hepatitis B surface antigen (HbsAg), [OR] or hepatitis C virus (HCV) \nRecent (2-year) history [OR] or evidence of alcoholism [OR] or drug abuse \nHistory [OR] or presence of significant cardiovascular, [OR] pulmonary, [OR] hepatic, [OR] gallbladder [OR] or biliary tract, renal, [OR] hematologic, [OR] gastrointestinal, [OR] endocrine, [OR] immunologic, [OR] dermatologic, [OR] neurologic, [OR] or psychiatric disease \nSubjects who have used any drugs [OR] or substances known to inhibit [OR] or induce cytochrome (CYP) P450 enzymes [OR] and/or P-glycoprotein (P-gp) within 28 days prior to the first dose and throughout the study \nDrug allergies to quinine sulfate [OR] or rosiglitazone<|eot_id|>']
Response: Recent participation (within 28 days) in other research studies 
Recent significant blood donation [OR] or plasma donation 
Pregnant [OR] or lactating 
Test positive at screening for human immunodeficiency virus (HIV), [OR] hepatitis B surface antigen (HbsAg), [OR] or hepatitis C virus (HCV) 
Recent (2-year) history [OR] or evidence of alcoholism [OR] or drug abuse 
