Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nCytologically proven acute lymphoblastic leukemia (ALL)\nNo relapse of a previously unrecognized ALL\nPatients must meet one of the following risk criteria:\nStandard-risk (SR) group meeting all of the following criteria:\nBlasts < 1,000/µL in peripheral blood (PB) on day 8\nAged 1 to < 6 years\nInitial WBC < 20,000/µL\nM1 (5%) or M2 (= 5% to < 25%) blasts in bone marrow on day 15;\nM1 marrow on day 33.\nAged < 1 or = 6 years and/or WBC = 20,000/µL\nBlasts < 1,000/µL in PB on day 8\nM1 or M2 marrow on day 15\nM3 (= 25%) marrow on day 15 OR meets SR criteria but M3 marrow on day 15 and *M1 marrow on day 33.\nMeets IR criteria and M3 marrow on day 15 (not SR and M3 on day 15)\nBlasts = 1,000/µL in PB on day 8\nM2 or M3 marrow on day 33\nTranslocation t(9;22) [BCR/ABL+] (Philadelphia chromosome-positive) or t(4;11) [MLL/AF4+].\n\n\n### Response:\nCytologically proven acute lymphoblastic leukemia (ALL)\n [NOT] No relapse of a previously unrecognized ALL\nPatients must meet one of the following risk criteria:\nStandard-risk (SR) group meeting all of the following criteria:\nBlasts < 1,000/µL in peripheral blood (PB) on day 8\nAged 1 to < 6 years\nInitial WBC < 20,000/µL\nM1 (5%) [OR] or M2 (= 5% to < 25%) blasts in bone marrow on day 15;\n M1 marrow on day 33.\nAged < 1 [OR] or = 6 years [OR] and/or WBC = 20,000/µL\nBlasts < 1,000/µL in PB on day 8\n M1 [OR] or M2 marrow on day 15\n M3 (= 25%) marrow on day 15 [OR] OR meets SR criteria [AND] but M3 marrow on day 15 [AND] and *M1 marrow on day 33.\nMeets IR criteria [AND] and M3 marrow on day 15 ([NOT] not SR [AND] and M3 on day 15)\nBlasts = 1,000/µL in PB on day 8\n M2 [OR] or M3 marrow on day 33\nTranslocation t(9;22) [BCR/ABL+] (Philadelphia chromosome-positive) [OR] or t(4;11) [MLL/AF4+].<|eot_id|>']
Response: Cytologically proven acute lymphoblastic leukemia (ALL)
 [NOT] No relapse of a previously unrecognized ALL
Patients must meet one of the following risk criteria:
Standard-risk (SR) group meeting all of the following criteria:
Blasts < 1,000/µL in peripheral blood (PB) on day 8
Aged 1 to < 6 years
Initial WBC < 20,000/µL
M1 (5%) [OR] or M2 (= 5% to < 25%) blasts in bone marrow on day 15;
 M1 marrow on day 33.
Aged < 1 [OR] or = 6 years [OR] and/or WBC = 20,000/µL
Blasts < 1,000/µL in PB on day 8
 M1 [OR] or M2 marrow on day 15
 M3 (= 25%) marrow on day 15 [OR] OR meets SR criteria [AND] but M3 marrow on day 15 [AND] and *M1 marrow on day 33.
Meets IR criteria [AND] and M3 marrow on day 15 ([NOT] not SR [AND] and M3 on day 15)
Blasts = 1,000/µL in PB on day 8
 M2 [OR] or M3 marrow on day 33
Translocation t(9;22) [BCR/ABL+] (Philadelphia chromosome-positive) [OR] or t(4;11) [MLL/AF4+].
