File: NCT00904202_inc 

Das File: /work/eauten2s/ec_criteria_struct/chia/input/chia_text_half/NCT00904202_inc.txt wurde erfolgreich geladen.
Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\n1. Had a diagnosis of PHN, DN, CRPS, carpal tunnel syndrome, HIV neuropathy, idiopathic sensory neuropathy, or other peripheral neuropathy (upon mutual agreement of the sponsor and investigator) \n2. Patients with PHN must have had pain >3 months after rash healing \n3. Patients with DN must have had Type I or II diabetes and painful distal symmetric sensorimotor polyneuropathy with or without dynamic allodynia of the lower extremities \n4. Patients with CRPS must have met current IASP (International Association for the Study of Pain) diagnostic criteria \n5. Patients with carpal tunnel syndrome must have had a diagnosis by combination clinical neurological examination (e.g., Phalen\'s and Tinel\'s signs), electrodiagnostic testing, and daily painful symptoms of at least 3 months\' duration \n6. Patients with HIV neuropathy must have had HIV, subjective symptoms of painful peripheral neuropathy, and daily painful symptoms of at least 3 months\' duration \n7. Patients with idiopathic sensory neuropathy must have had pain of at least 3 months\' duration \n8. Reached an average daily pain rating during the baseline week of pain ratings greater than 4 on the 0-to-10 numerical pain rating scale (Question 5 of the BPI) \n9. Had never received an analgesic regimen that contained lidocaine or gabapentin \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\n 1. Had a diagnosis of PHN, [OR] DN, [OR] CRPS, [OR] carpal tunnel syndrome, [OR] HIV neuropathy, [OR] idiopathic sensory neuropathy, or other peripheral neuropathy (upon mutual agreement of the sponsor and Investigator) \n 2. Patients with PHN must have had pain >3 months after rash healing \n 3. Patients with DN must have had Type I [OR] or II diabetes [AND] and painful distal symmetric sensorimotor polyneuropathy [AND] with or without dynamic allodynia of the lower extremities \n 4. Patients with CRPS must have met current IASP (International Association for the Study of Pain) diagnostic criteria \n 5. Patients with carpal tunnel syndrome must have had a diagnosis by combination clinical neurological examination (e.g., Phalen\'s [OR] and Tinel\'s signs), electrodiagnostic testing, [AND] and daily painful symptoms of at least 3 months\' duration \n 6. Patients with HIV neuropathy must have had HIV, subjective symptoms of painful peripheral neuropathy, [AND] and daily painful symptoms of at least 3 months\' duration \n 7. Patients with idiopathic sensory neuropathy must have had pain of at least 3 months\' duration \n 8. Reached an average daily pain rating during the baseline week of pain ratings greater than 4 on the 0-to-10 numerical pain rating scale (Question 5 of the BPI) \n 9. Had [NOT] never received an analgesic regimen that contained lidocaine [OR] or gabapentin<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
 1. Had a diagnosis of PHN, [OR] DN, [OR] CRPS, [OR] carpal tunnel syndrome, [OR] HIV neuropathy, [OR] idiopathic sensory neuropathy, or other peripheral neuropathy (upon mutual agreement of the sponsor and Investigator) 
 2. Patients with PHN must have had pain >3 months after rash healing 
 3. Patients with DN must have had Type I [OR] or II diabetes [AND] and painful distal symmetric sensorimotor polyneuropathy [AND] with or without dynamic allodynia of the lower extremities 
 4. Patients with CRPS must have met current IASP (International Association for the Study of Pain) diagnostic criteria 
 5. Patients with carpal tunnel syndrome must have had a diagnosis by combination clinical neurological examination (e.g., Phalen's [OR] and Tinel's signs), electrodiagnostic testing, [AND] and daily painful symptoms of at least 3 months' duration 
 6. Patients with HIV neuropathy must have had HIV, subjective symptoms of painful peripheral neuropathy, [AND] and daily painful symptoms of at least 3 months' duration 
 7. Patients with idiopathic sensory neuropathy must have had pain of at least 3 months' duration 
 8. Reached an average daily pain rating during the baseline week of pain ratings greater than 4 on the 0-to-10 numerical pain rating scale (Question 5 of the BPI) 
 9. Had [NOT] never received an analgesic regimen that contained lidocaine [OR] or gabapentin
