Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nMust be an outpatient with a primary DSM-IV Obsessive-Compulsive Disorder. Patients must have a score of greater than 20 on the Yale-Brown Obsessive Compulsive Scale (Y-BOCS; Goodman et al., 1989b).\nDiagnosis of comorbid DSM-IV major depressive episode will be allowed in the study provided that the diagnosis is secondary to OCD, they have a baseline Montgomery Depression Rating Scale (MADRS) score of less than or equal to 19, and the onset of OCD predates the onset of the current episode of depression by five or more years.\nThe ability to comprehend and comply with protocol requirements.\nWritten consent must be provided prior to study entry.\nAll women of childbearing potential (WOCBP) must be practicing a medically acceptable method of birth control\nAll female subjects of childbearing potential (WOCBP), including those who are practicing a medically acceptable method of birth control, must have a negative serum pregnancy test within 72 hours prior to the start of study medication.\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\n - Must be an outpatient [AND] with a primary DSM-IV Obsessive-Compulsive Disorder. Patients must have a score of greater than 20 on the Yale-Brown Obsessive Compulsive Scale (Y-BOCS; Goodman et al., 1989b).\n - Diagnosis of comorbid DSM-IV major depressive episode will be allowed in the study provided that the diagnosis is secondary to OCD, [AND] they have a baseline Montgomery Depression Rating Scale (MADRS) score of less than or equal to 19, [AND] and the onset of OCD predates the onset of the current episode of depression by five or more years.\n - The ability to comprehend and comply with protocol requirements.\n - Written consent must be provided prior to study entry.\n - All women of childbearing potential (WOCBP) must be practicing a medically acceptable method of birth control\n - All female subjects of childbearing potential (WOCBP), [AND] including those who are practicing a medically acceptable method of birth control, must have a negative serum pregnancy test within 72 hours prior to the start of study medication.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
 - Must be an outpatient [AND] with a primary DSM-IV Obsessive-Compulsive Disorder. Patients must have a score of greater than 20 on the Yale-Brown Obsessive Compulsive Scale (Y-BOCS; Goodman et al., 1989b).
 - Diagnosis of comorbid DSM-IV major depressive episode will be allowed in the study provided that the diagnosis is secondary to OCD, [AND] they have a baseline Montgomery Depression Rating Scale (MADRS) score of less than or equal to 19, [AND] and the onset of OCD predates the onset of the current episode of depression by five or more years.
 - The ability to comprehend and comply with protocol requirements.
 - Written consent must be provided prior to study entry.
 - All women of childbearing potential (WOCBP) must be practicing a medically acceptable method of birth control
 - All female subjects of childbearing potential (WOCBP), [AND] including those who are practicing a medically acceptable method of birth control, must have a negative serum pregnancy test within 72 hours prior to the start of study medication.
