Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nSubjects with hemoglobin SC or SB+ thalassemia \nSubjects on chronic transfusion program \nSubjects who have received RBC transfusions cannot have >15% adult hemoglobin \nKnown positive status for HIV, active hepatitis B or hepatitis C \nPregnant or breast feeding women \nIndividuals with a history of malignancy are ineligible except for the following circumstances. Individuals with a history of malignancy are eligible if they have been disease-free for at least 5 years and are deemed by the investigator to be at low risk for recurrence of that malignancy. Individuals with the following cancer are eligible if diagnosed and adequately treated within the past 5 years: cervical or breast cancer in situ, and basal cell or squamous cell carcinoma of the skin \nSubjects with a history of thrombosis or other reason (other than sickle cell disease) for enhanced thrombotic risk \nSubjects with unresolved infections \nSevere or uncontrolled medical conditions that could compromise study participation \nSubjects on fetal hemoglobin inducing agents \nSubjects on any other experimental treatment within 90 days of the first dose of study drug or who have not recovered from the side effects of such therapy \nKnown allergic reaction to a histone deacetylase inhibitor \nSubjects who have received valproic acid for treatment of epilepsy within 30 days of enrollment \nSubjects who have received any HDAC inhibitors other than valproic acid       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nSubjects with hemoglobin SC [OR] or SB+ thalassemia \nSubjects on chronic transfusion program \nSubjects who have received RBC transfusions [NOT] cannot have >15% adult hemoglobin \nKnown positive status for HIV, active hepatitis B [OR] or hepatitis C \nPregnant [OR] or breast feeding women \nIndividuals with a history of malignancy are ineligible except for the following circumstances. Individuals with a history of malignancy are eligible if they have been disease- [NOT] free for at least 5 years [AND] and are deemed by the investigator to be at low risk for recurrence of that malignancy. Individuals with the following cancer are eligible if diagnosed and adequately treated within the past 5 years: cervical [OR] or breast cancer in situ, [OR] and basal cell [OR] or squamous cell carcinoma of the skin \nSubjects with a history of thrombosis [OR] or other reason (other than sickle cell disease) for enhanced thrombotic risk \nSubjects with unresolved infections \nSevere [OR] or uncontrolled medical conditions that could compromise study participation \nSubjects on fetal hemoglobin inducing agents \nSubjects on any other experimental treatment within 90 days of the first dose of study drug [OR] or [NOT] who have [NOT] not recovered from the side effects of such therapy \nKnown allergic reaction to a histone deacetylase inhibitor \nSubjects [AND] who have received valproic acid [AND] for treatment of epilepsy within 30 days of enrollment\nSubjects [AND] who have received any HDAC inhibitors other than valproic acid<|eot_id|>']
Response: Subjects with hemoglobin SC [OR] or SB+ thalassemia 
Subjects on chronic transfusion program 
Subjects who have received RBC transfusions [NOT] cannot have >15% adult hemoglobin 
Known positive status for HIV, active hepatitis B [OR] or hepatitis C 
Pregnant [OR] or breast feeding women 
Individuals with a history of malignancy are ineligible except for the following circumstances. Individuals with a history of malignancy are eligible if they have been disease- [NOT] free for at least 5 years [AND] and are deemed by the investigator to be at low risk for recurrence of that malignancy. Individuals with the following cancer are eligible if diagnosed and adequately treated within the past 5 years: cervical [OR] or breast cancer in situ, [OR] and basal cell [OR] or squamous cell carcinoma of the skin 
Subjects with a history of thrombosis [OR] or other reason (other than sickle cell disease) for enhanced thrombotic risk 
Subjects with unresolved infections 
Severe [OR] or uncontrolled medical conditions that could compromise study participation 
Subjects on fetal hemoglobin inducing agents 
Subjects on any other experimental treatment within 90 days of the first dose of study drug [OR] or [NOT] who have [NOT] not recovered from the side effects of such therapy 
Known allergic reaction to a histone deacetylase inhibitor 
Subjects [AND] who have received valproic acid [AND] for treatment of epilepsy within 30 days of enrollment
Subjects [AND] who have received any HDAC inhibitors other than valproic acid
