ubclavian or distal) \nSubjects with non-functional CICC or PICC distal ports \nSubjects with femoral CICCs \nPregnant women       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nInability to obtain consent \nSubjects under 18 years of age \n[NOT] Non-English speaking subjects \nSubjects that are [NOT] unable to lay flat due to pulmonary complications, [OR] increased intracranial pressure (ICP), [OR] or unstable spinal cord injuries \nSubjects with known cardiac abnormalities (atrial septal defects [OR] or ventricular septal defects, severe tricuspid valve disease, severe pulmonary hypertension, [OR] Ejection fraction < 15%) \nPrisoners \nSubjects with known upper extremity deep vein thromboses (subclavian [OR] or distal) \nSubjects with [NOT] non-functional CICC [OR] or PICC distal ports \nSubjects with femoral CICCs \nPregnant women       \n<|eot_id|>']
