h Social Security \nPopulation Index related topics : \nThe presence of cycles until the age of 40 years with proven fertility, at least one child \nAmenorrhea and FSH> 30mUI/ml according to the criteria of the index subject \nMen of the family of index case \nPopulation control : \nWomen of Caucasian origin \nWomen who had regular cycles until at least age 40 and at least one child \nLack of land autoimmune (no history of thyroid disease or diabetes type 1) \nWoman signing the consent form for at least the blood sample \n\n\n### Response:\nPatients of familial cases of POF :\nFemale subjects between 16 and 40 years [OR] or women older than 40 years [AND] with a cessation of ovarian function before the age of 40 years [AND] with increased levels of FSH \nPrimary [OR] or secondary amenorrhea  for more than three months [AND] with LH [OR] and FSH> 30mUI/ml \n [NOT] No cases of fragile X syndrome [OR] in the family or blepharophimosis syndrome \nAt least two cases in the family\nOrigin Caucasian\nPatient signing the consent form for at least the blood sample\nPatient with Social Security\nPopulation Index related topics :\nThe presence of cycles until the age of 40 years [AND] with proven fertility, at least one child\nAmenorrhea [OR] and FSH> 30mUI/ml according to the criteria of the index subject\nMen of the family of index case\nPopulation control :\nWomen of Caucasian origin\nWomen [AND] who had regular cycles until at least age 40 [AND] and at least one child\nLack of land autoimmune ([NOT] no history of thyroid disease [OR] or diabetes type 1)\nWoman signing the consent form for at least the blood sample<|eot_id|>']
Response: Patients of familial cases of POF :
Female subjects between 16 and 40 years [OR] or women older than 40 years [AND] with a cessation of ovarian function before the age of 40 years [AND] with increased levels of FSH 
Primary [OR] or secondary amenorrhea  for more than three months [AND] with LH [OR] and FSH> 30mUI/ml 
 [NOT] No cases of fragile X syndrome [OR] in the family or blepharophimosis syndrome 
At least two cases in the family
Origin Caucasian
Patient signing the consent form for at least the blood sample
Patient with Social Security
Population Index related topics :
The presence of cycles until the age of 40 years [AND] with proven fertility, at least one child
Amenorrhea [OR] and FSH> 30mUI/ml according to the criteria of the index subject
Men of the family of index case
Population control :
Women of Caucasian origin
Women [AND] who had regular cycles until at least age 40 [AND] and at least one child
Lack of land autoimmune ([NOT] no history of thyroid disease [OR] or diabetes type 1)
Woman signing the consent form for at least the blood sample
