Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nDiabetes Mellitus\nAcute coronary syndrome in the past 6 months\nCardiac arrhythmias (2nd and 3rd degree heart block or premature ventricular complexes in Lown classes 4 or 5)\nSymptoms suggestive of obstructive or central sleep apnea (with a score of > 10 on Epworth sleepiness scale)\nPatients taking Clonidine\nBody mass index (BMI) > 34\nPatients unable to give consent\nPregnant women\nPatients with leg injury involving nerve damage\nPatients taking anticoagulant medication\nPatients with significant bleeding disorder or liver disorder\nHemoglobin <1.05 g/dl at the time of initiation of therapy\npatients with unilateral or bilateral nephrectomy\nPlanned kidney transplant in the next 4 months\nLife expectancy under 6 months\nOliguria (urine output less than 400 ml per day)\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nDiabetes Mellitus\nAcute coronary syndrome in the past 6 months\nCardiac arrhythmias (2nd and 3rd degree heart block [OR] or premature ventricular complexes in Lown classes 4 or 5)\nSymptoms suggestive of obstructive [OR] or central sleep apnea (with a score of > 10 on Epworth sleepiness scale)\nPatients taking Clonidine\nBody mass index (BMI) > 34\nPatients unable to give consent\nPregnant women\nPatients with leg injury involving nerve damage\nPatients taking anticoagulant medication\nPatients with significant bleeding disorder [OR] or liver disorder\nHemoglobin <1.05 g/dl at the time of initiation of therapy\npatients with unilateral [OR] or bilateral nephrectomy\nPlanned kidney transplant in the next 4 months\nLife expectancy under 6 months\nOliguria (urine output less than 400 ml per day)<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Diabetes Mellitus
Acute coronary syndrome in the past 6 months
Cardiac arrhythmias (2nd and 3rd degree heart block [OR] or premature ventricular complexes in Lown classes 4 or 5)
Symptoms suggestive of obstructive [OR] or central sleep apnea (with a score of > 10 on Epworth sleepiness scale)
Patients taking Clonidine
Body mass index (BMI) > 34
Patients unable to give consent
Pregnant women
Patients with leg injury involving nerve damage
Patients taking anticoagulant medication
Patients with significant bleeding disorder [OR] or liver disorder
Hemoglobin <1.05 g/dl at the time of initiation of therapy
patients with unilateral [OR] or bilateral nephrectomy
Planned kidney transplant in the next 4 months
Life expectancy under 6 months
Oliguria (urine output less than 400 ml per day)
