Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nPregnancy: Women who are pregnant or lactating. \nAsthma: Subjects with a current diagnosis of asthma. (Subjects with a prior history of asthma are eligible if they also have a current diagnosis of COPD). \nalpha 1-antitrypsin deficiency: Subjects with known alpha-1 antitrypsin deficiency as the underlying cause of COPD. \nOther respiratory disorders: Subjects with active tuberculosis, lung cancer, bronchiectasis, sarcoidosis, pulmonary fibrosis, pulmonary hypertension, interstitial lung diseases or other active pulmonary diseases. \nLung resection or transplantation: Subjects with lung volume reduction surgery within the 12 months prior to Screening or having had a lung transplant. \nA moderate/severe COPD exacerbation that has not resolved at least 14 days prior to Visit 1 and at least 30 days following the last dose of oral corticosteroids (if applicable). \nCurrent severe heart failure (New York Heart Association class IV). Subjects will also be excluded if they have a known ejection fraction of <30% or if they have an implantable cardioverter defibrillator (ICD). \nOther diseases/abnormalities: Any life-threatening condition with life expectancy <3 years, other than vascular disease or COPD, that might prevent the subject from completing the study. \nEnd stage chronic renal disease: Subjects will be excluded if on renal replacement therapy (hemodialysis or peritoneal). \nDrug/food allergy: Subjects with a history of hypersensitivity to any of the study medications (e.g. beta-agonists, corticosteroid) or components of the inhalation powder (e.g. lactose, magnesium stearate). In addition, patients with a history of severe milk protein allergy that, in the opinion of the study physician, contraindicates the subject\'s participation will also be excluded. \nDrug/alcohol abuse: Subjects with a known or suspected history of alcohol or drug abuse within the last 2 years. \nOxygen therapy: Subjects receiving treatment with long-term oxygen therapy (LTOT) or nocturnal oxygen therapy required for greater than 12 hours a day. Oxygen prn use (i.e. <=12 hours per day) is not exclusionary. \nQuestionable validity of consent: Subjects with a history of psychiatric disease, intellectual deficiency, poor motivation or other conditions that will limit the validity of informed consent to participate in the study or the potential compliance to study procedures. \nAffiliation with investigator site: Study investigators, sub-investigators, study coordinators, employees of a participating investigator or immediate family members of the aforementioned are excluded from participating in this study. \nAdditional medication: Use of the following medications within the following time intervals prior to Visit 1 or during the study (unless otherwise specified): \nMedication No use within the following time intervals prior to Screening or thereafter at any time during the study (unless otherwise specified) Inhaled Long acting beta-agonists (LABA) 48 hours ICS/LABA combination products 48 hours Inhaled corticosteroids 48 hours Tiotropium 1 week Systemic, Oral, parenteral, intra-articular corticosteroids 30 days (oral and systemic corticosteroids may be used to treat COPD exacerbations during the study) Cytochrome P450 3A4 strong inhibitors including but not limited to antiretrovirals (protease inhibitors) (e.g.Indinavir, Nelfinavir, Ritonavir, Saquinavir); Imidazole and Triazole anti-fungals (e.g. Ketaconazole, Itraconazole); Clarithromycin, Telithromycin, Amiodarone, and Nefazodone 6 weeks Grapefruit is allowed up to Visit 1, then limited to no more than one glass of grapefruit juice (250 mL/ 8 ounces) or one grapefruit per day Any other investigational drug 30 days or 5 half lives whichever is longer.       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nPregnancy: Women [AND] who are pregnant [OR] or lactating. \nAsthma: Subjects with a current diagnosis of asthma. (Subjects with a prior history of asthma [AND] are eligible if they also have a current diagnosis of COPD). \nalpha 1-antitrypsin deficiency: Subjects with known alpha-1 antitrypsin deficiency as the underlying cause of COPD. \nOther respiratory disorders: Subjects with active tuberculosis, [OR] lung cancer, [OR] bronchiectasis, [OR] sarcoidosis, [OR] pulmonary fibrosis, [OR] pulmonary hypertension, [OR] interstitial lung diseases [OR] or other active pulmonary diseases. \nLung resection [OR] or transplantation: Subjects with lung volume reduction surgery within the 12 months prior to Screening [OR] or having had a lung transplant. \nA moderate/ [OR] severe COPD exacerbation [AND] that has [NOT] not resolved at least 14 days prior to Visit 1 [AND] and at least 30 days following the last dose of oral corticosteroids (if applicable). \nCurrent severe heart failure (New York Heart Association class IV). Subjects will also be [NOT] excluded if they have a known ejection fraction of <30% [OR] or if they have an implantable cardioverter defibrillator (ICD). \nOther diseases/ [OR] abnormalities: Any life-threatening condition [AND] with life expectancy <3 years, other than vascular disease [OR] or COPD, that might [NOT] prevent the subject from completing the study. \nEnd stage chronic renal disease: Subjects will be [NOT] excluded if on renal replacement therapy (hemodialysis [OR] or peritoneal). \nDrug/ [OR] food allergy: Subjects with a history of hypersensitivity to any of the study medications (e.g. beta-agonists, [OR] corticosteroid) [OR] or components of the inhalation powder (e.g. lactose, [OR] magnesium stearate). In addition, patients with a history of severe milk protein allergy that, in the opinion of the study physician, contraindicates the subject\'s participation will also be [NOT] excluded. \nDrug/ [OR] alcohol abuse: Subjects with a known [OR] or suspected history of alcohol [OR] or drug abuse within the last 2 years. \nOxygen therapy: Subjects receiving treatment with long-term oxygen therapy (LTOT) [OR] or nocturnal oxygen therapy required for greater than 12 hours a day. Oxygen prn use (i.e. <=12 hours per day) is [NOT] not exclusionary. \nQuestionable validity of consent: Subjects with a history of psychiatric disease, [OR] intellectual deficiency, [OR] poor motivation [OR] or other conditions that will [NOT] limit the validity of informed consent to participate in the study or the potential compliance to study procedures. \nAffiliation with investigator site: Study investigators, sub-investigators, study coordinators, employees of a participating investigator or immediate family members of the aforementioned are [NOT] excluded from participating in this study. \nAdditional medication: Use of the following medications within the following time intervals prior to Visit 1 [OR] or during the study (unless otherwise specified): \nMedication [NOT] No use within the following time intervals prior to Screening [OR] or thereafter at any time during the study (unless otherwise specified) Inhaled Long acting beta-agonists (LABA) 48 hours ICS/ [OR] LABA combination products 48 hours Inhaled corticosteroids 48 hours Tiotropium 1 week Systemic, [OR] Oral, [OR] parenteral, [OR] intra-articular corticosteroids 30 days (oral [OR] and systemic corticosteroids may be used to treat COPD exacerbations during the study) Cytochrome P450 3A4 strong inhibitors including but not limited to antiretrovirals (protease inhibitors) (e.g.Indinavir, [OR] Nelfinavir, [OR] Ritonavir, [OR] Saquinavir); Imidazole [OR] and Triazole anti-fungals (e.g. Ketaconazole, [OR] Itraconazole); Clarithromycin, [OR] Telithromycin, [OR] Amiodarone, [OR] and Nefazodone 6 weeks Grapefruit is allowed up to Visit 1, then limited to [NOT] no more than one glass of grapefruit juice (250 mL/ 8 ounces) [OR] or one grapefruit per day Any other investigational drug 30 days [OR] or 5 half lives whichever is longer.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Pregnancy: Women [AND] who are pregnant [OR] or lactating. 
Asthma: Subjects with a current diagnosis of asthma. (Subjects with a prior history of asthma [AND] are eligible if they also have a current diagnosis of COPD). 
alpha 1-antitrypsin deficiency: Subjects with known alpha-1 antitrypsin deficiency as the underlying cause of COPD. 
Other respiratory disorders: Subjects with active tuberculosis, [OR] lung cancer, [OR] bronchiectasis, [OR] sarcoidosis, [OR] pulmonary fibrosis, [OR] pulmonary hypertension, [OR] interstitial lung diseases [OR] or other active pulmonary diseases. 
Lung resection [OR] or transplantation: Subjects with lung volume reduction surgery within the 12 months prior to Screening [OR] or having had a lung transplant. 
A moderate/ [OR] severe COPD exacerbation [AND] that has [NOT] not resolved at least 14 days prior to Visit 1 [AND] and at least 30 days following the last dose of oral corticosteroids (if applicable). 
Current severe heart failure (New York Heart Association class IV). Subjects will also be [NOT] excluded if they have a known ejection fraction of <30% [OR] or if they have an implantable cardioverter defibrillator (ICD). 
Other diseases/ [OR] abnormalities: Any life-threatening condition [AND] with life expectancy <3 years, other than vascular disease [OR] or COPD, that might [NOT] prevent the subject from completing the study. 
End stage chronic renal disease: Subjects will be [NOT] excluded if on renal replacement therapy (hemodialysis [OR] or peritoneal). 
Drug/ [OR] food allergy: Subjects with a history of hypersensitivity to any of the study medications (e.g. beta-agonists, [OR] corticosteroid) [OR] or components of the inhalation powder (e.g. lactose, [OR] magnesium stearate). In addition, patients with a history of severe milk protein allergy that, in the opinion of the study physician, contraindicates the subject's participation will also be [NOT] excluded. 
Drug/ [OR] alcohol abuse: Subjects with a known [OR] or suspected history of alcohol [OR] or drug abuse within the last 2 years. 
Oxygen therapy: Subjects receiving treatment with long-term oxygen therapy (LTOT) [OR] or nocturnal oxygen therapy required for greater than 12 hours a day. Oxygen prn use (i.e. <=12 hours per day) is [NOT] not exclusionary. 
Questionable validity of consent: Subjects with a history of psychiatric disease, [OR] intellectual deficiency, [OR] poor motivation [OR] or other conditions that will [NOT] limit the validity of informed consent to participate in the study or the potential compliance to study procedures. 
Affiliation with investigator site: Study investigators, sub-investigators, study coordinators, employees of a participating investigator or immediate family members of the aforementioned are [NOT] excluded from participating in this study. 
Additional medication: Use of the following medications within the following time intervals prior to Visit 1 [OR] or during the study (unless otherwise specified): 
Medication [NOT] No use within the following time intervals prior to Screening [OR] or thereafter at any time during the study (unless otherwise specified) Inhaled Long acting beta-agonists (LABA) 48 hours ICS/ [OR] LABA combination products 48 hours Inhaled corticosteroids 48 hours Tiotropium 1 week Systemic, [OR] Oral, [OR] parenteral, [OR] intra-articular corticosteroids 30 days (oral [OR] and systemic corticosteroids may be used to treat COPD exacerbations during the study) Cytochrome P450 3A4 strong inhibitors including but not limited to antiretrovirals (protease inhibitors) (e.g.Indinavir, [OR] Nelfinavir, [OR] Ritonavir, [OR] Saquinavir); Imidazole [OR] and Triazole anti-fungals (e.g. Ketaconazole, [OR] Itraconazole); Clarithromycin, [OR] Telithromycin, [OR] Amiodarone, [OR] and Nefazodone 6 weeks Grapefruit is allowed up to Visit 1, then limited to [NOT] no more than one glass of grapefruit juice (250 mL/ 8 ounces) [OR] or one grapefruit per day Any other investigational drug 30 days [OR] or 5 half lives whichever is longer.
