r chronic atopic dermatitis within one month \nCurrent use of active topical medication in the planned investigational area for chronic atopic dermatitis within two weeks \nHistory of a sunny holiday, UV-light therapy or solarium use within one month before beginning of study treatments, or planning such during the study or within 7 days after the study \nAllergy to cis-UCA, or any constituents of the placebo emulsion cream or any constituents of Protopic® ointment \nHistory of any skin-related cancer \nCongenital or acquired immunodeficiency or ongoing therapy that cause immunosuppression \nEarlier participation in a clinical study performed with cis-UCA \nAny clinically significant laboratory test result \nSuspected current drug or alcohol abuse \nClinically significant illness during the 4 weeks prior to the first dose administration \nAny other condition that in the opinion of the Investigator would interfere with the evaluation of the study results or constitute a health hazard for the patient \nUnwillingness or doubtful capacity to comply with the protocol \nDoubtful availability to complete the study       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nHistory of other significant skin disease, [OR] or skin manifestations of allergic illness [OR] or other dermatologic condition, except chronic moderate [OR] or severe atopic dermatitis, that would interfere with the trial assessments [OR] or compromise the patient\'s safety according to the opinion of the Investigator \nPresent symptoms of other skin diseases, except chronic atopic dermatitis, that could disturb the study assessment [OR] and evaluation of the skin \nCurrent use of any active systemic medication [OR] for chronic atopic dermatitis within one month \nCurrent use of active topical medication [OR] in the planned investigational area for chronic atopic dermatitis within two weeks \nHistory of a sunny holiday, [OR] UV-light therapy [OR] or solarium use within one month before beginning of study treatments, [OR] or planning such during the study [OR] or within 7 days after the study \nAllergy to cis-UCA, [OR] or any constituents of the placebo emulsion cream [OR] or any constituents of Protopic® ointment \nHistory of any skin-related cancer \nCongenital [OR] or acquired immunodeficiency [OR] or ongoing therapy that cause immunosuppression \nEarlier participation in a clinical study performed with cis-UCA \nAny clinically significant laboratory test result \nSuspected current drug [OR] or alcohol abuse \nClinically significant illness during the 4 weeks prior to the first dose administration \nAny other condition that in the opinion of the Investigator would interfere with the evaluation of the study results [OR] or constitute a health hazard for the patient \nUnwillingness [OR] or doubtful capacity to comply with the protocol \nDoubtful availability to complete the study<|eot_id|>']
Response: History of other significant skin disease, [OR] or skin manifestations of allergic illness [OR] or other dermatologic condition, except chronic moderate [OR] or severe atopic dermatitis, that would interfere with the trial assessments [OR] or compromise the patient's safety according to the opinion of the Investigator 
Present symptoms of other skin diseases, except chronic atopic dermatitis, that could disturb the study assessment [OR] and evaluation of the skin 
Current use of any active systemic medication [OR] for chronic atopic dermatitis within one month 
Current use of active topical medication [OR] in the planned investigational area for chronic atopic dermatitis within two weeks 
History of a sunny holiday, [OR] UV-light therapy [OR] or solarium use within one month before beginning of study treatments, [OR] or planning such during the study [OR] or within 7 days after the study 
Allergy to cis-UCA, [OR] or any constituents of the placebo emulsion cream [OR] or any constituents of Protopic® ointment 
History of any skin-related cancer 
Congenital [OR] or acquired immunodeficiency [OR] or ongoing therapy that cause immunosuppression 
Earlier participation in a clinical study performed with cis-UCA 
Any clinically significant laboratory test result 
Suspected current drug [OR] or alcohol abuse 
Clinically significant illness during the 4 weeks prior to the first dose administration 
Any other condition that in the opinion of the Investigator would interfere with the evaluation of the study results [OR] or constitute a health hazard for the patient 
Unwillingness [OR] or doubtful capacity to comply with the protocol 
Doubtful availability to complete the study
