Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInformed consent obtained prior to any screening procedure \nCaucasian male or female patient \nAt least 18 years of age \nWeight at least 45 kg \nPatient with moderate or severe chronic atopic dermatitis \nGood general health ascertained by medical history, physical examination and laboratory determinations, showing no signs of clinically significant findings, except chronic atopic dermatitis \nNegative pregnancy test (premenopausal female patient) at screening and use of adequate contraceptive measures (both male and female patients) throughout the study and 30 days after the last cis-UCA dose \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nInformed consent obtained prior to any screening procedure \nCaucasian male [OR] or female patient \nAt least 18 years of age \nWeight at least 45 kg \nPatient with moderate [OR] or severe chronic atopic dermatitis \nGood general health ascertained by medical history, physical examination [AND] and laboratory determinations, showing [NOT] no signs of clinically significant findings, except chronic atopic dermatitis \nNegative pregnancy test (premenopausal female patient) at screening [AND] and use of adequate contraceptive measures (both male [OR] and female patients) throughout the study [AND] and 30 days after the last cis-UCA dose<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Informed consent obtained prior to any screening procedure 
Caucasian male [OR] or female patient 
At least 18 years of age 
Weight at least 45 kg 
Patient with moderate [OR] or severe chronic atopic dermatitis 
Good general health ascertained by medical history, physical examination [AND] and laboratory determinations, showing [NOT] no signs of clinically significant findings, except chronic atopic dermatitis 
Negative pregnancy test (premenopausal female patient) at screening [AND] and use of adequate contraceptive measures (both male [OR] and female patients) throughout the study [AND] and 30 days after the last cis-UCA dose
