Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nCurrent pregnancy or lactation \nLiver disease or elevated liver enzymes \nEstablished diagnosis of diabetes mellitus \nAbnormal serum glucose levels either at fasting or after the 2-hr oral glucose tolerance test meeting criteria for the diagnosis of diabetes mellitus according to the American Diabetes Association. \nInsulin sensitizing treatment within 3 months prior to or during the eight week study period. \nHormonal treatment involving estrogen or progesterone 3 months prior to or during the study period, with the exception of medroxyprogesterone acetate for withdrawal bleeding. \nSystemic or inhaled corticosteroids. \nKnown hypersensitive reaction to cinnamon. \nPatients with seizure disorders, known cardiovascular disease, or cerebrovascular disease. \nBody mass index (BMI)range 20-50 (excluding all women with BMI under 20 or over 50).       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nCurrent pregnancy [OR] or lactation \nLiver disease [OR] or elevated liver enzymes \n Established diagnosis of diabetes mellitus \nAbnormal serum glucose levels either at fasting [OR] or after the 2-hr oral glucose tolerance test meeting criteria for the diagnosis of diabetes mellitus according to the American Diabetes Association. \nInsulin sensitizing treatment within 3 months prior to or during the eight week study period. \nHormonal treatment involving estrogen [OR] or progesterone 3 months prior to or during the study period, with the exception of medroxyprogesterone acetate for withdrawal bleeding. \nSystemic [OR] or inhaled corticosteroids. \nKnown hypersensitive reaction to cinnamon. \nPatients with seizure disorders, known cardiovascular disease, [OR] or cerebrovascular disease. \nBody mass index (BMI)range 20-50 (excluding all women [AND] with BMI under 20 [OR] or over 50).<|eot_id|>']
Response: Current pregnancy [OR] or lactation 
Liver disease [OR] or elevated liver enzymes 
 Established diagnosis of diabetes mellitus 
Abnormal serum glucose levels either at fasting [OR] or after the 2-hr oral glucose tolerance test meeting criteria for the diagnosis of diabetes mellitus according to the American Diabetes Association. 
Insulin sensitizing treatment within 3 months prior to or during the eight week study period. 
Hormonal treatment involving estrogen [OR] or progesterone 3 months prior to or during the study period, with the exception of medroxyprogesterone acetate for withdrawal bleeding. 
Systemic [OR] or inhaled corticosteroids. 
Known hypersensitive reaction to cinnamon. 
Patients with seizure disorders, known cardiovascular disease, [OR] or cerebrovascular disease. 
Body mass index (BMI)range 20-50 (excluding all women [AND] with BMI under 20 [OR] or over 50).
