 years of age \nAbility to understand and willingness to comply with the study protocol \nWritten informed consent \nPatients meeting the Rotterdam PCOS workshop criteria for polycystic ovary syndrome, defined by oligomenorrhea [OR] or amenorrhea [AND] and at least one of the following two signs: clinical [OR] or biochemical evidence of hyperandrogenism [OR] or ultrasound finding of polycystic appearing ovaries.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Patients aged greater than 18 years of age 
Ability to understand and willingness to comply with the study protocol 
Written informed consent 
Patients meeting the Rotterdam PCOS workshop criteria for polycystic ovary syndrome, defined by oligomenorrhea [OR] or amenorrhea [AND] and at least one of the following two signs: clinical [OR] or biochemical evidence of hyperandrogenism [OR] or ultrasound finding of polycystic appearing ovaries.
