Das File: /work/eauten2s/ec_criteria_struct/chia/input/chia_text_half/NCT01518946_exc.txt wurde erfolgreich geladen.
Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\n1. The subject is a pregnant or lactating female. \n2. The subject has pre-existing sustained supine hypertension greater than 180mmHg systolic and 110mmHg diastolic BP or had these measurements at the Screening Visit. Sustained is defined as persistently greater at 2 separate measurements at least 5 minutes apart with the subject supine and at rest for the 5 minutes. \n3. Subjects taking concomitant medications of interest are excluded unless those medications are reviewed and discussed with the Medical Monitor or Study Physician and documented prior to enrolling the subject. If agreement is reached between the Investigator and Sponsor for the subject to continue in the study, all allowed medications should be maintained at a constant dose throughout the study. \n4. The Principal Investigator deems any clinical laboratory test (at the Screening Visit) abnormality to be clinically significant \n5. The subject has participated in other studies of investigational drugs or devices within 30 days prior to enrollment in this study (other than Study SPD426-406). \n6. Current or relevant history of physical or psychiatric illness, any medical disorder that may require treatment or make the subject unlikely to fully comply with the requirements of the study or complete the study, or any condition that presents undue risk from the investigational product or study procedures. \n7. The subject has a concurrent chronic or acute illness, disability, or other condition (including significant unexpected laboratory or electrocardiogram [ECG] findings) that might confound the results of the tests and/or measurements administered in this study, or that might have increased the risk to the subject. \n8. Known or suspected intolerance or hypersensitivity to the investigational product(s), closely-related compounds, or any of the stated ingredients. \n9. Prior enrollment failure or randomization in this study. \n10. History of alcohol abuse or other substance abuse within the last year.       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\n1. The subject is a pregnant [OR] or lactating female. \n2. The subject has pre-existing sustained supine hypertension greater than 180mmHg systolic [OR] and 110mmHg diastolic BP [OR] or had these measurements at the Screening Visit. Sustained is defined as persistently greater at 2 separate measurements at least 5 minutes apart [AND] with the subject supine [AND] and at rest for the 5 minutes. \n3. Subjects taking concomitant medications of interest are [NOT] excluded unless those medications are reviewed and discussed with the Medical Monitor [OR] or Study Physician and documented prior to enrolling the subject. If agreement is reached between the Investigator and Sponsor for the subject to continue in the study, all allowed medications should be maintained at a constant dose throughout the study. \n4. The Principal Investigator deems any clinical laboratory test (at the Screening Visit) abnormality to be clinically significant \n5. The subject has participated in other studies of investigational drugs [OR] or devices within 30 days prior to enrollment in this study (other than Study SPD426-406). \n6. Current [OR] or relevant history of physical [OR] or psychiatric illness, any medical disorder that may require treatment [OR] or make the subject unlikely to fully comply with the requirements of the study [OR] or complete the study, [OR] or any condition that presents undue risk from the investigational product [OR] or study procedures. \n7. The subject has a concurrent chronic [OR] or acute illness, [OR] disability, [OR] or other condition (including significant unexpected laboratory [OR] or electrocardiogram [ECG] findings) that might confound the results of the tests [OR] and/or measurements administered in this study, [OR] or that might have increased the risk to the subject. \n8. Known [OR] or suspected intolerance [OR] or hypersensitivity to the investigational product(s), closely-related compounds, [OR] or any of the stated ingredients. \n9. Prior enrollment failure [OR] or randomization in this study. \n10. History of alcohol abuse [OR] or other substance abuse within the last year.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
1. The subject is a pregnant [OR] or lactating female. 
2. The subject has pre-existing sustained supine hypertension greater than 180mmHg systolic [OR] and 110mmHg diastolic BP [OR] or had these measurements at the Screening Visit. Sustained is defined as persistently greater at 2 separate measurements at least 5 minutes apart [AND] with the subject supine [AND] and at rest for the 5 minutes. 
3. Subjects taking concomitant medications of interest are [NOT] excluded unless those medications are reviewed and discussed with the Medical Monitor [OR] or Study Physician and documented prior to enrolling the subject. If agreement is reached between the Investigator and Sponsor for the subject to continue in the study, all allowed medications should be maintained at a constant dose throughout the study. 
4. The Principal Investigator deems any clinical laboratory test (at the Screening Visit) abnormality to be clinically significant 
5. The subject has participated in other studies of investigational drugs [OR] or devices within 30 days prior to enrollment in this study (other than Study SPD426-406). 
6. Current [OR] or relevant history of physical [OR] or psychiatric illness, any medical disorder that may require treatment [OR] or make the subject unlikely to fully comply with the requirements of the study [OR] or complete the study, [OR] or any condition that presents undue risk from the investigational product [OR] or study procedures. 
7. The subject has a concurrent chronic [OR] or acute illness, [OR] disability, [OR] or other condition (including significant unexpected laboratory [OR] or electrocardiogram [ECG] findings) that might confound the results of the tests [OR] and/or measurements administered in this study, [OR] or that might have increased the risk to the subject. 
8. Known [OR] or suspected intolerance [OR] or hypersensitivity to the investigational product(s), closely-related compounds, [OR] or any of the stated ingredients. 
9. Prior enrollment failure [OR] or randomization in this study. 
10. History of alcohol abuse [OR] or other substance abuse within the last year.
