File: NCT01700790_inc 

Das File: /work/eauten2s/ec_criteria_struct/chia/input/chia_text_half/NCT01700790_inc.txt wurde erfolgreich geladen.
Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nAntiretroviral naive\nTaking Kaletra containing regimen with suppressed viral load.\nTaking an NNRTI or integrase containing regimen without prior history of use of PI for more than 2 weeks\nTaking an NNRTI or integrase containing regimen with prior exposure to PI greater than 2 weeks. It must be clearly stated in the source document that PI was switched to another agent for convenience.\nTaking another PI containing regimens with suppressed viral load. It must be clearly stated in source document that if another PI was used for greater than 2 weeks the regimen was switched to another agent for convenience. Subjects with prior history of PI use may be enrolled, if there is a genotype showing no resistance to Kaletra Other Inclusion criteria\nBe at least 18 years of age and able to give informed consent.\nDiagnosed with TB by criteria per Brazilian Ministry of Health\nHave a good clinical response to TB.\nTolerating tuberculosis therapy containing rifampin for the 2 weeks prior to screening,except for persons taking protease inhibitors at time of diagnosis of TB.,. Subjects taking protease inhibitors will be screened and initiate visit 1 within 3 days of starting TB medication\nHIV positive with documentation present in source document.\nHave a CD4 cell count greater than 50 cells/mm3if not taking ART. Persons with cd4 < 50 may be enrolled, if it is felt that in the best interest of the patient, that enrollment in the study will allow for quicker initiation of antiretroviral therapy than referral to another treatment center.\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nAntiretroviral naive\nTaking Kaletra containing regimen [AND] with suppressed viral load.\nTaking an NNRTI [OR] or integrase containing regimen [NOT] without prior history of use of PI for more than 2 weeks\nTaking an NNRTI [OR] or integrase containing regimen [AND] with prior exposure to PI greater than 2 weeks. It must be clearly stated in the source document that PI was switched to another agent for convenience.\nTaking another PI containing regimens [AND] with suppressed viral load. It must be clearly stated in source document that if another PI was used for greater than 2 weeks the regimen was switched to another agent for convenience. Subjects with prior history of PI use may be enrolled, if there is a genotype showing [NOT] no resistance to Kaletra Other Inclusion criteria\nBe at least 18 years of age and able to give informed consent.\nDiagnosed with TB by criteria per Brazilian Ministry of Health\nHave a good clinical response to TB.\nTolerating tuberculosis therapy containing rifampin for the 2 weeks prior to screening,except for persons taking protease inhibitors at time of diagnosis of TB.,. Subjects taking protease inhibitors will be screened and initiate visit 1 within 3 days of starting TB medication\nHIV positive with documentation present in source document.\nHave a CD4 cell count greater than 50 cells/mm3if [NOT] not taking ART. Persons with cd4 < 50 may be enrolled, if it is felt that in the best interest of the patient, that enrollment in the study will allow for quicker initiation of antiretroviral therapy than referral to another treatment center.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Antiretroviral naive
Taking Kaletra containing regimen [AND] with suppressed viral load.
Taking an NNRTI [OR] or integrase containing regimen [NOT] without prior history of use of PI for more than 2 weeks
Taking an NNRTI [OR] or integrase containing regimen [AND] with prior exposure to PI greater than 2 weeks. It must be clearly stated in the source document that PI was switched to another agent for convenience.
Taking another PI containing regimens [AND] with suppressed viral load. It must be clearly stated in source document that if another PI was used for greater than 2 weeks the regimen was switched to another agent for convenience. Subjects with prior history of PI use may be enrolled, if there is a genotype showing [NOT] no resistance to Kaletra Other Inclusion criteria
Be at least 18 years of age and able to give informed consent.
Diagnosed with TB by criteria per Brazilian Ministry of Health
Have a good clinical response to TB.
Tolerating tuberculosis therapy containing rifampin for the 2 weeks prior to screening,except for persons taking protease inhibitors at time of diagnosis of TB.,. Subjects taking protease inhibitors will be screened and initiate visit 1 within 3 days of starting TB medication
HIV positive with documentation present in source document.
Have a CD4 cell count greater than 50 cells/mm3if [NOT] not taking ART. Persons with cd4 < 50 may be enrolled, if it is felt that in the best interest of the patient, that enrollment in the study will allow for quicker initiation of antiretroviral therapy than referral to another treatment center.
