Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\n1. For subjects in Cohort A: previous therapy for more than 48 hours with any parenteral antibiotic with activity against S. aureus within 72 hours of positive blood culture results. \n2. For subjects in Cohort B: previous therapy for more than 48 hours with any parenteral antibiotic with activity against MRSA, except vancomycin and/or daptomycin, within 72 hours of positive blood culture results confirming persistence. \n3. Previous episode of S. aureus bacteremia within 3 months. \n4. Known left-sided endocarditis or prosthetic heart valve. \n5. Osteomyelitis or prosthetic joint infection except new onset nonhardware-associated vertebral osteomyelitis. \n6. History of any hypersensitivity or allergic reaction to any β-lactam antibacterial agent. \n7. Evidence of significant hepatic, hematologic, or immunologic impairment. \n8. Pregnant or nursing females.       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\n 1. For subjects in Cohort A: previous therapy for more than 48 hours with any parenteral antibiotic [AND] with activity against S. aureus within 72 hours of positive blood culture results. \n 2. For subjects in Cohort B: previous therapy for more than 48 hours with any parenteral antibiotic [AND] with activity against MRSA, except vancomycin [OR] and/or daptomycin, within 72 hours of positive blood culture results confirming persistence. \n 3. Previous episode of S. aureus bacteremia within 3 months. \n 4. Known left-sided endocarditis [OR] or prosthetic heart valve. \n 5. Osteomyelitis [OR] or prosthetic joint infection except new onset [NOT] nonhardware-associated vertebral osteomyelitis. \n 6. History of any hypersensitivity [OR] or allergic reaction to any β-lactam antibacterial agent. \n 7. Evidence of significant hepatic, [OR] hematologic, [OR] or immunologic impairment. \n 8. Pregnant [OR] or nursing females.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
 1. For subjects in Cohort A: previous therapy for more than 48 hours with any parenteral antibiotic [AND] with activity against S. aureus within 72 hours of positive blood culture results. 
 2. For subjects in Cohort B: previous therapy for more than 48 hours with any parenteral antibiotic [AND] with activity against MRSA, except vancomycin [OR] and/or daptomycin, within 72 hours of positive blood culture results confirming persistence. 
 3. Previous episode of S. aureus bacteremia within 3 months. 
 4. Known left-sided endocarditis [OR] or prosthetic heart valve. 
 5. Osteomyelitis [OR] or prosthetic joint infection except new onset [NOT] nonhardware-associated vertebral osteomyelitis. 
 6. History of any hypersensitivity [OR] or allergic reaction to any β-lactam antibacterial agent. 
 7. Evidence of significant hepatic, [OR] hematologic, [OR] or immunologic impairment. 
 8. Pregnant [OR] or nursing females.
