er the last dose of study drug. \n4. Expectation of survival for at least 2 months. \n\n\n### Response:\n1. Presence of bacteremia due solely to: \nS. aureus on at least 1 blood culture within 72 hours of beginning study drug (Cohort A) [OR] OR \nMRSA on a baseline blood culture [AND] and on at least 1 additional blood culture after at least 72 hours of vancomycin [OR] and/or daptomycin treatment (Cohort B). \n2. Male [OR] or female ≥ 18 years of age. \n3. If female of childbearing potential must be willing to practice sexual abstinence [OR] or dual methods of contraception during treatment [AND] and for at least 30 days after the last dose of study drug. \n4. Expectation of survival for at least 2 months.<|eot_id|>']
Response: 1. Presence of bacteremia due solely to: 
S. aureus on at least 1 blood culture within 72 hours of beginning study drug (Cohort A) [OR] OR 
MRSA on a baseline blood culture [AND] and on at least 1 additional blood culture after at least 72 hours of vancomycin [OR] and/or daptomycin treatment (Cohort B). 
2. Male [OR] or female ≥ 18 years of age. 
3. If female of childbearing potential must be willing to practice sexual abstinence [OR] or dual methods of contraception during treatment [AND] and for at least 30 days after the last dose of study drug. 
4. Expectation of survival for at least 2 months.
