ption, one of which must be a barrier method, for the duration of the study and for 77 days after the last dose \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nHealthy male volunteers, 18 to 45 years of age, inclusive. Healthy status is defined by [NOT] absence of evidence of any active [OR] or chronic disease following a detailed medical [OR] and surgical history, a complete physical examination including vital signs, 12-lead ECG, hematology, [OR] blood chemistry, [OR] serology [OR] and urinalysis \nBody mass index (BMI) 18 to 30 kg/m2 inclusive \nMale subjects (whether surgically sterilized [OR] or [NOT] not) [AND] with female partners [AND] of child-bearing potential must use two forms of contraception, one of which must be a barrier method, for the duration of the study [AND] and for 77 days after the last dose<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Healthy male volunteers, 18 to 45 years of age, inclusive. Healthy status is defined by [NOT] absence of evidence of any active [OR] or chronic disease following a detailed medical [OR] and surgical history, a complete physical examination including vital signs, 12-lead ECG, hematology, [OR] blood chemistry, [OR] serology [OR] and urinalysis 
Body mass index (BMI) 18 to 30 kg/m2 inclusive 
Male subjects (whether surgically sterilized [OR] or [NOT] not) [AND] with female partners [AND] of child-bearing potential must use two forms of contraception, one of which must be a barrier method, for the duration of the study [AND] and for 77 days after the last dose
