Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nany neurological conditions other than PD; \nsignificant musculoskeletal or cardiopulmonary diseases; \nother disorders that may affect balance or locomotion; \ntaken any structured behavioral or exercise programs in the past 3 months \nor they are receiving regular physical rehabilitation at present; \nunstable condition on anti-parkinsonian medications; \nsurgical interventions for PD; \ncommunication or cognitive deficits with mini-mental state examination, (MMSE) <24/30 (Folstein et al., 1975); \na history of more than two falls in the previous 12 months.       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\n  -  diagnosed with PD;\n  -  aged 40-80 years;\n  -  scored 24 or above on the Folstein Mini-Mental State Examination (MMSE);\n  -  able to give written, informed consent;\n  -  able to walk with full capability on lower extremity passive range of motion;\n  -  able to walk for at least 50 feet with full capability on lower extremity passive range of motion;\n  -  able to get up and down from the floor with no external support (arm rests OK) in one attempt;\n  -  has a score of 27 or above on the Berg Balance Scale;\n  -  has a score of 0.5 or above on the Schwab and England Activities of Daily Living Scale;\n  -  has a score of 20 or above on the Folstein Mini-Mental State Examination (MMSE);\n  -  able to walk with full capability on lower extremity passive range of motion;\n  -  able to walk for at least 50 feet with full capability on lower extremity passive range of motion;\n  -  able to get up and down from the floor with no external support (arm rests OK) in one attempt;\n  -  has a score of 27 or above on the Berg Balance Scale;\n  -  has a score of 0.5 or above on the Schwab and England Activities of Daily Living Scale;\n  -  has a score of 20 or above on the Folstein Mini-Mental State Examination (MMSE);\nExclusion Criteria:\n - any neurological conditions other than PD; \n - significant musculoskeletal [OR] or cardiopulmonary diseases; \n - other disorders that may affect balance [OR] or locomotion; \n - taken any structured behavioral [OR] or exercise programs in the past 3 months \n - or they are receiving regular physical rehabilitation at present; \n - unstable condition on anti-parkinsonian medications; \n - surgical interventions for PD; \n - communication [OR] or cognitive deficits [AND] with mini-mental state examination, (MMSE) <24/30 (Folstein et al., 1975); \n - a history of more than two falls in the previous 12 months.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
  -  diagnosed with PD;
  -  aged 40-80 years;
  -  scored 24 or above on the Folstein Mini-Mental State Examination (MMSE);
  -  able to give written, informed consent;
  -  able to walk with full capability on lower extremity passive range of motion;
  -  able to walk for at least 50 feet with full capability on lower extremity passive range of motion;
  -  able to get up and down from the floor with no external support (arm rests OK) in one attempt;
  -  has a score of 27 or above on the Berg Balance Scale;
  -  has a score of 0.5 or above on the Schwab and England Activities of Daily Living Scale;
  -  has a score of 20 or above on the Folstein Mini-Mental State Examination (MMSE);
  -  able to walk with full capability on lower extremity passive range of motion;
  -  able to walk for at least 50 feet with full capability on lower extremity passive range of motion;
  -  able to get up and down from the floor with no external support (arm rests OK) in one attempt;
  -  has a score of 27 or above on the Berg Balance Scale;
  -  has a score of 0.5 or above on the Schwab and England Activities of Daily Living Scale;
  -  has a score of 20 or above on the Folstein Mini-Mental State Examination (MMSE);
Exclusion Criteria:
 - any neurological conditions other than PD; 
 - significant musculoskeletal [OR] or cardiopulmonary diseases; 
 - other disorders that may affect balance [OR] or locomotion; 
 - taken any structured behavioral [OR] or exercise programs in the past 3 months 
 - or they are receiving regular physical rehabilitation at present; 
 - unstable condition on anti-parkinsonian medications; 
 - surgical interventions for PD; 
 - communication [OR] or cognitive deficits [AND] with mini-mental state examination, (MMSE) <24/30 (Folstein et al., 1975); 
 - a history of more than two falls in the previous 12 months.
