Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nSubject has been diagnosed with symptomatic paroxysmal atrial fibrillation as defined above and at least two symptomatic episodes in the last six months prior to inclusion.\nAt least one episode of AF must be documented during the prior year by any kind of ECG recording.\nSubject has structural normal heart with an LVEF = 50%, thickness of the inter-ventricular septum =12 mm and left atrium diameters (short axis) < 46 mm obtained by transthoracic echocardiography.\nSubject has normal ECG parameters (QRS width in the 12 channel surface ECG =120 ms, QTc - interval < 440 ms, PQ - interval = 210 ms; all parameters should be measured at sinus rhythm).\nSubject is at least 18 and not older than 75years old.\nSubject is able and willing to give informed consent.\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nSubject has been diagnosed with symptomatic paroxysmal atrial fibrillation as defined above [AND] and at least two symptomatic episodes in the last six months prior to inclusion.\nAt least one episode of AF must be documented during the prior year by any kind of ECG recording.\nSubject has structural normal heart [AND] with an LVEF = 50%, thickness of the inter-ventricular septum =12 mm [AND] and left atrium diameters (short axis) < 46 mm obtained by transthoracic echocardiography.\nSubject has normal ECG parameters (QRS width in the 12 channel surface ECG =120 ms, QTc - interval < 440 ms, PQ - interval = 210 ms; all parameters should be measured at sinus rhythm).\nSubject is at least 18 [AND] and [NOT] not older than 75years old.\nSubject is able and willing to give informed consent.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Subject has been diagnosed with symptomatic paroxysmal atrial fibrillation as defined above [AND] and at least two symptomatic episodes in the last six months prior to inclusion.
At least one episode of AF must be documented during the prior year by any kind of ECG recording.
Subject has structural normal heart [AND] with an LVEF = 50%, thickness of the inter-ventricular septum =12 mm [AND] and left atrium diameters (short axis) < 46 mm obtained by transthoracic echocardiography.
Subject has normal ECG parameters (QRS width in the 12 channel surface ECG =120 ms, QTc - interval < 440 ms, PQ - interval = 210 ms; all parameters should be measured at sinus rhythm).
Subject is at least 18 [AND] and [NOT] not older than 75years old.
Subject is able and willing to give informed consent.
