Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nHospitalization for acute decompensated HF within previous 30 days\nHospitalization for myocardial infarction or cardiac surgery within previous 90 days\nPresence of a left ventricular assist device\nHistory of heart transplantation\nPoorly controlled hypertension (>170/>110)\nPoorly controlled diabetes (HbA1c > 9.0)\nSevere renal failure with estimated glomerular filtration rate <30 ml/min\nPrior stroke with functional impairment or other severe, uncontrolled medical problems that may impair ability to participate in the study exams, based on medical history and review of medical records\nSevere chronic insomnia, with reported usual sleep duration <4 hours\nSevere daytime sleepiness, defined as Epworth Sleepiness Scale score 18 or higher or a report of falling asleep driving during the previous year, and deemed a safety risk by study physician\nAwake resting oxyhemoglobin saturation <89%\nPregnancy\nSmoking by subject or other person in the subject\'s bedroom, or other open flame in bedroom\nCurrent use of a positive airway pressure device (including continuous or bi-level positive airway pressure or adaptive servo-ventilation) or supplemental oxygen therapy\n\n\n### Response:\nHospitalization for acute decompensated HF within previous 30 days\nHospitalization for myocardial infarction [OR] or cardiac surgery within previous 90 days\nPresence of a left ventricular assist device\nHistory of heart transplantation\nPoorly controlled hypertension (>170/>110)\nPoorly controlled diabetes (HbA1c > 9.0)\nSevere renal failure [AND] with estimated glomerular filtration rate <30 ml/min\nPrior stroke [AND] with functional impairment [OR] or other severe, uncontrolled medical problems that may impair ability to participate in the study exams, based on medical history and review of medical records\nSevere chronic insomnia, [AND] with reported usual sleep duration <4 hours\n Severe daytime sleepiness, defined as Epworth Sleepiness Scale score 18 or higher [OR] or a report of falling asleep driving during the previous year, and deemed a safety risk by study physician\nAwake resting oxyhemoglobin saturation <89%\nPregnancy\nSmoking by subject [OR] or other person in the subject\'s bedroom, [OR] or other open flame in bedroom\nCurrent use of a positive airway pressure device (including continuous [OR] or bi-level positive airway pressure [OR] or adaptive servo-ventilation) [OR] or supplemental oxygen therapy<|eot_id|>']
Response: Hospitalization for acute decompensated HF within previous 30 days
Hospitalization for myocardial infarction [OR] or cardiac surgery within previous 90 days
Presence of a left ventricular assist device
History of heart transplantation
Poorly controlled hypertension (>170/>110)
Poorly controlled diabetes (HbA1c > 9.0)
Severe renal failure [AND] with estimated glomerular filtration rate <30 ml/min
Prior stroke [AND] with functional impairment [OR] or other severe, uncontrolled medical problems that may impair ability to participate in the study exams, based on medical history and review of medical records
Severe chronic insomnia, [AND] with reported usual sleep duration <4 hours
 Severe daytime sleepiness, defined as Epworth Sleepiness Scale score 18 or higher [OR] or a report of falling asleep driving during the previous year, and deemed a safety risk by study physician
Awake resting oxyhemoglobin saturation <89%
Pregnancy
Smoking by subject [OR] or other person in the subject's bedroom, [OR] or other open flame in bedroom
Current use of a positive airway pressure device (including continuous [OR] or bi-level positive airway pressure [OR] or adaptive servo-ventilation) [OR] or supplemental oxygen therapy
