Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nCases (with a history of TBI): \n1. Ages 50-95 years \n2. History of traumatic brain injury of sufficient severity to have resulted in medical attention (ascertained via the Ohio State University TBI Identification Questionnaire—OSU TBI-ID, and based on DoD/VA criteria) \n3. Residence in AFRH-Washington D.C. or the Veterans Home of California-Yountville \n4. MMSE score ≥ 20 \n5. Capacity to provide consent to participate in research (assessment made by study physician) \n6. Ability to read and write English \nControls (without a history of TBI): \n1. Ages 50-95 years \n2. No history of traumatic brain injury of sufficient severity to have resulted in medical attention (ascertained via the Ohio State University TBI Identification Questionnaire—OSU TBI-ID) \n3. Residence in AFRH-Washington or the Veterans Home of California-Yountville \n4. MMSE score ≥ 20 \n5. Capacity to provide consent or assent to participate in research \n6. Ability to read and write English - \n\n\n### Response:\nCases (with a history of TBI): \n 1. Ages 50-95 years \n 2. History of traumatic brain injury of sufficient severity to have resulted in medical attention (ascertained via the Ohio State University TBI Identification Questionnaire—OSU TBI-ID, and based on DoD/VA criteria) \n 3. Residence in AFRH-Washington D.C. [OR] or the Veterans Home of California-Yountville \n 4. MMSE score ≥ 20 \n 5. Capacity to provide consent to participate in research (assessment made by study physician) \n 6. Ability to read and write English \nControls ([NOT] without a history of TBI): \n 1. Ages 50-95 years \n 2. [NOT] No history of traumatic brain injury of sufficient severity to have resulted in medical attention (ascertained via the Ohio State University TBI Identification Questionnaire—OSU TBI-ID) \n 3. Residence in AFRH-Washington [OR] or the Veterans Home of California-Yountville \n 4. MMSE score ≥ 20 \n 5. Capacity to provide consent or assent to participate in research \n 6. Ability to read and write English -<|eot_id|>']
Response: Cases (with a history of TBI): 
 1. Ages 50-95 years 
 2. History of traumatic brain injury of sufficient severity to have resulted in medical attention (ascertained via the Ohio State University TBI Identification Questionnaire—OSU TBI-ID, and based on DoD/VA criteria) 
 3. Residence in AFRH-Washington D.C. [OR] or the Veterans Home of California-Yountville 
 4. MMSE score ≥ 20 
 5. Capacity to provide consent to participate in research (assessment made by study physician) 
 6. Ability to read and write English 
Controls ([NOT] without a history of TBI): 
 1. Ages 50-95 years 
 2. [NOT] No history of traumatic brain injury of sufficient severity to have resulted in medical attention (ascertained via the Ohio State University TBI Identification Questionnaire—OSU TBI-ID) 
 3. Residence in AFRH-Washington [OR] or the Veterans Home of California-Yountville 
 4. MMSE score ≥ 20 
 5. Capacity to provide consent or assent to participate in research 
 6. Ability to read and write English -
