Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nFailure to provide informed consent \nInability to complete 400 m walk within 15 minutes without sitting or interpersonal assistance, as an indicator of disablement and likely inability to fully engage in the exercise intervention \nPrimary indication for ACE inhibitor use, i.e. Congestive Heart Failure, CAD, diabetes \nKnown hypersensitivity to ACE inhibitors \nResistant hypertension, defined as BP > 140/90, despite the use of three or more anti-hypertensive drugs \nOffice or average home SBP > 180 mm Hg or DBP > 110 mm Hg (Average home BP in any seven day period during trial) \nPrimary renal disease \nSerum creatinine >2.5 mg/dL in men, or >2.0 mg/dL in women \nSerum potassium >5.0 molar equivalent/L \nUrinary protein > 1 on dipstick \nAbnormal liver enzymes (Aspartate transaminase (AST), Alanine transaminase (ALT), or alkaline phosphatase > 2.5 times the upper limit of normal) \nSevere cardiac disease, including New York Heart Association Class III or IV congestive heart failure, clinically significant aortic stenosis, history of cardiac arrest, use of a cardiac defibrillator, or uncontrolled angina \nAcute myocardial infarction identified by ECG \nLives in a nursing home (persons living in assisted or independent housing will not be excluded) \nSignificant cognitive impairment, defined as a known diagnosis of dementia or a Mini-Mental State Examination exam score < 24 \nUnable to communicate because of severe hearing loss or speech disorder \nSevere visual impairment, which would preclude completion of the assessments and/or intervention \nOther significant co-morbid disease that would prevent participation in exercise \nPlanning to move out of the area during the study time frame \nSimultaneous participation in another intervention trial       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\n  -  Participant in the Dartmouth Hitchcock Weight and Wellness Center (WWC) Healthy Lifestyle Program (HLP)\n  -  Aged 18-65 years\n  -  English-speaking\nExclusion Criteria:\n  -  Failure to provide informed consent \nInability to complete 400 m walk [AND] within 15 minutes [NOT] without sitting [OR] or interpersonal assistance, as an indicator of disablement [AND] and likely [NOT] inability to fully engage in the exercise intervention \nPrimary indication for ACE inhibitor use, i.e. Congestive Heart Failure, [OR] CAD, [OR] diabetes \nKnown hypersensitivity to ACE inhibitors \nResistant hypertension, defined as BP [AND] > 140/90, [NOT] despite the use of three or more anti-hypertensive drugs \nOffice [OR] or average home SBP [AND] > 180 mm Hg [OR] or DBP > 110 mm Hg (Average home BP in any seven day period during trial) \nPrimary renal disease \nSerum creatinine >2.5 mg/dL in men, [OR] or >2.0 mg/dL in women \nSerum potassium >5.0 molar equivalent/L \nUrinary protein > 1 on dipstick \nAbnormal liver enzymes (Aspartate transaminase (AST), Alanine transaminase (ALT), [OR] or alkaline phosphatase > 2.5 times the upper limit of normal) \nSevere cardiac disease, including New York Heart Association Class III or IV congestive heart failure, clinically significant aortic stenosis, history of cardiac arrest, use of a cardiac defibrillator, [OR] or uncontrolled angina \nAcute myocardial infarction identified by ECG \nLives in a nursing home (persons living in assisted [OR] or independent housing will [NOT] not be excluded) \nSignificant cognitive impairment, defined as a known diagnosis of dementia [OR] or a Mini-Mental State Examination exam score < 24 \nUnable to communicate because of severe hearing loss [OR] or speech disorder \nSevere visual impairment, which would [NOT] preclude completion of the assessments [OR] and/or intervention \nOther significant co-morbid disease that would [NOT] prevent participation in exercise \nPlanning to move out of the area during the study time frame \nSimultaneous participation in another intervention trial<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
  -  Participant in the Dartmouth Hitchcock Weight and Wellness Center (WWC) Healthy Lifestyle Program (HLP)
  -  Aged 18-65 years
  -  English-speaking
Exclusion Criteria:
  -  Failure to provide informed consent 
Inability to complete 400 m walk [AND] within 15 minutes [NOT] without sitting [OR] or interpersonal assistance, as an indicator of disablement [AND] and likely [NOT] inability to fully engage in the exercise intervention 
Primary indication for ACE inhibitor use, i.e. Congestive Heart Failure, [OR] CAD, [OR] diabetes 
Known hypersensitivity to ACE inhibitors 
Resistant hypertension, defined as BP [AND] > 140/90, [NOT] despite the use of three or more anti-hypertensive drugs 
Office [OR] or average home SBP [AND] > 180 mm Hg [OR] or DBP > 110 mm Hg (Average home BP in any seven day period during trial) 
Primary renal disease 
Serum creatinine >2.5 mg/dL in men, [OR] or >2.0 mg/dL in women 
Serum potassium >5.0 molar equivalent/L 
Urinary protein > 1 on dipstick 
Abnormal liver enzymes (Aspartate transaminase (AST), Alanine transaminase (ALT), [OR] or alkaline phosphatase > 2.5 times the upper limit of normal) 
Severe cardiac disease, including New York Heart Association Class III or IV congestive heart failure, clinically significant aortic stenosis, history of cardiac arrest, use of a cardiac defibrillator, [OR] or uncontrolled angina 
Acute myocardial infarction identified by ECG 
Lives in a nursing home (persons living in assisted [OR] or independent housing will [NOT] not be excluded) 
Significant cognitive impairment, defined as a known diagnosis of dementia [OR] or a Mini-Mental State Examination exam score < 24 
Unable to communicate because of severe hearing loss [OR] or speech disorder 
Severe visual impairment, which would [NOT] preclude completion of the assessments [OR] and/or intervention 
Other significant co-morbid disease that would [NOT] prevent participation in exercise 
Planning to move out of the area during the study time frame 
Simultaneous participation in another intervention trial
