Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nSuccessful cardiac ablation for AF\nDocumented freedom from AF recurrence (symptomatic or asymptomatic arrhythmic recurrences lasting longer than 30 seconds) 3 months after successful cardiac ablation (AF recurrence during 3-month blanking period is excluded).\nPatient must have been on a commercially approved anticoagulation therapy for at least two (2) months prior to randomization in the OAT Study.\nCHADS2 score = 2 or CHA2DS2-VASc score (=3)\nLeft ventricular ejection fraction > 25%\nLA size < 65\nHigh risk for thromboembolic events (i.e., CHADS2 score = 2 or CHA2DS2-VASc score = 3) and require OAT before undergoing cardiac ablation\nAble and willing to comply with all pre- and follow-up testing and requirements\nSigned informed consent form\nAge 18 years or older\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nSuccessful cardiac ablation for AF\nDocumented freedom from AF recurrence (symptomatic [OR] or asymptomatic arrhythmic recurrences lasting longer than 30 seconds) 3 months after successful cardiac ablation (AF recurrence during 3-month blanking period is [NOT] excluded).\nPatient must have been on a commercially approved anticoagulation therapy for at least two (2) months prior to randomization in the OAT Study.\nCHADS2 score = 2 [OR] or CHA2DS2-VASc score (=3)\nLeft ventricular ejection fraction > 25%\n LA size < 65\nHigh risk for thromboembolic events (i.e., CHADS2 score = 2 [OR] or CHA2DS2-VASc score = 3) [AND] and require OAT before undergoing cardiac ablation\nAble and willing to comply with all pre- and follow-up testing and requirements\nSigned informed consent form\nAge 18 years or older<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Successful cardiac ablation for AF
Documented freedom from AF recurrence (symptomatic [OR] or asymptomatic arrhythmic recurrences lasting longer than 30 seconds) 3 months after successful cardiac ablation (AF recurrence during 3-month blanking period is [NOT] excluded).
Patient must have been on a commercially approved anticoagulation therapy for at least two (2) months prior to randomization in the OAT Study.
CHADS2 score = 2 [OR] or CHA2DS2-VASc score (=3)
Left ventricular ejection fraction > 25%
 LA size < 65
High risk for thromboembolic events (i.e., CHADS2 score = 2 [OR] or CHA2DS2-VASc score = 3) [AND] and require OAT before undergoing cardiac ablation
Able and willing to comply with all pre- and follow-up testing and requirements
Signed informed consent form
Age 18 years or older
