4 weeks (with the exception of diuretics)\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nPatients with chronic heart failure [AND] of New York Heart Association Class II [OR] or III, a left ventricular ejection fraction of = 40% [AND] for patients in NYHA class II [OR] or = 45% for patients in NYHA class III, a hemoglobin level at the screening visit between 9.5-13.5 g/dl, [AND] and iron deficiency, which is defined as serum ferritin level < 100µg/l [OR] or between 100 and 299 µg/l, when transferring saturation is < 20%.\nAge =18 years\nObtained informed consent\nStable pharmacological therapy during the last 4 weeks (with the exception of diuretics)<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Patients with chronic heart failure [AND] of New York Heart Association Class II [OR] or III, a left ventricular ejection fraction of = 40% [AND] for patients in NYHA class II [OR] or = 45% for patients in NYHA class III, a hemoglobin level at the screening visit between 9.5-13.5 g/dl, [AND] and iron deficiency, which is defined as serum ferritin level < 100µg/l [OR] or between 100 and 299 µg/l, when transferring saturation is < 20%.
Age =18 years
Obtained informed consent
Stable pharmacological therapy during the last 4 weeks (with the exception of diuretics)
