Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nRichter\'s syndrome, Burkitt\'s lymphoma, or Burkitt-like Lymphoma (transformed DLBCL from Follicular NHL are eligible). \nPrior transplant with stem cell infusion 90 days or active graft-versus-host treatment within 8 weeks of Day 1. \nPrior therapy with SYK inhibitors. \nChronic treatment with strong CYP3A4 inhibitor/ inducer, acid reducing agent, Proton pump inhibitors \nKnown lymphomatous involvement of the CNS. \nPersistent, unresolved NCI CTCAE v4.0 ≥ Grade 2, previous drug-related toxicity (except alopecia, erectile impotence, hot flashes, libido, neuropathy). \nPrior monoclonal antibody, radioimmunoconjugate, antibody drug conjugate, phototherapy, radiotherapy, chemotherapy, immunotherapy, immunosuppressive therapy, or any test agent within 3 weeks or for alemtuzumab 8 weeks of Day 1. \nFor CTCL: (TSEBT) within 12 weeks, or initiation of topical steroid, nitrogen mustard, or topical retinoid within 2 weeks. (Stable topical ≥ 4 weeks prior to Day 1 allowed). \nKnown carrier or infection for HIV/Hep B or C. HCV ab+ must be PCR-. HBV ab+ must be HBsAg- or undetectable DNA \nActive infection requiring systemic treatment, \nSignificant GI disease, previous major gastric/bowel surgery, difficulty swallowing or malabsorption syndrome. \nMajor surgery within 4 weeks \nPrevious malignancies within 2 yrs. unless relapse risk is small (< 5%). \nCurrent use of systemic steroids >20 mg QD prednisone (or equivalent) \nBreastfeeding or pregnant (intention to become) females or participation in other clinical trials       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nRichter\'s syndrome, [OR] Burkitt\'s lymphoma, [OR] or Burkitt-like Lymphoma (transformed DLBCL [AND] from Follicular NHL are eligible). \nPrior transplant [AND] with stem cell infusion 90 days [OR] or active graft-versus-host treatment within 8 weeks of Day 1. \nPrior therapy with SYK inhibitors. \nChronic treatment with strong CYP3A4 inhibitor/ [OR] inducer, acid reducing agent, [OR] Proton pump inhibitors \nKnown lymphomatous involvement of the CNS. \nPersistent, unresolved NCI CTCAE v4.0 ≥ Grade 2, previous drug-related toxicity (except alopecia, [OR] erectile impotence, [OR] hot flashes, [OR] libido, [OR] neuropathy). \nPrior monoclonal antibody, [OR] radioimmunoconjugate, [OR] antibody drug conjugate, [OR] phototherapy, [OR] radiotherapy, [OR] chemotherapy, [OR] immunotherapy, [OR] immunosuppressive therapy, [OR] or any test agent within 3 weeks [OR] or for alemtuzumab 8 weeks of Day 1. \nFor CTCL: (TSEBT) within 12 weeks, [OR] or initiation of topical steroid, [OR] nitrogen mustard, [OR] or topical retinoid within 2 weeks. (Stable topical ≥ 4 weeks prior to Day 1 allowed). \nKnown carrier [OR] or infection for HIV/ [OR] Hep B [OR] or C. HCV ab+ must be PCR-. HBV ab+ must be HBsAg- [OR] or undetectable DNA \nActive infection requiring systemic treatment, \nSignificant GI disease, previous major gastric/ [OR] bowel surgery, [OR] difficulty swallowing [OR] or malabsorption syndrome. \nMajor surgery within 4 weeks \nPrevious malignancies within 2 yrs. unless relapse risk is small (< 5%). \nCurrent use of systemic steroids >20 mg QD prednisone [OR] (or equivalent) \nBreastfeeding [OR] or pregnant (intention to become) females [OR] or participation in other clinical trials<|eot_id|>']
Response: Richter's syndrome, [OR] Burkitt's lymphoma, [OR] or Burkitt-like Lymphoma (transformed DLBCL [AND] from Follicular NHL are eligible). 
Prior transplant [AND] with stem cell infusion 90 days [OR] or active graft-versus-host treatment within 8 weeks of Day 1. 
Prior therapy with SYK inhibitors. 
Chronic treatment with strong CYP3A4 inhibitor/ [OR] inducer, acid reducing agent, [OR] Proton pump inhibitors 
Known lymphomatous involvement of the CNS. 
Persistent, unresolved NCI CTCAE v4.0 ≥ Grade 2, previous drug-related toxicity (except alopecia, [OR] erectile impotence, [OR] hot flashes, [OR] libido, [OR] neuropathy). 
Prior monoclonal antibody, [OR] radioimmunoconjugate, [OR] antibody drug conjugate, [OR] phototherapy, [OR] radiotherapy, [OR] chemotherapy, [OR] immunotherapy, [OR] immunosuppressive therapy, [OR] or any test agent within 3 weeks [OR] or for alemtuzumab 8 weeks of Day 1. 
For CTCL: (TSEBT) within 12 weeks, [OR] or initiation of topical steroid, [OR] nitrogen mustard, [OR] or topical retinoid within 2 weeks. (Stable topical ≥ 4 weeks prior to Day 1 allowed). 
Known carrier [OR] or infection for HIV/ [OR] Hep B [OR] or C. HCV ab+ must be PCR-. HBV ab+ must be HBsAg- [OR] or undetectable DNA 
Active infection requiring systemic treatment, 
Significant GI disease, previous major gastric/ [OR] bowel surgery, [OR] difficulty swallowing [OR] or malabsorption syndrome. 
Major surgery within 4 weeks 
Previous malignancies within 2 yrs. unless relapse risk is small (< 5%). 
Current use of systemic steroids >20 mg QD prednisone [OR] (or equivalent) 
Breastfeeding [OR] or pregnant (intention to become) females [OR] or participation in other clinical trials
