5.\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\n=18 years old, men [OR] or post-menopausal women ([women] [AND] [NOT] with [NOT] no periods [OR] for 12 months or more, [OR] or those who have had a surgical menopause)\nTreated hypertensive patients [AND] with an average daytime ambulatory blood pressure measurement (ABPM) <150/95mmHg [AND] on stable doses of one or more antihypertensive medication (at least one of which should be; an ACE inhibitor, [OR] angiotensin receptor blocker [OR] or diuretic) for 3 months, [OR] or [NOT] untreated hypertensive patients [AND] with an average daytime ABPM =135/85 [AND] but <150/95.<|eot_id|>']
