Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nUse of any investigational or non-registered drug or vaccine product within 30 days preceding the administration of the study vaccine or planned use within the first six weeks of the study period \nHas received any licensed or other investigational influenza vaccine within 3 months prior to enrollment in this study or expected receipt of any influenza vaccination before the Day 21 blood collection \nHistory of excessive alcohol use, drug abuse or significant psychiatric illness \nTobacco use within 3 months of enrollment and throughout first 6 months of the study \nHas a chronic illness (e.g., liver or kidney disease), receiving a concomitant therapy or have any other condition that could interfere with the subject\'s participation in the study or in the interpretation of the study results \nClinically significant abnormal liver function tests at screening \nPositive serology for HBsAg, HCV or HIV antibodies \nPregnant or lactating female \nHaving cancer or have received treatment for cancer within three years (persons with a history of cancer who are disease-free without treatment for three years or more are eligible), excluding minor skin cancers, which are allowed unless located at the vaccination site \nPersons with impaired immune responsiveness (of any cause), including diabetes mellitus and autoimmune disorders \nPersons presently receiving or having a recent history of receiving (within the past six months) any medication or therapeutic modality that affects the immune system such as allergy shots, immune globulin, interferon, immunomodulators, radiation therapy, cytotoxic drugs or drugs known to be frequently associated with significant major organ toxicity, or systemic corticosteroids (oral or injectable). Inhaled and topical corticosteroids are allowed. \nPersons with a history of severe allergic reaction after previous vaccinations or hypersensitivity to any seasonal influenza vaccine component \nPersons with a history of Guillain-Barré Syndrome \nReceipt of blood or blood products 8 weeks prior to vaccination or planned administration during the three week study period following vaccination \nDonation of blood or blood products within 8 weeks prior to vaccination or during the three week study period following \nAn oral temperature >100.4° or acute disease within 72 hours prior to vaccination, defined as the presence of a moderate or severe illness (as determined by the investigator through medical history and physical examination; for example, those requiring an absence from work) with or without fever. \nBody Mass Index >29.9 \nAny disorder of coagulation \nA clinical diagnosis of influenza within the previous 12 months \nAny other condition or circumstance which, in the opinion of the Principal Investigator, poses an unacceptable risk for participation in the study       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\n  -  Adults 18 years of age or older\n  -  Subjects able to provide written informed consent\n  -  Subjects able to provide a blood sample\n  -  Subjects willing to return annually for up to five years for a booster vaccination and blood sampling\n  -  Subjects willing and able to provide a nasal wash or saliva sample\n  -  Subjects able to provide a stool sample\n  -  Subjects willing to be contacted annually for up to five years to complete a health questionnaire\nExclusion Criteria:\n  -  Use of any investigational [OR] or non-registered drug [OR] or vaccine product within 30 days preceding the administration of the study vaccine [OR] or planned use within the first six weeks of the study period \n  -  Has received any licensed [OR] or other investigational influenza vaccine within 3 months prior to enrollment in this study [OR] or expected receipt of any influenza vaccination before the Day 21 blood collection \n  -  History of excessive alcohol use, [OR] drug abuse [OR] or significant psychiatric illness \n  -  Tobacco use within 3 months of enrollment and throughout first 6 months of the study \n  -  Has a chronic illness [OR] (e.g., liver [OR] or kidney disease), receiving a concomitant therapy [OR] or have any other condition that could interfere with the subject\'s participation in the study [OR] or in the interpretation of the study results \n  -  Clinically significant abnormal liver function tests at screening \n  -  Positive serology for HBsAg, [OR] HCV [OR] or HIV antibodies \n  -  Pregnant [OR] or lactating female \n  -  Having cancer [OR] or have received treatment for cancer within three years (persons with a history of cancer [AND] who are disease- [NOT] free [NOT] without treatment for three years or more are eligible), excluding minor skin cancers, which are allowed unless located at the vaccination site \n  -  Persons with impaired immune responsiveness (of any cause), including diabetes mellitus [OR] and autoimmune disorders \n  -  Persons presently receiving [OR] or having a recent history of receiving (within the past six months) any medication [OR] or therapeutic modality that affects the immune system such as allergy shots, [OR] immune globulin, [OR] interferon, [OR] immunomodulators, [OR] radiation therapy, [OR] cytotoxic drugs [OR] or drugs known to be frequently associated with significant major organ toxicity, [OR] or systemic corticosteroids (oral [OR] or injectable). Inhaled [OR] and topical corticosteroids are allowed. \n  -  Persons with a history of severe allergic reaction after previous vaccinations [OR] or hypersensitivity to any seasonal influenza vaccine component \n  -  Persons with a history of Guillain-Barré Syndrome \n  -  Receipt of blood [OR] or blood products 8 weeks prior to vaccination [OR] or planned administration during the three week study period following vaccination \n  -  Donation of blood [OR] or blood products within 8 weeks prior to vaccination [OR] or during the three week study period following \n  -  An oral temperature  >100.4° [OR] or acute disease within 72 hours prior to vaccination, defined as the presence of a moderate [OR] or severe illness (as determined by the investigator through medical history [OR] and physical examination; for example, those requiring an [NOT] absence [OR] from work) with or without fever. \n  -  Body Mass Index >29.9 \n  -  Any disorder of coagulation \n  -  A clinical diagnosis of influenza within the previous 12 months \n  -  Any other condition [OR] or circumstance which, in the opinion of the Principal Investigator, poses an unacceptable risk for participation in the study<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
  -  Adults 18 years of age or older
  -  Subjects able to provide written informed consent
  -  Subjects able to provide a blood sample
  -  Subjects willing to return annually for up to five years for a booster vaccination and blood sampling
  -  Subjects willing and able to provide a nasal wash or saliva sample
  -  Subjects able to provide a stool sample
  -  Subjects willing to be contacted annually for up to five years to complete a health questionnaire
Exclusion Criteria:
  -  Use of any investigational [OR] or non-registered drug [OR] or vaccine product within 30 days preceding the administration of the study vaccine [OR] or planned use within the first six weeks of the study period 
  -  Has received any licensed [OR] or other investigational influenza vaccine within 3 months prior to enrollment in this study [OR] or expected receipt of any influenza vaccination before the Day 21 blood collection 
  -  History of excessive alcohol use, [OR] drug abuse [OR] or significant psychiatric illness 
  -  Tobacco use within 3 months of enrollment and throughout first 6 months of the study 
  -  Has a chronic illness [OR] (e.g., liver [OR] or kidney disease), receiving a concomitant therapy [OR] or have any other condition that could interfere with the subject's participation in the study [OR] or in the interpretation of the study results 
  -  Clinically significant abnormal liver function tests at screening 
  -  Positive serology for HBsAg, [OR] HCV [OR] or HIV antibodies 
  -  Pregnant [OR] or lactating female 
  -  Having cancer [OR] or have received treatment for cancer within three years (persons with a history of cancer [AND] who are disease- [NOT] free [NOT] without treatment for three years or more are eligible), excluding minor skin cancers, which are allowed unless located at the vaccination site 
  -  Persons with impaired immune responsiveness (of any cause), including diabetes mellitus [OR] and autoimmune disorders 
  -  Persons presently receiving [OR] or having a recent history of receiving (within the past six months) any medication [OR] or therapeutic modality that affects the immune system such as allergy shots, [OR] immune globulin, [OR] interferon, [OR] immunomodulators, [OR] radiation therapy, [OR] cytotoxic drugs [OR] or drugs known to be frequently associated with significant major organ toxicity, [OR] or systemic corticosteroids (oral [OR] or injectable). Inhaled [OR] and topical corticosteroids are allowed. 
  -  Persons with a history of severe allergic reaction after previous vaccinations [OR] or hypersensitivity to any seasonal influenza vaccine component 
  -  Persons with a history of Guillain-Barré Syndrome 
  -  Receipt of blood [OR] or blood products 8 weeks prior to vaccination [OR] or planned administration during the three week study period following vaccination 
  -  Donation of blood [OR] or blood products within 8 weeks prior to vaccination [OR] or during the three week study period following 
  -  An oral temperature  >100.4° [OR] or acute disease within 72 hours prior to vaccination, defined as the presence of a moderate [OR] or severe illness (as determined by the investigator through medical history [OR] and physical examination; for example, those requiring an [NOT] absence [OR] from work) with or without fever. 
  -  Body Mass Index >29.9 
  -  Any disorder of coagulation 
  -  A clinical diagnosis of influenza within the previous 12 months 
  -  Any other condition [OR] or circumstance which, in the opinion of the Principal Investigator, poses an unacceptable risk for participation in the study
