Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nMales and females aged 18-40 years of age at the time of vaccination in good health as determined by medical history, physical exam, laboratory assessments and the clinical judgment of the Principal Investigator \nAble to provide informed consent indicating that they understand the purpose of this study and are willing to adhere to the procedures described in this protocol \nIf the subject is a female of childbearing potential, she must use adequate contraceptive precautions (e.g., intrauterine contraceptive device, oral contraceptives or other equivalent hormonal contraception) for 2 months prior to vaccination and continue to use such precautions for a minimum of three months after vaccination. She must also have a negative urine pregnancy test within 24 hours prior to receiving study vaccine. Women at least one year post-menopausal or surgically sterile will not be considered of childbearing potential. \nWilling to receive the unlicensed vaccine given as an IM injection \nWilling to provide multiple blood specimens collected by venipuncture \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nMales [OR] and females aged 18-40 years of age at the time of vaccination in good health as determined by medical history, [OR] physical exam, [OR] laboratory assessments and the clinical judgment of the Principal Investigator \nAble to provide informed consent indicating that they understand the purpose of this study and are willing to adhere to the procedures described in this protocol \nIf the subject is a female [AND] of childbearing potential, she must use adequate contraceptive precautions (e.g., intrauterine contraceptive device, [OR] oral contraceptives or other equivalent hormonal contraception) for 2 months prior to vaccination and continue to use such precautions for a minimum of three months after vaccination. She must also have a negative urine pregnancy test within 24 hours prior to receiving study vaccine. Women [AND] at least one year post-menopausal [OR] or surgically sterile will [NOT] not be considered of childbearing potential. \nWilling to receive the unlicensed vaccine given as an IM injection \nWilling to provide multiple blood specimens collected by venipuncture<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Males [OR] and females aged 18-40 years of age at the time of vaccination in good health as determined by medical history, [OR] physical exam, [OR] laboratory assessments and the clinical judgment of the Principal Investigator 
Able to provide informed consent indicating that they understand the purpose of this study and are willing to adhere to the procedures described in this protocol 
If the subject is a female [AND] of childbearing potential, she must use adequate contraceptive precautions (e.g., intrauterine contraceptive device, [OR] oral contraceptives or other equivalent hormonal contraception) for 2 months prior to vaccination and continue to use such precautions for a minimum of three months after vaccination. She must also have a negative urine pregnancy test within 24 hours prior to receiving study vaccine. Women [AND] at least one year post-menopausal [OR] or surgically sterile will [NOT] not be considered of childbearing potential. 
Willing to receive the unlicensed vaccine given as an IM injection 
Willing to provide multiple blood specimens collected by venipuncture
