t give informed consent\n\n\n### Response:\nCases of rectal tumours below 12cm from anal verge, [OR] or locally advanced tumours invading blood vessels, [OR] nerves [OR] or bone.\nMultiple bone metastasis [OR] or central nervous system metastasis\nOther neoplastic disease in the 5 previous years, except squamous [OR] or basal cell skin carcinoma [OR] or cervical "in situ" carcinoma\nSignificant heart disease (chronic congestive heart failure, symptomatic coronary disease) [OR] or myocardial infarction in the previous 6 months\nPeripheral neuropathy\nPatients who do not give informed consent<|eot_id|>']
