Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nThalassemia syndromes;\nMyelodysplastic syndrome (MDS) or myelofibrosis;\nDiamond Blackfan anemia;\nPrimary bone marrow failure;\nBaseline LIC >30 mg/g dw (measured by MRI);\nUnable or unwilling to undergo a 7 day washout period if currently being treated with deferiprone or deferoxamine or deferasirox;\nPrevious discontinuation of treatment with deferiprone or deferoxamine due to adverse events;\nHistory or presence of hypersensitivity or idiosyncratic reaction to deferiprone or deferoxamine;\nTreated with hydroxyurea within 30 days;\nHistory of malignancy;\nEvidence of abnormal liver function (serum ALT level(s) > 5 times upper limit of normal at screening or creatinine levels >2 times upper limit of normal at screening);\nA serious, unstable illness, as judged by the Investigator, during the past 3 months before screening/baseline visit including but not limited to: hepatic, renal, gastro-enterologic, respiratory, cardiovascular, endocrinologic, neurologic or immunologic disease;\nClinically significant abnormal 12-lead ECG findings;\nCardiac MRI T2* <10ms;\nMyocardial infarction, cardiac arrest or cardiac failure within 1 year before screening/baseline visit;\nUnable to undergo MRI\nPresence of metallic objects such as artificial joints, inner ear (cochlear) implants, brain aneurysm clips, pacemakers, and metallic foreign bodies in the eye or other body areas that would prevent use of MRI imaging\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nThalassemia syndromes;\nMyelodysplastic syndrome (MDS) [OR] or myelofibrosis;\nDiamond Blackfan anemia;\nPrimary bone marrow failure;\nBaseline LIC >30 mg/g dw (measured by MRI);\n [NOT] Unable [OR] or [NOT] unwilling to undergo a 7 day washout period if currently being treated with deferiprone [OR] or deferoxamine [OR] or deferasirox;\nPrevious discontinuation of treatment with deferiprone [OR] or deferoxamine due to adverse events;\nHistory [OR] or presence of hypersensitivity [OR] or idiosyncratic reaction to deferiprone [OR] or deferoxamine;\nTreated with hydroxyurea within 30 days;\nHistory of malignancy;\nEvidence of abnormal liver function (serum ALT level(s) > 5 times upper limit of normal at screening [OR] or creatinine levels >2 times upper limit of normal at screening);\n A serious, unstable illness, as judged by the Investigator, during the past 3 months before screening/baseline visit including but not limited to: hepatic, [OR] renal, [OR] gastro-enterologic, [OR] respiratory, [OR] cardiovascular, [OR] endocrinologic, [OR] neurologic [OR] or immunologic disease;\nClinically significant abnormal 12-lead ECG findings;\n Cardiac MRI T2* <10ms;\n Myocardial infarction, [OR] cardiac arrest [OR] or cardiac failure within 1 year before screening/baseline visit;\n [NOT] Unable to undergo MRI\nPresence of metallic objects such as artificial joints, [OR] inner ear (cochlear) implants, [OR] brain aneurysm clips, [OR] pacemakers, [OR] and metallic foreign bodies in the eye [OR] or other body areas that would [NOT] prevent use of MRI imaging<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Thalassemia syndromes;
Myelodysplastic syndrome (MDS) [OR] or myelofibrosis;
Diamond Blackfan anemia;
Primary bone marrow failure;
Baseline LIC >30 mg/g dw (measured by MRI);
 [NOT] Unable [OR] or [NOT] unwilling to undergo a 7 day washout period if currently being treated with deferiprone [OR] or deferoxamine [OR] or deferasirox;
Previous discontinuation of treatment with deferiprone [OR] or deferoxamine due to adverse events;
History [OR] or presence of hypersensitivity [OR] or idiosyncratic reaction to deferiprone [OR] or deferoxamine;
Treated with hydroxyurea within 30 days;
History of malignancy;
Evidence of abnormal liver function (serum ALT level(s) > 5 times upper limit of normal at screening [OR] or creatinine levels >2 times upper limit of normal at screening);
 A serious, unstable illness, as judged by the Investigator, during the past 3 months before screening/baseline visit including but not limited to: hepatic, [OR] renal, [OR] gastro-enterologic, [OR] respiratory, [OR] cardiovascular, [OR] endocrinologic, [OR] neurologic [OR] or immunologic disease;
Clinically significant abnormal 12-lead ECG findings;
 Cardiac MRI T2* <10ms;
 Myocardial infarction, [OR] cardiac arrest [OR] or cardiac failure within 1 year before screening/baseline visit;
 [NOT] Unable to undergo MRI
Presence of metallic objects such as artificial joints, [OR] inner ear (cochlear) implants, [OR] brain aneurysm clips, [OR] pacemakers, [OR] and metallic foreign bodies in the eye [OR] or other body areas that would [NOT] prevent use of MRI imaging
