Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nThe patients have other cancers at the same time or have the history of other cancers except controlled skin basal cell carcinoma or skin squamous cell carcinoma or carcinoma in situ of cervix uterus;\nThe patients have active infections that were not suitable for chemotherapy;\nThe patients have severe non-cancerous diseases.\nThe patients have history of neoadjuvant hormone therapy.\nThe patients have bilateral breast cancers or DCIS or metastatic breast cancers.\nThe patients are undergoing current administration of anti-cancer therapies, or are attending other clinical trials.\nThe patients are pregnant or lactational, or they refuse to practice contraception during the whole trial.\nThe patients are in some special conditions that they can\'t understand the written informed consent, such as they are demented or hawkish.\nThe patients have allergic history or contraindication of tamoxifen.\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\n  -  The patients are diagnosed as early breast cancer, and they are indicated for adjuvant chemotherapy.\n  -  The patients are aged from 18 to 65 years old.\n  -  The patients are postoperative, and they have received the first course of chemotherapy.\n  -  The patients are suitable for general surgery and one-lung ventilation.\n  -  The patients have the American Society of Anesthesiologists (ASA) physical status I or II.\nExclusion Criteria:\n  -  The patients have other cancers at the same time [OR] or have the history of other cancers except controlled skin basal cell carcinoma [OR] or skin squamous cell carcinoma [OR] or carcinoma in situ of cervix uterus;\n  -  The patients have active infections that were [NOT] not suitable for chemotherapy;\n  -  The patients have severe [NOT] non-cancerous diseases.\n  -  The patients have history of neoadjuvant hormone therapy.\n  -  The patients have bilateral breast cancers [OR] or DCIS [OR] or metastatic breast cancers.\n  -  The patients are undergoing current administration of anti-cancer therapies, [OR] or are attending other clinical trials.\n  -  The patients are pregnant [OR] or lactational, [OR] or they refuse to practice contraception during the whole trial.\n  -  The patients are in some special conditions that they can\'t understand the written informed consent, such as they are demented [OR] or hawkish.\n  -  The patients have allergic history [OR] or contraindication of tamoxifen.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
  -  The patients are diagnosed as early breast cancer, and they are indicated for adjuvant chemotherapy.
  -  The patients are aged from 18 to 65 years old.
  -  The patients are postoperative, and they have received the first course of chemotherapy.
  -  The patients are suitable for general surgery and one-lung ventilation.
  -  The patients have the American Society of Anesthesiologists (ASA) physical status I or II.
Exclusion Criteria:
  -  The patients have other cancers at the same time [OR] or have the history of other cancers except controlled skin basal cell carcinoma [OR] or skin squamous cell carcinoma [OR] or carcinoma in situ of cervix uterus;
  -  The patients have active infections that were [NOT] not suitable for chemotherapy;
  -  The patients have severe [NOT] non-cancerous diseases.
  -  The patients have history of neoadjuvant hormone therapy.
  -  The patients have bilateral breast cancers [OR] or DCIS [OR] or metastatic breast cancers.
  -  The patients are undergoing current administration of anti-cancer therapies, [OR] or are attending other clinical trials.
  -  The patients are pregnant [OR] or lactational, [OR] or they refuse to practice contraception during the whole trial.
  -  The patients are in some special conditions that they can't understand the written informed consent, such as they are demented [OR] or hawkish.
  -  The patients have allergic history [OR] or contraindication of tamoxifen.
