diac shunts\nHypersensitivity to perflutren, blood, blood products or albumin\n\n\n### Response:\nCongestive heart failure [OR] or coronary artery disease\nBlood pressure averaging > 159/99 mmHg\nSerum creatinine > 1.5 mg/dL\nDiabetes mellitus [OR] or other systemic illness\nLeft ventricular hypertrophy by echocardiography [OR] or ECG\nPregnancy\nHypersensitivity to spironolactone, [OR] chlorthalidone, [OR] amlodipine, human recombinant insulin [OR] or Definity\nAny history of substance abuse (other than tobacco)\nHistory of gouty arthritis\nPatients with right-to-left, [OR] bi-directional, [OR] or transient right-to-left cardiac shunts\nHypersensitivity to perflutren, blood, [OR] blood products [OR] or albumin<|eot_id|>']
