IV heart disease.       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nKnown pregnancy [OR] or breast-feeding. \nMedical illness unrelated to the tumor which in the opinion of the attending physician and principal investigator will [NOT] preclude administration of the agent. This includes patients with uncontrolled infection, chronic renal insufficiency, myocardial infarction within the past 6 months, unstable angina, [OR] cardiac arrhythmias other than chronic atrial fibrillation [OR] and chronic active [OR] or persistent hepatitis, [OR] or New York Heart Association Classification III or IV heart disease.<|eot_id|>']
