e than mild cognitive impairment) [OR] or delirium on preoperative CAM testing; 3) language barriers that would [NOT] preclude testing; 4) preoperative steroid use within 3 days of surgery; or 5) anticipation of postoperative intubation.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
1) preoperative diagnosis of delirium [OR] or dementia; 2) MMSE score of = 20 out of 30 on preoperative testing (more than mild cognitive impairment) [OR] or delirium on preoperative CAM testing; 3) language barriers that would [NOT] preclude testing; 4) preoperative steroid use within 3 days of surgery; or 5) anticipation of postoperative intubation.
