Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nPrimary groups: Vaccination against typhoid fever within 5 years before dosing.\nHistory of clinical typhoid fever, clinical paratyphoid A or B fever.\nImmunization with any other vaccine (oral or parenteral) within 4 weeks prior to study start or planned vaccination during the study\nCurrent intake of antibiotics or end of antibiotic therapy <8 days before first IMP administration\nChronic (longer than 14 days) administration of immunosuppressants or other immune-modifying drugs within 6 months before the first dose of investigational vaccine; oral corticosteroids in dosages of =0.5 mg/kg/d prednisolone or equivalent are excluded; inhaled or topical steroids are allowed\nAcute or chronic clinically significant gastrointestinal disease\n\n\n### Response:\nPrimary groups: Vaccination against typhoid fever within 5 years before dosing.\nHistory of clinical typhoid fever, clinical paratyphoid A [OR] or B fever.\nImmunization with any other vaccine (oral [OR] or parenteral) within 4 weeks prior to study start [OR] or planned vaccination during the study\nCurrent intake of antibiotics [OR] or end of antibiotic therapy <8 days before first IMP administration\nChronic (longer than 14 days) administration of immunosuppressants [OR] or other immune-modifying drugs within 6 months before the first dose of investigational vaccine; oral corticosteroids in dosages of =0.5 mg/kg/d prednisolone [OR] or equivalent are [NOT] excluded; inhaled [OR] or topical steroids are allowed\nAcute [OR] or chronic clinically significant gastrointestinal disease<|eot_id|>']
Response: Primary groups: Vaccination against typhoid fever within 5 years before dosing.
History of clinical typhoid fever, clinical paratyphoid A [OR] or B fever.
Immunization with any other vaccine (oral [OR] or parenteral) within 4 weeks prior to study start [OR] or planned vaccination during the study
Current intake of antibiotics [OR] or end of antibiotic therapy <8 days before first IMP administration
Chronic (longer than 14 days) administration of immunosuppressants [OR] or other immune-modifying drugs within 6 months before the first dose of investigational vaccine; oral corticosteroids in dosages of =0.5 mg/kg/d prednisolone [OR] or equivalent are [NOT] excluded; inhaled [OR] or topical steroids are allowed
Acute [OR] or chronic clinically significant gastrointestinal disease
