Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nLifetime history of Bipolar Disorder, Dementia, Autism Spectrum Disorder, Schizophrenia, or any other Psychotic Disorder.\nPsychotic symptoms occurring at any time during the current major depressive episode.\nCurrent (past 12 months) diagnosis of Panic disorder, Obsessive Compulsive Disorder, Posttraumatic Stress Disorder, Anorexia Nervosa, or Bulimia Nervosa.\nAlcohol or Drug Dependence within 12 months or Abuse within 3 months (excluding nicotine and caffeine) of baseline visit, as assessed by history and urine drug screen.\nClinical evidence of a severe Personality Disorder, as assessed by the study psychiatrist, which would impede participation or completion of the trial.\nKnown neurological disorders or documented serious head injury.\nSerious and unstable medical illnesses including cardiovascular disease and cancer.\nActive medical conditions with known mood changes (endocrine, autoimmune disorders).\nCurrent diabetes mellitus.\nFor women, pregnancy, lactation, or unwillingness to comply with birth control requirements.\nUse of any of the following treatments or any other alternative therapy within 2 weeks of the pre-treatment PET scan that may have beneficial effects on mood, including St John\'s Wort, S-adenosyl methionine (SAMe), n-3 fatty acids, or light therapy.\nUse of antidepressant medication within 1 month of the pre-treatment PET scan (within 5 weeks for fluoxetine and protryptyline).\nFailure to achieve a much improved status (i.e. equivalent to >50% symptom reduction) with any lifetime treatment course of CBT (defined as a minimum of 4 sessions of a specified manual-driven therapy by a CBT-trained therapist) or escitalopram (defined as a minimum of 6 weeks of at least 10 mg/day).\nClinically significant active suicidal ideation or self-injurious behavior necessitating immediate treatment, as determined by the investigator.\nReceived electroconvulsive therapy in the past 6 months or during the current depressive episode.\nCurrently responding to medication treatment, without clinical reasons to change.\nCurrent treatment with weekly individual or group psychotherapy of any type targeted at depressive symptoms.\nQTc >500 milliseconds on EKG at screening.\nContraindications for MRI, including, but not limited to pacemaker, aneurysm clips, neurostimulators, cochlear implants, metal in eyes, steel worker, intra-uterine devices for birth control.\nMaintenance or prophylactic therapy for stable medical conditions.\nHypnotic medication prescribed or approved by the study physician, (up to a three doses per week) for insomnia, as long if not the night before a PET/MRI or clinic ratings visit. Antipsychotic medications, whether prescribed for sleep or other indications, are prohibited.\n\n\n### Response:\nLifetime history of Bipolar Disorder, [OR] Dementia, [OR] Autism Spectrum Disorder, [OR] Schizophrenia, [OR] or any other Psychotic Disorder.\nPsychotic symptoms occurring at any time during the current major depressive episode.\nCurrent (past 12 months) diagnosis of Panic disorder, [OR] Obsessive Compulsive Disorder, [OR] Posttraumatic Stress Disorder, [OR] Anorexia Nervosa, [OR] or Bulimia Nervosa.\nAlcohol [OR] or Drug Dependence within 12 months [OR] or Abuse within 3 months (excluding nicotine [OR] and caffeine) of baseline visit, as assessed by history [OR] and urine drug screen.\nClinical evidence of a severe Personality Disorder, as assessed by the study psychiatrist, which would impede participation or completion of the trial.\nKnown neurological disorders [OR] or documented serious head injury.\nSerious [OR] and unstable medical illnesses including cardiovascular disease [OR] and cancer.\nActive medical conditions [AND] with known mood changes (endocrine, [OR] autoimmune disorders).\nCurrent diabetes mellitus.\nFor women, pregnancy, [OR] lactation, [OR] or unwillingness to comply with birth control requirements.\nUse of any of the following treatments [OR] or any other alternative therapy within 2 weeks of the pre-treatment PET scan that may have beneficial effects on mood, including St John\'s Wort, [OR] S-adenosyl methionine (SAMe), n-3 fatty acids, [OR] or light therapy.\nUse of antidepressant medication within 1 month of the pre-treatment PET scan (within 5 weeks for fluoxetine [OR] and protryptyline).\nFailure to achieve a much improved status (i.e. equivalent to >50% symptom reduction) with any lifetime treatment course of CBT (defined as a minimum of 4 sessions of a specified manual-driven therapy by a CBT-trained therapist) [OR] or escitalopram (defined as a minimum of 6 weeks of at least 10 mg/day).\nClinically significant active suicidal ideation [OR] or self-injurious behavior necessitating immediate treatment, as determined by the investigator.\nReceived electroconvulsive therapy in the past 6 months [OR] or during the current depressive episode.\nCurrently responding to medication treatment, [NOT] without clinical reasons to change.\nCurrent treatment with weekly individual [OR] or group psychotherapy of any type targeted at depressive symptoms.\nQTc >500 milliseconds on EKG at screening.\nContraindications for MRI, including, but not limited to pacemaker, [OR] aneurysm clips, [OR] neurostimulators, [OR] cochlear implants, [OR] metal in eyes, [OR] steel worker, [OR] intra-uterine devices for birth control.\nMaintenance [OR] or prophylactic therapy for stable medical conditions.\nHypnotic medication prescribed [OR] or approved by the study physician, (up to a three doses per week) for insomnia, as long if [NOT] not the night before a PET/ [OR] MRI or clinic ratings visit. Antipsychotic medications, whether prescribed for sleep [OR] or other indications, are [NOT] prohibited.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Lifetime history of Bipolar Disorder, [OR] Dementia, [OR] Autism Spectrum Disorder, [OR] Schizophrenia, [OR] or any other Psychotic Disorder.
Psychotic symptoms occurring at any time during the current major depressive episode.
Current (past 12 months) diagnosis of Panic disorder, [OR] Obsessive Compulsive Disorder, [OR] Posttraumatic Stress Disorder, [OR] Anorexia Nervosa, [OR] or Bulimia Nervosa.
Alcohol [OR] or Drug Dependence within 12 months [OR] or Abuse within 3 months (excluding nicotine [OR] and caffeine) of baseline visit, as assessed by history [OR] and urine drug screen.
Clinical evidence of a severe Personality Disorder, as assessed by the study psychiatrist, which would impede participation or completion of the trial.
Known neurological disorders [OR] or documented serious head injury.
Serious [OR] and unstable medical illnesses including cardiovascular disease [OR] and cancer.
Active medical conditions [AND] with known mood changes (endocrine, [OR] autoimmune disorders).
Current diabetes mellitus.
For women, pregnancy, [OR] lactation, [OR] or unwillingness to comply with birth control requirements.
Use of any of the following treatments [OR] or any other alternative therapy within 2 weeks of the pre-treatment PET scan that may have beneficial effects on mood, including St John's Wort, [OR] S-adenosyl methionine (SAMe), n-3 fatty acids, [OR] or light therapy.
Use of antidepressant medication within 1 month of the pre-treatment PET scan (within 5 weeks for fluoxetine [OR] and protryptyline).
Failure to achieve a much improved status (i.e. equivalent to >50% symptom reduction) with any lifetime treatment course of CBT (defined as a minimum of 4 sessions of a specified manual-driven therapy by a CBT-trained therapist) [OR] or escitalopram (defined as a minimum of 6 weeks of at least 10 mg/day).
Clinically significant active suicidal ideation [OR] or self-injurious behavior necessitating immediate treatment, as determined by the investigator.
Received electroconvulsive therapy in the past 6 months [OR] or during the current depressive episode.
Currently responding to medication treatment, [NOT] without clinical reasons to change.
Current treatment with weekly individual [OR] or group psychotherapy of any type targeted at depressive symptoms.
QTc >500 milliseconds on EKG at screening.
Contraindications for MRI, including, but not limited to pacemaker, [OR] aneurysm clips, [OR] neurostimulators, [OR] cochlear implants, [OR] metal in eyes, [OR] steel worker, [OR] intra-uterine devices for birth control.
Maintenance [OR] or prophylactic therapy for stable medical conditions.
Hypnotic medication prescribed [OR] or approved by the study physician, (up to a three doses per week) for insomnia, as long if [NOT] not the night before a PET/ [OR] MRI or clinic ratings visit. Antipsychotic medications, whether prescribed for sleep [OR] or other indications, are [NOT] prohibited.
