File: NCT02141061_exc 

Das File: /work/eauten2s/ec_criteria_struct/chia/input/chia_text_half/NCT02141061_exc.txt wurde erfolgreich geladen.
Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\n1. Subject is a post-menopausal woman, defined as either; six (6) months or more (immediately prior to screening visit) without a menstrual period, or prior hysterectomy and/or oophorectomy \n2. Subject is pregnant or lactating or is attempting or expecting to become pregnant during the study \n3. Women with abnormally high liver enzymes or liver disease. (ALT or AST exceeding 2.0 x ULN AND total bilirubin exceeding 1.5 x ULN at screening and confirmed on repeat). \n4. Received an investigational drug in the 30 days prior to the screening for this study \n5. Women with a history of PCOS \n6. Concurrent use of any testosterone, progestin, androgen, estrogen, anabolic steroids, DHEA or hormonal products for at least 2 weeks prior to screening and during the study. \n7. Use of oral contraceptives in the preceding 2 weeks. Use of Depo-Provera® in the preceding 10 months. \n8. Has an IUD in place \n9. Women currently using narcotics \n10. Women currently taking spironolactone \n11. Infectious disease screen is positive for HIV or Hepatitis A, B or C. \n12. Clinically significant abnormal findings on screening examination or any condition which in the opinion of the investigator would interfere with the participant\'s ability to comply with the study instructions or endanger the participant if she took part in the study       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\n 1. Subject is a post-menopausal woman, defined as either; six (6) months [OR] or more (immediately prior to screening visit) [NOT] without a menstrual period, [OR] or prior hysterectomy [OR] and/or oophorectomy \n 2. Subject is pregnant [OR] or lactating [OR] or is attempting [OR] or expecting to become pregnant during the study \n 3. Women [AND] with abnormally high liver enzymes [OR] or liver disease. (ALT [OR] or AST exceeding 2.0 x ULN [AND] AND total bilirubin exceeding 1.5 x ULN at screening [AND] and confirmed on repeat). \n 4. Received an investigational drug in the 30 days prior to the screening for this study \n 5. Women [AND] with a history of PCOS \n 6. Concurrent use of any testosterone, [OR] progestin, [OR] androgen, [OR] estrogen, [OR] anabolic steroids, [OR] DHEA [OR] or hormonal products for at least 2 weeks prior to screening [AND] and during the study. \n 7. Use of oral contraceptives in the preceding 2 weeks. Use of Depo-Provera® in the preceding 10 months. \n 8. Has an IUD in place \n 9. Women currently using narcotics \n 10. Women currently taking spironolactone \n 11. Infectious disease screen is positive for HIV [OR] or Hepatitis A, [OR] B [OR] or C. \n 12. Clinically significant abnormal findings on screening examination [OR] or any condition which in the opinion of the investigator would interfere with the participant\'s ability to comply with the study instructions [OR] or endanger the participant if she took part in the study<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
 1. Subject is a post-menopausal woman, defined as either; six (6) months [OR] or more (immediately prior to screening visit) [NOT] without a menstrual period, [OR] or prior hysterectomy [OR] and/or oophorectomy 
 2. Subject is pregnant [OR] or lactating [OR] or is attempting [OR] or expecting to become pregnant during the study 
 3. Women [AND] with abnormally high liver enzymes [OR] or liver disease. (ALT [OR] or AST exceeding 2.0 x ULN [AND] AND total bilirubin exceeding 1.5 x ULN at screening [AND] and confirmed on repeat). 
 4. Received an investigational drug in the 30 days prior to the screening for this study 
 5. Women [AND] with a history of PCOS 
 6. Concurrent use of any testosterone, [OR] progestin, [OR] androgen, [OR] estrogen, [OR] anabolic steroids, [OR] DHEA [OR] or hormonal products for at least 2 weeks prior to screening [AND] and during the study. 
 7. Use of oral contraceptives in the preceding 2 weeks. Use of Depo-Provera® in the preceding 10 months. 
 8. Has an IUD in place 
 9. Women currently using narcotics 
 10. Women currently taking spironolactone 
 11. Infectious disease screen is positive for HIV [OR] or Hepatitis A, [OR] B [OR] or C. 
 12. Clinically significant abnormal findings on screening examination [OR] or any condition which in the opinion of the investigator would interfere with the participant's ability to comply with the study instructions [OR] or endanger the participant if she took part in the study
