Das File: /work/eauten2s/ec_criteria_struct/chia/input/chia_text_half/NCT02145026_inc.txt wurde erfolgreich geladen.
Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nAdult participants with low or intermediate-1 risk MDS\nNo previous treatment with hematopoietic growth factors within 3 months prior to screening\nSymptomatic anemia (hemoglobin <10 g/dL) as determined by investigator\nSerum erythropoietin <500 milliunits/milliliter (mU/mL) within 14 days prior to the first dose of study treatment\nRequire no red blood cell transfusion or dependent on <4 units within 8 weeks prior to screening\nClinically stable for at least 1 month prior to entry into the study\nFor female participants of childbearing potential and male participants with partners of childbearing potential, agreement (by participants and/or partner) to use highly effective form(s) of contraception\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nAdult participants [AND] with low [OR] or intermediate-1 risk MDS\n [NOT] No previous treatment with hematopoietic growth factors within 3 months prior to screening\nSymptomatic anemia (hemoglobin <10 g/dL) as determined by investigator\nSerum erythropoietin <500 milliunits/milliliter (mU/mL) within 14 days prior to the first dose of study treatment\nRequire [NOT] no red blood cell transfusion [OR] or dependent on <4 units within 8 weeks prior to screening\nClinically stable for at least 1 month prior to entry into the study\nFor female participants of childbearing potential [OR] and male participants with partners of childbearing potential, agreement (by participants and/or partner) to use highly effective form(s) of contraception<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Adult participants [AND] with low [OR] or intermediate-1 risk MDS
 [NOT] No previous treatment with hematopoietic growth factors within 3 months prior to screening
Symptomatic anemia (hemoglobin <10 g/dL) as determined by investigator
Serum erythropoietin <500 milliunits/milliliter (mU/mL) within 14 days prior to the first dose of study treatment
Require [NOT] no red blood cell transfusion [OR] or dependent on <4 units within 8 weeks prior to screening
Clinically stable for at least 1 month prior to entry into the study
For female participants of childbearing potential [OR] and male participants with partners of childbearing potential, agreement (by participants and/or partner) to use highly effective form(s) of contraception
