Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nFemale with a persisting pregnancy of unknown location: \nA pregnancy of unknown location is defined as a pregnancy in a woman with a positive pregnancy test but no definitive signs of pregnancy in the uterus or adnexa on ultrasound imaging. A definitive sign of gestation includes ultrasound visualization of a gestational sac with a yolk sac (with or without an embryo) in the uterus or in the adnexa. Ultrasound must be performed within 7 days prior to randomization. \nPersistence of hCG is defined as at least 2 serial hCG values (over 2-14 days), showing < 15% rise per day, or < 50% fall between the first and last value. \nPatient is hemodynamically stable, hemoglobin >10 mg/dL \nGreater than or 18 years of age \n\n\n### Response:\nFemale [AND] with a persisting pregnancy [AND] of unknown location: \nA pregnancy [AND] of unknown location is defined as a pregnancy in a woman [AND] with a positive pregnancy test [AND] but [NOT] no definitive signs of pregnancy in the uterus [OR] or adnexa on ultrasound imaging. A definitive sign of gestation includes ultrasound visualization of a gestational sac [AND] with a yolk sac (with or without an embryo) in the uterus [OR] or in the adnexa. Ultrasound must be performed within 7 days prior to randomization. \nPersistence of hCG is defined as at least 2 serial hCG values (over 2-14 days), showing < 15% rise per day, [OR] or < 50% fall between the first and last value. \nPatient is hemodynamically stable, hemoglobin >10 mg/dL \nGreater than or 18 years of age<|eot_id|>']
Response: Female [AND] with a persisting pregnancy [AND] of unknown location: 
A pregnancy [AND] of unknown location is defined as a pregnancy in a woman [AND] with a positive pregnancy test [AND] but [NOT] no definitive signs of pregnancy in the uterus [OR] or adnexa on ultrasound imaging. A definitive sign of gestation includes ultrasound visualization of a gestational sac [AND] with a yolk sac (with or without an embryo) in the uterus [OR] or in the adnexa. Ultrasound must be performed within 7 days prior to randomization. 
Persistence of hCG is defined as at least 2 serial hCG values (over 2-14 days), showing < 15% rise per day, [OR] or < 50% fall between the first and last value. 
Patient is hemodynamically stable, hemoglobin >10 mg/dL 
Greater than or 18 years of age
