Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\n1. Diagnosis: Diagnosis of CP secondary to neuronal migration. \n2. Co-morbidities: Medical conditions that may prevent the administration of rehabilitation therapies at the intensity required by the study, or that may compromise the study ability to maintain blindness, or that have a co-morbidity not typically associated with CP (i.e. cancer, cystic fibrosis). \n3. Co-interventions: Anticipated pharmacological intervention or procedure or participation in other studies that may interfere with this study.       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\n1. Diagnosis: Diagnosis of CP secondary to neuronal migration. \n2. Co-morbidities: Medical conditions that may [NOT] prevent the administration of rehabilitation therapies at the intensity required by the study, [OR] or that may compromise the study ability to maintain blindness, [OR] or that have a co-morbidity [NOT] not typically associated with CP (i.e. cancer, [OR] cystic fibrosis). \n3. Co-interventions: Anticipated pharmacological intervention [OR] or procedure [OR] or participation in other studies that may interfere with this study.<|eot_id|>']
Response: 1. Diagnosis: Diagnosis of CP secondary to neuronal migration. 
2. Co-morbidities: Medical conditions that may [NOT] prevent the administration of rehabilitation therapies at the intensity required by the study, [OR] or that may compromise the study ability to maintain blindness, [OR] or that have a co-morbidity [NOT] not typically associated with CP (i.e. cancer, [OR] cystic fibrosis). 
3. Co-interventions: Anticipated pharmacological intervention [OR] or procedure [OR] or participation in other studies that may interfere with this study.
