Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\n1. Age: 12 to 36 months of age (The diagnosis of CP is often uncertain under the age of 12 months. The cutoff at 36 months is to have a population of young children when the brain is most "plastic" and most susceptible to reorganization). \n2. Diagnosis: Diagnosis of spastic CP confirmed by a pediatric neurologist or pediatric rehabilitation specialist. \n3. Etiology: The insult to the central nervous system that caused the motor dysfunction must have occurred during gestation or within one year after birth independent of gestational age. \n4. Disease severity level: Gross Motor Function Classification System (GMFCS) levels I, II and III. \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\n 1. Age: 12 to 36 months of age (The diagnosis of CP is often uncertain under the age of 12 months. The cutoff at 36 months is to have a population of young children [AND] when the brain is most "plastic" [AND] and most susceptible to reorganization). \n 2. Diagnosis: Diagnosis of spastic CP confirmed by a pediatric neurologist [OR] or pediatric rehabilitation specialist. \n 3. Etiology: The insult to the central nervous system that caused the motor dysfunction must have occurred during gestation [OR] or within one year after birth independent of gestational age. \n 4. Disease severity level: Gross Motor Function Classification System (GMFCS) levels I, II and III.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
 1. Age: 12 to 36 months of age (The diagnosis of CP is often uncertain under the age of 12 months. The cutoff at 36 months is to have a population of young children [AND] when the brain is most "plastic" [AND] and most susceptible to reorganization). 
 2. Diagnosis: Diagnosis of spastic CP confirmed by a pediatric neurologist [OR] or pediatric rehabilitation specialist. 
 3. Etiology: The insult to the central nervous system that caused the motor dysfunction must have occurred during gestation [OR] or within one year after birth independent of gestational age. 
 4. Disease severity level: Gross Motor Function Classification System (GMFCS) levels I, II and III.
