Have Paget\'s disease, heart disease, uncontrolled hypertension, renal disease, or other concomitant conditions that prohibit participation in exercises, risedronate therapy, or use of CaD supplements.       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nHave osteoporosis \nHave a 10 yr probability of hip fracture >3% [OR] or major fracture >20% based on results of the FRAX tool \nCurrently take bisphosphonates, [OR] estrogen replacement therapy, [OR] glucocorticosteroids, [OR] or other drugs affecting bone \nCurrently participate in a resistance training [OR] or high impact weight bearing exercise program two or more times weekly \nWeigh >300 lbs \nHave abnormal results for the following laboratory tests: serum 25(OH)D; serum creatinine; serum calcium; PTH; TSH \nHave Paget\'s disease, [OR] heart disease, uncontrolled hypertension, [OR] renal disease, [OR] or other concomitant conditions that [NOT] prohibit participation in exercises, [OR] risedronate therapy, [OR] or use of CaD supplements.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Have osteoporosis 
Have a 10 yr probability of hip fracture >3% [OR] or major fracture >20% based on results of the FRAX tool 
Currently take bisphosphonates, [OR] estrogen replacement therapy, [OR] glucocorticosteroids, [OR] or other drugs affecting bone 
Currently participate in a resistance training [OR] or high impact weight bearing exercise program two or more times weekly 
Weigh >300 lbs 
Have abnormal results for the following laboratory tests: serum 25(OH)D; serum creatinine; serum calcium; PTH; TSH 
Have Paget's disease, [OR] heart disease, uncontrolled hypertension, [OR] renal disease, [OR] or other concomitant conditions that [NOT] prohibit participation in exercises, [OR] risedronate therapy, [OR] or use of CaD supplements.
