 Contraceptive pills\nIntraoperative use of vasopressin and uterine tourniquet is permissible\nCan have had prior Cesarean delivery\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nPatients presenting for abdominal myomectomy [AND] with documented uterine fibroids on pelvic imaging (pelvic ultrasound [OR] or MRI) within in last 12 months\nAge = 18 years [AND] and = 50 years\nPre-operative hemoglobin >8 g/dl\nWilling to have buccal administration of misoprostol [OR] or a placebo at least one hour pre-procedure.\nAbility to understand and the willingness to sign a written informed consent.\nAdmissible medical/ [OR] surgical history\nCan be previously treated with Depo-Lupron, [OR] Depo-Provera, [OR] or Oral Contraceptive pills\nIntraoperative use of vasopressin [OR] and uterine tourniquet is permissible\nCan have had prior Cesarean delivery<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Patients presenting for abdominal myomectomy [AND] with documented uterine fibroids on pelvic imaging (pelvic ultrasound [OR] or MRI) within in last 12 months
Age = 18 years [AND] and = 50 years
Pre-operative hemoglobin >8 g/dl
Willing to have buccal administration of misoprostol [OR] or a placebo at least one hour pre-procedure.
Ability to understand and the willingness to sign a written informed consent.
Admissible medical/ [OR] surgical history
Can be previously treated with Depo-Lupron, [OR] Depo-Provera, [OR] or Oral Contraceptive pills
Intraoperative use of vasopressin [OR] and uterine tourniquet is permissible
Can have had prior Cesarean delivery
