Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\n    \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\n  -  Biopsy confirmed diagnosis of SNIP and scheduled to undergo surgical resection;\n  -  Age ≥ 18 years;\n  -  Written informed consent;\n  -  Mentally competent person that is able and willing to comply with study procedures.\nExclusion Criteria:\n  -  Medical or psychiatric conditions that compromise the patient\'s ability to give informed consent;\n  -  Concurrent uncontrolled medical conditions;\n  -  Received an investigational drug within 30 days prior to the dose of bevacizumab-IRDye800CW;\n  -  Tumors at sites of which the surgeon would assess that in vivo imaging would not be feasible;\n  -  History of myocardial infarction, cerebrovascular accident, uncontrolled cardiac heart failure, significant liver disease or unstable angina within 6 months prior to enrollment;\n  -  Inadequately controlled hypertension with or without current antihypertensive medications;\n  -  History of infusion reactions to bevacizumab or other monoclonal antibody therapies;\n  -  Pregnant or lactating women. Documentation of a negative pregnancy test must be available for women of childbearing potential. Woman of childbearing potential are premenopausal women with intact reproductive organs and women less than two years after menopause;\n  -  Lab values that in the opinion of the primary surgeon would prevent surgical resection;\n  -  Life expectancy < 12 weeks;\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\n - Biopsy confirmed diagnosis of SNIP [AND] and scheduled to undergo surgical resection;\n - Age ≥ 18 years;\n - Written informed consent;\n - Mentally competent person that is able and willing to comply with study procedures.\nExclusion Criteria:\n - Medical [OR] or psychiatric conditions that compromise the patient\'s ability to give informed consent;\n - Concurrent uncontrolled medical conditions;\n - Received an investigational drug within 30 days prior to the dose of bevacizumab-IRDye800CW;\n - Tumors at sites of which the surgeon would assess that in vivo imaging would [NOT] not be feasible;\n - History of myocardial infarction, [OR] cerebrovascular accident, uncontrolled cardiac heart failure, significant liver disease [OR] or unstable angina within 6 months prior to enrollment;\n - Inadequately controlled hypertension with or without current antihypertensive medications;\n - History of infusion reactions to bevacizumab [OR] or other monoclonal antibody therapies;\n - Pregnant [OR] or lactating women. Documentation of a negative pregnancy test must be available for women of childbearing potential. Woman of childbearing potential [AND] are premenopausal women [AND] with intact reproductive organs [AND] and women less than two years after menopause;\n - Lab values that in the opinion of the primary surgeon would [NOT] prevent surgical resection;\n - Life expectancy < 12 weeks;<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
  -  Biopsy confirmed diagnosis of SNIP and scheduled to undergo surgical resection;
  -  Age ≥ 18 years;
  -  Written informed consent;
  -  Mentally competent person that is able and willing to comply with study procedures.
Exclusion Criteria:
  -  Medical or psychiatric conditions that compromise the patient's ability to give informed consent;
  -  Concurrent uncontrolled medical conditions;
  -  Received an investigational drug within 30 days prior to the dose of bevacizumab-IRDye800CW;
  -  Tumors at sites of which the surgeon would assess that in vivo imaging would not be feasible;
  -  History of myocardial infarction, cerebrovascular accident, uncontrolled cardiac heart failure, significant liver disease or unstable angina within 6 months prior to enrollment;
  -  Inadequately controlled hypertension with or without current antihypertensive medications;
  -  History of infusion reactions to bevacizumab or other monoclonal antibody therapies;
  -  Pregnant or lactating women. Documentation of a negative pregnancy test must be available for women of childbearing potential. Woman of childbearing potential are premenopausal women with intact reproductive organs and women less than two years after menopause;
  -  Lab values that in the opinion of the primary surgeon would prevent surgical resection;
  -  Life expectancy < 12 weeks;
