File: NCT02243553_exc 

Das File: /work/eauten2s/ec_criteria_struct/chia/input/chia_text_half/NCT02243553_exc.txt wurde erfolgreich geladen.
Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\n1. History or presence of allergy to the study drugs or their components or drugs of their class, or a history of drug or other allergy that, in the opinion of the physician responsible, contraindicates their participation \n2. Any finding of the medical examination (including blood pressure, pulse rate and electrocardiogram) deviating from normal and of clinical relevance \n3. History or diagnosis of any significant medical conditions: Including but not limited to gastrointestinal, hepatic, renal, respiratory, cardiovascular, metabolic, immunologic, hematological, psychiatric, neurological, oncological or hormonal disorders \n4. Known elevated liver enzymes in past clinical trials with any compound (experimental or marketed) \n5. Clinically relevant laboratory abnormalities (e.g. Hgb<11g/dL, Hct<30g/dL, total cholesterol >240mg/dL, triglycerides >500mg/dL, fasting glucose >130mg/dL, liver function tests >2.5x upper limit of normal, baseline international normalized ratio >1.2) \n6. History of evidence of clinically significant hepatic, cardiac, pulmonary, endocrine, immunological, gastrointestinal, hematological, vascular or collagen disease \n7. History of alcohol abuse or use of any illicit drugs \n8. Unable to abstain from more than one beer or alcohol equivalent per day for the duration of the study \n9. Use of tobacco products and/or history of smoking within the past 2 months \n10. Pregnant or breast feeding \n11. Sexually active women of childbearing age who do not use an acceptable barrier method of birth control \n12. Hypersensitivity to caffeine, warfarin, vitamin K, omeprazole, dextromethorphan, midazolam, tipranavir, ritonavir or their excipients \n13. Concomitant treatment with other experimental compounds \n14. Concomitant administration of any prescription or over the counter medications known to alter P450 enzyme or P-gp activity \n15. Concomitant administration of any prescription or over the counter medications known to be highly dependent on P450 or P-gp for clearance for which elevated plasma concentrations are known to be associated with serious toxicity \n16. Concomitant administration of any food product known to alter P450 enzyme or P-gp activity such as grapefruit juice, Seville oranges \n17. Concomitant administration of any drug that could affect bleeding (e.g., aspirin, clopidogrel, ticlopidine, warfarin, heparin, low-molecular weight heparin) \n18. Concomitant administration of oral contraceptives (may be included with 7-day washout period) \n19. Concomitant administration of any herbal medications \n20. Inadequate venous access \n21. Renal or hepatic insufficiency \n22. Clinically unacceptable result at the screening physical examination \n23. Use of investigational medications within 30 days before study entry \n24. HIV-positive \n25. Body Mass Index (BMI) > 30 kg/m²       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\n1. History [OR] or presence of allergy to the study drugs [OR] or their components [OR] or drugs of their class, [OR] or a history of drug [OR] or other allergy that, in the opinion of the physician responsible, contraindicates their participation \n2. Any finding of the medical examination (including blood pressure, [OR] pulse rate [OR] and electrocardiogram) deviating from normal [AND] and of clinical relevance \n3. History [OR] or diagnosis of any significant medical conditions: Including but not limited to gastrointestinal, [OR] hepatic, [OR] renal, [OR] respiratory, [OR] cardiovascular, [OR] metabolic, [OR] immunologic, [OR] hematological, [OR] psychiatric, [OR] neurological, [OR] oncological [OR] or hormonal disorders \n4. Known elevated liver enzymes in past clinical trials [AND] with any compound (experimental [OR] or marketed) \n5. Clinically relevant laboratory abnormalities (e.g. Hgb<11g/dL, [OR] Hct<30g/dL, total cholesterol >240mg/dL, [OR] triglycerides >500mg/dL, [OR] fasting glucose >130mg/dL, liver function tests >2.5x upper limit of normal, baseline international normalized ratio >1.2) \n6. History of evidence of clinically significant hepatic, [OR] cardiac, [OR] pulmonary, [OR] endocrine, [OR] immunological, [OR] gastrointestinal, [OR] hematological, [OR] vascular [OR] or collagen disease \n7. History of alcohol abuse [OR] or use of any illicit drugs \n8. [NOT] Unable to abstain from more than one beer [OR] or alcohol equivalent per day for the duration of the study \n9. Use of tobacco products [OR] and/or history of smoking within the past 2 months \n10. Pregnant [OR] or breast feeding \n11. Sexually active women [AND] of childbearing age [AND] who do [NOT] not use an acceptable barrier method of birth control \n12. Hypersensitivity to caffeine, [OR] warfarin, [OR] vitamin K, [OR] omeprazole, [OR] dextromethorphan, [OR] midazolam, [OR] tipranavir, [OR] ritonavir [OR] or their excipients \n13. Concomitant treatment with other experimental compounds \n14. Concomitant administration of any prescription [OR] or over the counter medications known to alter P450 enzyme [OR] or P-gp activity \n15. Concomitant administration of any prescription [OR] or over the counter medications known to be highly dependent on P450 [OR] or P-gp for clearance for which elevated plasma concentrations are known to be associated with serious toxicity \n16. Concomitant administration of any food product known to alter P450 enzyme [OR] or P-gp activity such as grapefruit juice, [OR] Seville oranges \n17. Concomitant administration of any drug that could affect bleeding (e.g., aspirin, [OR] clopidogrel, [OR] ticlopidine, [OR] warfarin, [OR] heparin, [OR] low-molecular weight heparin) \n18. Concomitant administration of oral contraceptives (may be included with 7-day washout period) \n19. Concomitant administration of any herbal medications \n20. Inadequate venous access \n21. Renal [OR] or hepatic insufficiency \n22. Clinically unacceptable result at the screening physical examination \n23. Use of investigational medications within 30 days before study entry \n24. HIV-positive \n25. Body Mass Index (BMI) > 30 kg/m²<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
1. History [OR] or presence of allergy to the study drugs [OR] or their components [OR] or drugs of their class, [OR] or a history of drug [OR] or other allergy that, in the opinion of the physician responsible, contraindicates their participation 
2. Any finding of the medical examination (including blood pressure, [OR] pulse rate [OR] and electrocardiogram) deviating from normal [AND] and of clinical relevance 
3. History [OR] or diagnosis of any significant medical conditions: Including but not limited to gastrointestinal, [OR] hepatic, [OR] renal, [OR] respiratory, [OR] cardiovascular, [OR] metabolic, [OR] immunologic, [OR] hematological, [OR] psychiatric, [OR] neurological, [OR] oncological [OR] or hormonal disorders 
4. Known elevated liver enzymes in past clinical trials [AND] with any compound (experimental [OR] or marketed) 
5. Clinically relevant laboratory abnormalities (e.g. Hgb<11g/dL, [OR] Hct<30g/dL, total cholesterol >240mg/dL, [OR] triglycerides >500mg/dL, [OR] fasting glucose >130mg/dL, liver function tests >2.5x upper limit of normal, baseline international normalized ratio >1.2) 
6. History of evidence of clinically significant hepatic, [OR] cardiac, [OR] pulmonary, [OR] endocrine, [OR] immunological, [OR] gastrointestinal, [OR] hematological, [OR] vascular [OR] or collagen disease 
7. History of alcohol abuse [OR] or use of any illicit drugs 
8. [NOT] Unable to abstain from more than one beer [OR] or alcohol equivalent per day for the duration of the study 
9. Use of tobacco products [OR] and/or history of smoking within the past 2 months 
10. Pregnant [OR] or breast feeding 
11. Sexually active women [AND] of childbearing age [AND] who do [NOT] not use an acceptable barrier method of birth control 
12. Hypersensitivity to caffeine, [OR] warfarin, [OR] vitamin K, [OR] omeprazole, [OR] dextromethorphan, [OR] midazolam, [OR] tipranavir, [OR] ritonavir [OR] or their excipients 
13. Concomitant treatment with other experimental compounds 
14. Concomitant administration of any prescription [OR] or over the counter medications known to alter P450 enzyme [OR] or P-gp activity 
15. Concomitant administration of any prescription [OR] or over the counter medications known to be highly dependent on P450 [OR] or P-gp for clearance for which elevated plasma concentrations are known to be associated with serious toxicity 
16. Concomitant administration of any food product known to alter P450 enzyme [OR] or P-gp activity such as grapefruit juice, [OR] Seville oranges 
17. Concomitant administration of any drug that could affect bleeding (e.g., aspirin, [OR] clopidogrel, [OR] ticlopidine, [OR] warfarin, [OR] heparin, [OR] low-molecular weight heparin) 
18. Concomitant administration of oral contraceptives (may be included with 7-day washout period) 
19. Concomitant administration of any herbal medications 
20. Inadequate venous access 
21. Renal [OR] or hepatic insufficiency 
22. Clinically unacceptable result at the screening physical examination 
23. Use of investigational medications within 30 days before study entry 
24. HIV-positive 
25. Body Mass Index (BMI) > 30 kg/m²
