File: NCT02243553_inc 

Das File: /work/eauten2s/ec_criteria_struct/chia/input/chia_text_half/NCT02243553_inc.txt wurde erfolgreich geladen.
Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\n1. Signed informed consent \n2. Healthy subjects aged between 18 years and 45 years inclusive \n3. Weighing at least 50 kg \n4. Volunteers must be hospitalized on Days 1-4, 7-9, and 17-20 for pharmacokinetic assessments for each biomarker and TPV/r (Days 7-9 and 17-20) \n5. Volunteers must be willing to complete all study-related activities \n6. Each volunteer must have a valid social security number \n7. Each volunteer must have acceptable medical history, physical examination and laboratory test \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\n 1. Signed informed consent \n 2. Healthy subjects aged between 18 years and 45 years inclusive \n 3. Weighing at least 50 kg \n 4. Volunteers must be hospitalized on Days 1-4, 7-9, and 17-20 for pharmacokinetic assessments for each biomarker [AND] and TPV/r (Days 7-9 [AND] and 17-20) \n 5. Volunteers must be willing to complete all study-related activities \n 6. Each volunteer must have a valid social security number \n 7. Each volunteer must have acceptable medical history, [OR] physical examination [OR] and laboratory test \n\nExclusion Criteria:\n 1. Pregnancy \n 2. Breastfeeding \n 3. HIV infection \n 4. Hepatitis B or C infection \n 5. Any medical condition or illness \n 6. Use of any medication \n 7. History of allergy to TPV/r \n 8. Lactose intolerance \n 9. Any condition that, in the view of the Investigator, the medical record of the volunteer in the duration of observation is not reliable, or not accessible.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
 1. Signed informed consent 
 2. Healthy subjects aged between 18 years and 45 years inclusive 
 3. Weighing at least 50 kg 
 4. Volunteers must be hospitalized on Days 1-4, 7-9, and 17-20 for pharmacokinetic assessments for each biomarker [AND] and TPV/r (Days 7-9 [AND] and 17-20) 
 5. Volunteers must be willing to complete all study-related activities 
 6. Each volunteer must have a valid social security number 
 7. Each volunteer must have acceptable medical history, [OR] physical examination [OR] and laboratory test 

Exclusion Criteria:
 1. Pregnancy 
 2. Breastfeeding 
 3. HIV infection 
 4. Hepatitis B or C infection 
 5. Any medical condition or illness 
 6. Use of any medication 
 7. History of allergy to TPV/r 
 8. Lactose intolerance 
 9. Any condition that, in the view of the Investigator, the medical record of the volunteer in the duration of observation is not reliable, or not accessible.
