Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nPreoperative use of an anticoagulant (Plavix, warfarin, lovenox, etc.)\nHistory of hypersensitivity to EACA\nHistory of thromboembolic event (e.g., PE or DVT)\nHistory of renal insufficiency or failure\nCongenital or acquired coagulopathy as evidence by INR >1.4 or PTT > 1.4 times normal, or Platelets <150,000/mm3 on preoperative laboratory testing\nUse of hormone replacement therapy or hormonal contraceptive agents within days prior to surgery\nUse of acetylsalicylic acid (ASA), antiplatelet agents within 7 days prior to surgery\nPregnant\nBreastfeeding\nNot received neuraxial anesthesia\n\n\n### Response:\nPreoperative use of an anticoagulant (Plavix, [OR] warfarin, [OR] lovenox, etc.)\nHistory of hypersensitivity to EACA\nHistory of thromboembolic event (e.g., PE [OR] or DVT)\n History of renal insufficiency [OR] or failure\nCongenital [OR] or acquired coagulopathy as evidence by INR >1.4 [OR] or PTT > 1.4 times normal, [OR] or Platelets <150,000/mm3 on preoperative laboratory testing\nUse of hormone replacement therapy [OR] or hormonal contraceptive agents within days prior to surgery\nUse of acetylsalicylic acid (ASA), antiplatelet agents within 7 days prior to surgery\nPregnant\nBreastfeeding\n [NOT] Not received neuraxial anesthesia<|eot_id|>']
Response: Preoperative use of an anticoagulant (Plavix, [OR] warfarin, [OR] lovenox, etc.)
History of hypersensitivity to EACA
History of thromboembolic event (e.g., PE [OR] or DVT)
 History of renal insufficiency [OR] or failure
Congenital [OR] or acquired coagulopathy as evidence by INR >1.4 [OR] or PTT > 1.4 times normal, [OR] or Platelets <150,000/mm3 on preoperative laboratory testing
Use of hormone replacement therapy [OR] or hormonal contraceptive agents within days prior to surgery
Use of acetylsalicylic acid (ASA), antiplatelet agents within 7 days prior to surgery
Pregnant
Breastfeeding
 [NOT] Not received neuraxial anesthesia
