Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nParticipant has a clinically significant abnormal physical examination, vital signs or 12 lead ECG (including QTc greater than (>) 450msec, Left Bundle Branch Block, permanent pacemaker or implantable cardioverter defibrillator) at Screening or admission \nParticipant has a history of or current liver or renal insufficiency; significant cardiac, vascular, pulmonary, gastrointestinal, endocrine, neurologic, hematologic, rheumatologic, psychiatric, or metabolic disturbances \nUse of any prescription or over-the-counter medication, herbal medication, vitamins, or mineral supplements within 14 days prior to study drug administration (not including paracetamol). Medication for chronic use in age related disease will be allowed after approval by both the investigator and to the sponsor. No change in dose or regimen will be permitted during the study that is, from the Screening visit until the follow-up visit \nParticipant has a history of spontaneous, prolonged or severe bleeding of unclear origin \nParticipant has a history of epilepsy or fits or unexplained black-outs other than vasovagal collapse       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nParticipant has a clinically significant abnormal physical examination, [OR] vital signs [OR] or 12 lead ECG (including QTc greater than (>) 450msec, Left Bundle Branch Block, permanent pacemaker [OR] or implantable cardioverter defibrillator) at Screening [OR] or admission \nParticipant has a history [OR] of or current liver [OR] or renal insufficiency; significant cardiac, [OR] vascular, [OR] pulmonary, [OR] gastrointestinal, [OR] endocrine, [OR] neurologic, [OR] hematologic, [OR] rheumatologic, [OR] psychiatric, [OR] or metabolic disturbances \nUse of any prescription [OR] or over-the-counter medication, [OR] herbal medication, [OR] vitamins, [OR] or mineral supplements within 14 days prior to study drug administration (not including paracetamol). Medication for chronic use in age related disease will be allowed after approval by both the investigator and to the sponsor. [NOT] No change in dose [OR] or regimen will be permitted during the study that is, from the Screening visit until the follow-up visit \nParticipant has a history of spontaneous, [OR] prolonged [OR] or severe bleeding [NOT] of unclear origin \nParticipant has a history of epilepsy [OR] or fits [OR] or unexplained black-outs other than vasovagal collapse<|eot_id|>']
Response: Participant has a clinically significant abnormal physical examination, [OR] vital signs [OR] or 12 lead ECG (including QTc greater than (>) 450msec, Left Bundle Branch Block, permanent pacemaker [OR] or implantable cardioverter defibrillator) at Screening [OR] or admission 
Participant has a history [OR] of or current liver [OR] or renal insufficiency; significant cardiac, [OR] vascular, [OR] pulmonary, [OR] gastrointestinal, [OR] endocrine, [OR] neurologic, [OR] hematologic, [OR] rheumatologic, [OR] psychiatric, [OR] or metabolic disturbances 
Use of any prescription [OR] or over-the-counter medication, [OR] herbal medication, [OR] vitamins, [OR] or mineral supplements within 14 days prior to study drug administration (not including paracetamol). Medication for chronic use in age related disease will be allowed after approval by both the investigator and to the sponsor. [NOT] No change in dose [OR] or regimen will be permitted during the study that is, from the Screening visit until the follow-up visit 
Participant has a history of spontaneous, [OR] prolonged [OR] or severe bleeding [NOT] of unclear origin 
Participant has a history of epilepsy [OR] or fits [OR] or unexplained black-outs other than vasovagal collapse
