Das File: /work/eauten2s/ec_criteria_struct/chia/input/chia_text_half/NCT02301039_exc.txt wurde erfolgreich geladen.
Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nPrior systemic therapy targeting PD-1: PD-L1 axis. \nPatients who are curable by conventional multidisciplinary management. \nPatients with severe and/or uncontrolled concurrent medical disease that in the opinion of the investigator could cause unacceptable safety risks or compromise compliance with the protocol. \nPatients who have received wide field radiotherapy ≤ 4 weeks or limited field radiation for palliation < 2 weeks prior to screening or who have not recovered adequately from side effects of such therapy. \nPatients who have active infections requiring therapy. \nPatients that are known to be positive for Human Immunodeficiency Virus (HIV) (HIV 1/2 antibodies), active Hepatitis B (HBsAg reactive), or Hepatitis C (HCV RNA [qualitative] is detected); patients with negative Hepatitis C antibody testing may not need RNA testing. \nPatients that have a known psychiatric or substance abuse disorder that would interfere with cooperation with the requirements of the trial. \nPatients who received systemic anti-cancer treatment prior to the first dose of study drug within the following time frames: \nPatients with active autoimmune disease or a documented history of autoimmune disease or syndrome that requires systemic steroids or immunosuppressive agents. Patients with vitiligo or resolved childhood asthma/atopy would be exception to this rule. Patients that require inhaled steroids or local steroid injections would not be excluded from the study. Patients with hypothyroidism not from autoimmune disease that is stable on hormone replacement will not be excluded from the study. \nWomen who are pregnant or nursing/breastfeeding. \nKnown hypersensitivity to pembrolizumab or another mAb. \nHas a history of (non-infectious) pneumonitis that required steroids or current pneumonitis. \nPatients with untreated central nervous system disease. Patients with controlled treated CNS lesions who have undergone surgery or stereotactic radiosurgery and stable for 4 weeks are eligible. \nInability to comply with protocol required procedures. \nPatients with medical conditions that require chronic systemic corticosteroid therapy or require any other form of immunosuppressive medication. However, patients using physiologic replacement doses of hydrocortisone, or its equivalent, will be considered eligible for this study: up to 20 mg hydrocortisone (or 5 mg of prednisone) in the morning and 10 mg hydrocortisone (or 2.5 mg prednisone) in the evening. \nPatients with the risk factors for bowel obstruction or bowel perforation (examples include but not limited to a history of acute diverticulitis, intra-abdominal abscess, abdominal carcinomatosis). \nPatients who have received a live vaccine within 30 days prior to the first dose of trial treatment.       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nPrior systemic therapy targeting PD-1: PD-L1 axis.\nExclusion Criteria:\nPatients who are curable by conventional multidisciplinary management.\nPatients with severe [OR] and/or uncontrolled concurrent medical disease that in the opinion of the investigator could cause unacceptable safety risks [OR] or compromise compliance with the protocol.\nPatients who have received wide field radiotherapy ≤ 4 weeks [OR] or limited field radiation for palliation < 2 weeks prior to screening [OR] or who have [NOT] not recovered adequately from side effects of such therapy.\n Patients who have active infections requiring therapy.\n Patients that are known to be positive for Human Immunodeficiency Virus (HIV) (HIV 1/2 antibodies), active Hepatitis B (HBsAg reactive), [OR] or Hepatitis C (HCV RNA [qualitative] is detected); patients with negative Hepatitis C antibody testing may [NOT] not need RNA testing.\n Patients that have a known psychiatric [OR] or substance abuse disorder that would interfere with cooperation with the requirements of the trial.\n Patients who received systemic anti-cancer treatment prior to the first dose of study drug within the following time frames:\nPatients with active autoimmune disease [OR] or a documented history of autoimmune disease [OR] or syndrome that requires systemic steroids [OR] or immunosuppressive agents. Patients with vitiligo [OR] or resolved childhood asthma/ [OR] atopy would be exception to this rule. Patients that require inhaled steroids [OR] or local steroid injections would [NOT] not be excluded from the study. Patients with hypothyroidism [NOT] not from autoimmune disease that is stable on hormone replacement will [NOT] not be excluded from the study.\n Women [AND] who are pregnant [OR] or nursing/ [OR] breastfeeding.\n Known hypersensitivity to pembrolizumab [OR] or another mAb.\n Has a history of (non-infectious) pneumonitis that required steroids [OR] or current pneumonitis.\n Patients with [NOT] untreated central nervous system disease. Patients with controlled treated CNS lesions [AND] who have undergone surgery [OR] or stereotactic radiosurgery [AND] and stable for 4 weeks are eligible.\n Inability to comply with protocol required procedures.\n Patients with medical conditions that require chronic systemic corticosteroid therapy [OR] or require any other form of immunosuppressive medication. However, patients using physiologic replacement doses of hydrocortisone, [OR] or its equivalent, will be considered eligible for this study: up to 20 mg hydrocortisone [OR] (or 5 mg of prednisone) in the morning [AND] and 10 mg hydrocortisone [OR] (or 2.5 mg prednisone) in the evening.\n Patients with the risk factors for bowel obstruction [OR] or bowel perforation (examples include but not limited to a history of acute diverticulitis, [OR] intra-abdominal abscess, [OR] abdominal carcinomatosis).\n Patients who have received a live vaccine within 30 days prior to the first dose of trial treatment.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Prior systemic therapy targeting PD-1: PD-L1 axis.
Exclusion Criteria:
Patients who are curable by conventional multidisciplinary management.
Patients with severe [OR] and/or uncontrolled concurrent medical disease that in the opinion of the investigator could cause unacceptable safety risks [OR] or compromise compliance with the protocol.
Patients who have received wide field radiotherapy ≤ 4 weeks [OR] or limited field radiation for palliation < 2 weeks prior to screening [OR] or who have [NOT] not recovered adequately from side effects of such therapy.
 Patients who have active infections requiring therapy.
 Patients that are known to be positive for Human Immunodeficiency Virus (HIV) (HIV 1/2 antibodies), active Hepatitis B (HBsAg reactive), [OR] or Hepatitis C (HCV RNA [qualitative] is detected); patients with negative Hepatitis C antibody testing may [NOT] not need RNA testing.
 Patients that have a known psychiatric [OR] or substance abuse disorder that would interfere with cooperation with the requirements of the trial.
 Patients who received systemic anti-cancer treatment prior to the first dose of study drug within the following time frames:
Patients with active autoimmune disease [OR] or a documented history of autoimmune disease [OR] or syndrome that requires systemic steroids [OR] or immunosuppressive agents. Patients with vitiligo [OR] or resolved childhood asthma/ [OR] atopy would be exception to this rule. Patients that require inhaled steroids [OR] or local steroid injections would [NOT] not be excluded from the study. Patients with hypothyroidism [NOT] not from autoimmune disease that is stable on hormone replacement will [NOT] not be excluded from the study.
 Women [AND] who are pregnant [OR] or nursing/ [OR] breastfeeding.
 Known hypersensitivity to pembrolizumab [OR] or another mAb.
 Has a history of (non-infectious) pneumonitis that required steroids [OR] or current pneumonitis.
 Patients with [NOT] untreated central nervous system disease. Patients with controlled treated CNS lesions [AND] who have undergone surgery [OR] or stereotactic radiosurgery [AND] and stable for 4 weeks are eligible.
 Inability to comply with protocol required procedures.
 Patients with medical conditions that require chronic systemic corticosteroid therapy [OR] or require any other form of immunosuppressive medication. However, patients using physiologic replacement doses of hydrocortisone, [OR] or its equivalent, will be considered eligible for this study: up to 20 mg hydrocortisone [OR] (or 5 mg of prednisone) in the morning [AND] and 10 mg hydrocortisone [OR] (or 2.5 mg prednisone) in the evening.
 Patients with the risk factors for bowel obstruction [OR] or bowel perforation (examples include but not limited to a history of acute diverticulitis, [OR] intra-abdominal abscess, [OR] abdominal carcinomatosis).
 Patients who have received a live vaccine within 30 days prior to the first dose of trial treatment.
