Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nDiagnosed epileptic patients of either sex with age between 10-19 yrs (<19yrs), coming to the medicine Out Patient /In Patient Departments and undergoing AED therapy for more than 6 months. \nEpileptics with high homocysteine levels i.e. > 10.9 µmol/L (Normal homocysteine levels are 4.3-9.9 µmol/L for male and 3.3-7.2 µmol/L for female adolescent and a high homocysteine concentration is deaned as at least 11.4 µmol/L for male and at least 10.4 µmol/L for female. Gender mean of high homocysteine concentration is 10.9 µmol/L) [5] \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nDiagnosed epileptic patients of either sex [AND] with age between 10-19 yrs (<19yrs), coming to the medicine Out Patient /In Patient Departments [AND] and undergoing AED therapy for more than 6 months. \nEpileptics [AND] with high homocysteine levels i.e. > 10.9 µmol/L (Normal homocysteine levels are 4.3-9.9 µmol/L [AND] for male [AND] and 3.3-7.2 µmol/L for female adolescent [AND] and a high homocysteine concentration is deaned as at least 11.4 µmol/L [AND] for male [AND] and at least 10.4 µmol/L for female. Gender mean of high homocysteine concentration is 10.9 µmol/L) [5]<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Diagnosed epileptic patients of either sex [AND] with age between 10-19 yrs (<19yrs), coming to the medicine Out Patient /In Patient Departments [AND] and undergoing AED therapy for more than 6 months. 
Epileptics [AND] with high homocysteine levels i.e. > 10.9 µmol/L (Normal homocysteine levels are 4.3-9.9 µmol/L [AND] for male [AND] and 3.3-7.2 µmol/L for female adolescent [AND] and a high homocysteine concentration is deaned as at least 11.4 µmol/L [AND] for male [AND] and at least 10.4 µmol/L for female. Gender mean of high homocysteine concentration is 10.9 µmol/L) [5]
