75y \nPerformed intraoperative ablation \nUnresectable tumor during operation \nAllergic reactions against fish or egg proteins       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nContraindication for hepatectomy, including gastrointestinal hemorrhage, severe hemorrhagic disorders, explicit acute [NOT] nonspecific infectious lesion, overt ascites, Child-Pugh Score C, indocyanine green retention rate at 15min (ICGR15)＞30%(12), serum hepatitis B virus (HBV)-DNA＞126 copies/ml [AND] and serum alanine aminotransferase (ALT) ＞ 2×ULN, serum triglycerides＞2.0 mmol/L, circulatory shock, [OR] stroke, [OR] acute myocardial infarction, [OR] renal failure, [OR] coma of unknown cause \nPregnancy \nAge of＜18y [OR] or＞75y \nPerformed intraoperative ablation \nUnresectable tumor during operation \nAllergic reactions against fish [OR] or egg proteins<|eot_id|>']
Response: Contraindication for hepatectomy, including gastrointestinal hemorrhage, severe hemorrhagic disorders, explicit acute [NOT] nonspecific infectious lesion, overt ascites, Child-Pugh Score C, indocyanine green retention rate at 15min (ICGR15)＞30%(12), serum hepatitis B virus (HBV)-DNA＞126 copies/ml [AND] and serum alanine aminotransferase (ALT) ＞ 2×ULN, serum triglycerides＞2.0 mmol/L, circulatory shock, [OR] stroke, [OR] acute myocardial infarction, [OR] renal failure, [OR] coma of unknown cause 
Pregnancy 
Age of＜18y [OR] or＞75y 
Performed intraoperative ablation 
Unresectable tumor during operation 
Allergic reactions against fish [OR] or egg proteins
