Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nCurrent or past diagnoses of other Axis I psychiatric disorders, except for generalized anxiety disorder (GAD) symptoms occurring during a depressive episode\nHistory of alcohol or drug dependence or abuse in the last three years\nHistory of developmental disorder or IQ score < 70\nPresence of acute suicidality\nAcute grief (< 1 month)\nCurrent or past psychosis\nPrimary neurological disorder, including but not limited to dementia, stroke, brain tumors, epilepsy, Parkinson\'s disease, or demyelinating diseases\nMRI contraindications\nAny physical or intellectual disability adversely affecting ability to complete assessments\nElectroconvulsive therapy in last 6 months\nUse of antidepressant medications or other psychotropic medications in the last 4 weeks (or the last 6 weeks for fluoxetine). Occasional use of benzodiazepines or non-benzodiazepine sedatives (such as zolpidem, eszopiclone, or zaleplon) during this period is allowable.\nA failed therapeutic trial of escitalopram in the current depressive episode (defined as at least 6 weeks of treatment at a daily dose of 10mg or higher)\nKnown allergy or hypersensitivity to escitalopram or bupropion\nCurrent or planned psychotherapy\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\n  -  Current diagnosis of major depressive disorder\n  -  Daily access to smartphone or tablet with internet connection for the study duration\n  -  Willing and able to complete MRI, mood, and neuropsychological testing\n  -  IQ > 70\nExclusion Criteria:\n  -  Current or past diagnoses of other Axis I psychiatric disorders, except for generalized anxiety disorder (GAD) symptoms occurring during a depressive episode\n  -  History of alcohol [OR] or drug dependence [OR] or abuse in the last three years\n  -  History of developmental disorder [OR] or IQ score < 70\n  -  Presence of acute suicidality\n  -  Acute grief (< 1 month)\n  -  Current [OR] or past psychosis\n  -  Primary neurological disorder, including but not limited to dementia, [OR] stroke, [OR] brain tumors, [OR] epilepsy, [OR] Parkinson\'s disease, [OR] or demyelinating diseases\n  -  MRI contraindications\n  -  Any physical [OR] or intellectual disability adversely affecting ability to complete assessments\n  -  Electroconvulsive therapy in last 6 months\n  -  Use of antidepressant medications [OR] or other psychotropic medications in the last 4 weeks ([OR] or the last 6 weeks for fluoxetine). Occasional use of benzodiazepines [OR] or [NOT] non-benzodiazepine sedatives (such as zolpidem, [OR] eszopiclone, [OR] or zaleplon) during this period is allowable.\n  -  A failed therapeutic trial of escitalopram in the current depressive episode (defined as at least 6 weeks of treatment at a daily dose of 10mg or higher)\n  -  Known allergy [OR] or hypersensitivity to escitalopram [OR] or bupropion\n  -  Current [OR] or planned psychotherapy<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
  -  Current diagnosis of major depressive disorder
  -  Daily access to smartphone or tablet with internet connection for the study duration
  -  Willing and able to complete MRI, mood, and neuropsychological testing
  -  IQ > 70
Exclusion Criteria:
  -  Current or past diagnoses of other Axis I psychiatric disorders, except for generalized anxiety disorder (GAD) symptoms occurring during a depressive episode
  -  History of alcohol [OR] or drug dependence [OR] or abuse in the last three years
  -  History of developmental disorder [OR] or IQ score < 70
  -  Presence of acute suicidality
  -  Acute grief (< 1 month)
  -  Current [OR] or past psychosis
  -  Primary neurological disorder, including but not limited to dementia, [OR] stroke, [OR] brain tumors, [OR] epilepsy, [OR] Parkinson's disease, [OR] or demyelinating diseases
  -  MRI contraindications
  -  Any physical [OR] or intellectual disability adversely affecting ability to complete assessments
  -  Electroconvulsive therapy in last 6 months
  -  Use of antidepressant medications [OR] or other psychotropic medications in the last 4 weeks ([OR] or the last 6 weeks for fluoxetine). Occasional use of benzodiazepines [OR] or [NOT] non-benzodiazepine sedatives (such as zolpidem, [OR] eszopiclone, [OR] or zaleplon) during this period is allowable.
  -  A failed therapeutic trial of escitalopram in the current depressive episode (defined as at least 6 weeks of treatment at a daily dose of 10mg or higher)
  -  Known allergy [OR] or hypersensitivity to escitalopram [OR] or bupropion
  -  Current [OR] or planned psychotherapy
