Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nPatients must be at least 21 years old.\nThe patient must have severe, symptomatic (ACC/AHA Stage D symptoms) tricuspid regurgitation (TR) as assessed by 2D echocardiogram with evidence of peripheral and central venous congestion (specifically lower extremity edema and abdominal ascites requiring diuretics.)\nThe patient must be evaluated by a "heart team" of physicians including an interventional cardiologist, cardiothoracic surgeon, heart failure specialist, and imaging specialist, and presented for review at a local multi-disciplinary conference. By consensus, the heart team must agree (and verify in the case review process) that valve implantation will likely benefit the patient.\nThe heart team must agree that medical factors preclude operation, based on a conclusion that the probability of death or serious, irreversible morbidity exceeds the probability of meaningful improvement. Also, other factors which may increase the patients perceived surgical risk for inclusion in the trial will be clearly delineated if they are present. These include, but are not limited to the following as defined by VARC 2: Frailty, Hostile chest, porcelain aorta, IMA or other critical conduit crossing the midline or adherent to the posterior table of sternum, severe right ventricular (RV) dysfunction. The surgeons\' consultation notes shall specify the medical or anatomic factors leading to that conclusion. At least one of the cardiac surgeon assessors must have interviewed and examined the patient.\nThe study patient provides informed consent and agrees to comply with all required post-procedure follow-up visits, including annual visits up to 5 years.\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nPatients must be at least 21 years old.\nThe patient must have severe, symptomatic (ACC/AHA Stage D symptoms) tricuspid regurgitation (TR) as assessed by 2D echocardiogram [AND] with evidence of peripheral [OR] and central venous congestion (specifically lower extremity edema [OR] and abdominal ascites requiring diuretics.)\nThe patient must be evaluated by a "heart team" of physicians including an interventional cardiologist, [OR] cardiothoracic surgeon, [OR] heart failure specialist, [OR] and imaging specialist, and presented for review at a local multi-disciplinary conference. By consensus, the heart team must agree (and verify in the case review process) that valve implantation will likely benefit the patient.\nThe heart team must agree that medical factors [NOT] preclude operation, based on a conclusion that the probability of death [OR] or serious, irreversible morbidity exceeds the probability of meaningful improvement. Also, other factors which may increase the patients perceived surgical risk for inclusion in the trial will be clearly delineated if they are present. These include, but are not limited to the following as defined by VARC 2: Frailty, Hostile chest, [OR] porcelain aorta, [OR] IMA [OR] or other critical conduit crossing the midline [OR] or adherent to the posterior table of sternum, severe right ventricular (RV) dysfunction. The surgeons\' consultation notes shall specify the medical [OR] or anatomic factors leading to that conclusion. At least one of the cardiac surgeon assessors must have interviewed and examined the patient.\nThe study patient provides informed consent and agrees to comply with all required post-procedure follow-up visits, including annual visits up to 5 years.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Patients must be at least 21 years old.
The patient must have severe, symptomatic (ACC/AHA Stage D symptoms) tricuspid regurgitation (TR) as assessed by 2D echocardiogram [AND] with evidence of peripheral [OR] and central venous congestion (specifically lower extremity edema [OR] and abdominal ascites requiring diuretics.)
The patient must be evaluated by a "heart team" of physicians including an interventional cardiologist, [OR] cardiothoracic surgeon, [OR] heart failure specialist, [OR] and imaging specialist, and presented for review at a local multi-disciplinary conference. By consensus, the heart team must agree (and verify in the case review process) that valve implantation will likely benefit the patient.
The heart team must agree that medical factors [NOT] preclude operation, based on a conclusion that the probability of death [OR] or serious, irreversible morbidity exceeds the probability of meaningful improvement. Also, other factors which may increase the patients perceived surgical risk for inclusion in the trial will be clearly delineated if they are present. These include, but are not limited to the following as defined by VARC 2: Frailty, Hostile chest, [OR] porcelain aorta, [OR] IMA [OR] or other critical conduit crossing the midline [OR] or adherent to the posterior table of sternum, severe right ventricular (RV) dysfunction. The surgeons' consultation notes shall specify the medical [OR] or anatomic factors leading to that conclusion. At least one of the cardiac surgeon assessors must have interviewed and examined the patient.
The study patient provides informed consent and agrees to comply with all required post-procedure follow-up visits, including annual visits up to 5 years.
