Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nActive proliferative diabetic retinopathy (PDR) in the study eye such as NVE, NVD, vitreous hemorrhage, or neovascular glaucoma.\nUncontrolled hypertension defined as systolic >180 mmHg or > 160 mmHg on 2 consecutive measurements or diastolic > 100 mmHg on optimal medical regimen\nScreening HgA1c blood test > 10.0\nFocal laser photocoagulation or intravitreal/periocular steroids of any type in the study eye within the last 90 days prior to study enrollment.\nA history of intravitreal anti-VEGF injection of any type in the study eye within the last 45 days prior to study enrollment.\nHistory of rhegmatogenous retinal detachment, retinal tear(s), or traction retinal detachments in the study eye.\nEpiretinal membrane and/or vitreomacular traction in the study eye as determined by the central reading center.\nPrevious pars plana vitrectomy in the study eye\nAny intraocular surgery in the study eye within the last 90 days prior to study enrollment.\nYAG laser treatment in the study eye in last 30 days prior to study enrollment.\nHigh myopia in the study eye, with a spherical equivalent of >8.00D at screening\nOther ocular pathologies that in the investigator\'s opinion would interfere with the subject\'s vision in the study eye.\nChronic or recurrent uveitis.\nOngoing ocular infection or inflammation in either eye.\nA history of cataract surgery complications/vitreous loss in the study eye.\nCongenital eye malformations in the study eye.\nA history of penetrating ocular trauma in the study eye.\nMentally handicapped.\nPregnant female, as determined for women less than 60 years old by a positive urine pregnancy test during the screening window.\nNursing female.\nCurrently participating in any other clinical research study.\nContraindication to the study medication.\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nActive proliferative diabetic retinopathy (PDR) in the study eye such as NVE, [OR] NVD, [OR] vitreous hemorrhage, [OR] or neovascular glaucoma.\nUncontrolled hypertension defined as systolic >180 mmHg [OR] or > 160 mmHg on 2 consecutive measurements [OR] or diastolic > 100 mmHg on optimal medical regimen\nScreening HgA1c blood test > 10.0\nFocal laser photocoagulation [OR] or intravitreal/ [OR] periocular steroids of any type in the study eye within the last 90 days prior to study enrollment.\nA history of intravitreal anti-VEGF injection of any type in the study eye within the last 45 days prior to study enrollment.\nHistory of rhegmatogenous retinal detachment, [OR] retinal tear(s), [OR] or traction retinal detachments in the study eye.\nEpiretinal membrane [OR] and/or vitreomacular traction in the study eye as determined by the central reading center.\nPrevious pars plana vitrectomy in the study eye\nAny intraocular surgery in the study eye within the last 90 days prior to study enrollment.\nYAG laser treatment in the study eye in last 30 days prior to study enrollment.\nHigh myopia in the study eye, [AND] with a spherical equivalent of >8.00D at screening\nOther ocular pathologies that in the investigator\'s opinion would interfere with the subject\'s vision in the study eye.\nChronic [OR] or recurrent uveitis.\nOngoing ocular infection [OR] or inflammation in either eye.\nA history of cataract surgery complications/ [OR] vitreous loss in the study eye.\nCongenital eye malformations in the study eye.\n A history of penetrating ocular trauma in the study eye.\nMentally handicapped.\nPregnant female, as determined for women less than 60 years old by a positive urine pregnancy test during the screening window.\nNursing female.\nCurrently participating in any other clinical research study.\nContraindication to the study medication.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Active proliferative diabetic retinopathy (PDR) in the study eye such as NVE, [OR] NVD, [OR] vitreous hemorrhage, [OR] or neovascular glaucoma.
Uncontrolled hypertension defined as systolic >180 mmHg [OR] or > 160 mmHg on 2 consecutive measurements [OR] or diastolic > 100 mmHg on optimal medical regimen
Screening HgA1c blood test > 10.0
Focal laser photocoagulation [OR] or intravitreal/ [OR] periocular steroids of any type in the study eye within the last 90 days prior to study enrollment.
A history of intravitreal anti-VEGF injection of any type in the study eye within the last 45 days prior to study enrollment.
History of rhegmatogenous retinal detachment, [OR] retinal tear(s), [OR] or traction retinal detachments in the study eye.
Epiretinal membrane [OR] and/or vitreomacular traction in the study eye as determined by the central reading center.
Previous pars plana vitrectomy in the study eye
Any intraocular surgery in the study eye within the last 90 days prior to study enrollment.
YAG laser treatment in the study eye in last 30 days prior to study enrollment.
High myopia in the study eye, [AND] with a spherical equivalent of >8.00D at screening
Other ocular pathologies that in the investigator's opinion would interfere with the subject's vision in the study eye.
Chronic [OR] or recurrent uveitis.
Ongoing ocular infection [OR] or inflammation in either eye.
A history of cataract surgery complications/ [OR] vitreous loss in the study eye.
Congenital eye malformations in the study eye.
 A history of penetrating ocular trauma in the study eye.
Mentally handicapped.
Pregnant female, as determined for women less than 60 years old by a positive urine pregnancy test during the screening window.
Nursing female.
Currently participating in any other clinical research study.
Contraindication to the study medication.
