Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nMale or female, 18 years of age or older.\nStudy eye with clinically significant diabetic macular edema (DME) with central subfield thickness ≥ 350µm on spectral domain OCT\nBest corrected visual acuity (BCVA) of 20/50 to 20/320 ETDRS equivalent (65 letters to 23 letters) in the study eye, with BCVA decrement primarily attributable to DME.\nTreatment naïve, i.e., no previous anti-VEGF treatment in the study eye or no anti-VEGF treatment in the 45 days prior to study enrollment.\nIn the investigator\'s opinion, the subject still has significant intraretinal fluid with room for improvement in both macular edema and BCVA.\nIntra-Ocular Pressure (IOP) is under control (i.e., IOP ≤ 25 mm in the study eye) and study eye is not receiving any IOP lowering drops.\nWilling and able to return for all study visits.\nAble to meet the extensive post-op evaluation regimen.\nUnderstands and signs the informed consent form.\n\n\n### Response:\nMale [OR] or female, 18 years of age or older.\nStudy eye with clinically significant diabetic macular edema (DME) [AND] with central subfield thickness ≥ 350µm on spectral domain OCT\nBest corrected visual acuity (BCVA) of 20/50 to 20/320 ETDRS equivalent (65 letters to 23 letters) in the study eye, [AND] with BCVA decrement primarily attributable to DME.\nTreatment naïve, i.e., [NOT] no previous anti-VEGF treatment in the study eye [OR] or [NOT] no anti-VEGF treatment in the 45 days prior to study enrollment.\nIn the investigator\'s opinion, the subject still has significant intraretinal fluid [AND] with room for improvement in both macular edema [AND] and BCVA.\nIntra-Ocular Pressure (IOP) is under control (i.e., IOP ≤ 25 mm in the study eye) [AND] and study eye is [NOT] not receiving any IOP lowering drops.\nWilling and able to return for all study visits.\nAble to meet the extensive post-op evaluation regimen.\nUnderstands and signs the informed consent form.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Male [OR] or female, 18 years of age or older.
Study eye with clinically significant diabetic macular edema (DME) [AND] with central subfield thickness ≥ 350µm on spectral domain OCT
Best corrected visual acuity (BCVA) of 20/50 to 20/320 ETDRS equivalent (65 letters to 23 letters) in the study eye, [AND] with BCVA decrement primarily attributable to DME.
Treatment naïve, i.e., [NOT] no previous anti-VEGF treatment in the study eye [OR] or [NOT] no anti-VEGF treatment in the 45 days prior to study enrollment.
In the investigator's opinion, the subject still has significant intraretinal fluid [AND] with room for improvement in both macular edema [AND] and BCVA.
Intra-Ocular Pressure (IOP) is under control (i.e., IOP ≤ 25 mm in the study eye) [AND] and study eye is [NOT] not receiving any IOP lowering drops.
Willing and able to return for all study visits.
Able to meet the extensive post-op evaluation regimen.
Understands and signs the informed consent form.
