Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nHistologically confirmed locally advanced gastric (primary endpoint includes proximal and mid-body stomach) or esophagogastric adenocarcinoma; distal gastric (antral) adenocarcinomas are eligible for enrolment but will not be included in the primary analysis\nLocally advanced disease as determined by endoscopic ultrasound (EUS) stage > primary tumor (T) 3 and/or any T, lymph nodes (N)+ disease without metastatic disease (Mx)\nAll patients must have diagnostic laparoscopy with diagnostic washings for cytology; both cytology positive and negative patients are eligible for enrolment, but only cytology negative patients will be included in the primary analyses; gross peritoneal disease is not eligible\nEastern Cooperative Oncology Group (ECOG) performance status =< 1\nEligible for surgery with curative intent\nAbsolute neutrophil count (ANC) >= 1250/ul\nHemoglobin >= 9 g/dL\nPlatelets >= 100,000/ul\nTotal bilirubin < 1.5 x upper limit of normal\nSerum glutamic oxaloacetic transaminase (SGOT) and serum glutamate pyruvate transaminase (SGPT) < 2.5 x upper limit of normal for patients without liver metastases OR SGOT and SGPT < 5 x upper limit of normal for patients with liver metastases\nCreatinine =< 1.5 x upper limit of normal\nMeasurable or non-measurable disease by Response Evaluation Criteria in Solid Tumor (RECIST) 1.1 will be allowed\nWomen of child-bearing potential and men must agree to use adequate contraception (hormonal or barrier method of birth control; abstinence) prior to study entry and for the duration of study participation, up until 30 days after final study treatment; should a woman become pregnant or suspect that she is pregnant while participating in this study, she should inform her treating physician immediately\nPatients taking substrates, inhibitors, or inducers of cytochrome P450, family 3, subfamily A, polypeptide 4 (CYP3A4) should be encouraged to switch to alternative drugs whenever possible, given the potential for drug-drug interactions with irinotecan\nSigned informed consent\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nHistologically confirmed locally advanced gastric (primary endpoint includes proximal [OR] and mid-body stomach) [OR] or esophagogastric adenocarcinoma; distal gastric (antral) adenocarcinomas are eligible for enrolment but will [NOT] not be included in the primary analysis\nLocally advanced disease as determined by endoscopic ultrasound (EUS) stage > primary tumor (T) 3 [OR] and/or any T, lymph nodes (N)+ disease [NOT] without metastatic disease (Mx)\nAll patients must have diagnostic laparoscopy [AND] with diagnostic washings for cytology; both cytology positive [OR] and negative patients are eligible for enrolment, but only cytology negative patients will be included in the primary analyses; gross peritoneal disease is [NOT] not eligible\nEastern Cooperative Oncology Group (ECOG) performance status =< 1\nEligible for surgery with curative intent\nAbsolute neutrophil count (ANC) >= 1250/ul\nHemoglobin >= 9 g/dL\nPlatelets >= 100,000/ul\nTotal bilirubin < 1.5 x upper limit of normal\nSerum glutamic oxaloacetic transaminase (SGOT) [OR] and serum glutamate pyruvate transaminase (SGPT) < 2.5 x upper limit of normal for patients [NOT] without liver metastases [OR] OR SGOT [OR] and SGPT < 5 x upper limit of normal for patients [AND] with liver metastases\nCreatinine =< 1.5 x upper limit of normal\nMeasurable [OR] or [NOT] non-measurable disease by Response Evaluation Criteria in Solid Tumor (RECIST) 1.1 will be allowed\nWomen [AND] of child-bearing potential [AND] and men must agree to use adequate contraception (hormonal [OR] or barrier method of birth control; [OR] abstinence) prior to study entry and for the duration of study participation, up until 30 days after final study treatment; should a woman become pregnant [OR] or suspect that she is pregnant while participating in this study, she should inform her treating physician immediately\nPatients taking substrates, [OR] inhibitors, [OR] or inducers of cytochrome P450, family 3, subfamily A, polypeptide 4 (CYP3A4) should be encouraged to switch to alternative drugs whenever possible, given the potential for drug-drug interactions with irinotecan\nSigned informed consent<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Histologically confirmed locally advanced gastric (primary endpoint includes proximal [OR] and mid-body stomach) [OR] or esophagogastric adenocarcinoma; distal gastric (antral) adenocarcinomas are eligible for enrolment but will [NOT] not be included in the primary analysis
Locally advanced disease as determined by endoscopic ultrasound (EUS) stage > primary tumor (T) 3 [OR] and/or any T, lymph nodes (N)+ disease [NOT] without metastatic disease (Mx)
All patients must have diagnostic laparoscopy [AND] with diagnostic washings for cytology; both cytology positive [OR] and negative patients are eligible for enrolment, but only cytology negative patients will be included in the primary analyses; gross peritoneal disease is [NOT] not eligible
Eastern Cooperative Oncology Group (ECOG) performance status =< 1
Eligible for surgery with curative intent
Absolute neutrophil count (ANC) >= 1250/ul
Hemoglobin >= 9 g/dL
Platelets >= 100,000/ul
Total bilirubin < 1.5 x upper limit of normal
Serum glutamic oxaloacetic transaminase (SGOT) [OR] and serum glutamate pyruvate transaminase (SGPT) < 2.5 x upper limit of normal for patients [NOT] without liver metastases [OR] OR SGOT [OR] and SGPT < 5 x upper limit of normal for patients [AND] with liver metastases
Creatinine =< 1.5 x upper limit of normal
Measurable [OR] or [NOT] non-measurable disease by Response Evaluation Criteria in Solid Tumor (RECIST) 1.1 will be allowed
Women [AND] of child-bearing potential [AND] and men must agree to use adequate contraception (hormonal [OR] or barrier method of birth control; [OR] abstinence) prior to study entry and for the duration of study participation, up until 30 days after final study treatment; should a woman become pregnant [OR] or suspect that she is pregnant while participating in this study, she should inform her treating physician immediately
Patients taking substrates, [OR] inhibitors, [OR] or inducers of cytochrome P450, family 3, subfamily A, polypeptide 4 (CYP3A4) should be encouraged to switch to alternative drugs whenever possible, given the potential for drug-drug interactions with irinotecan
Signed informed consent
