File: NCT02384850_exc 

Das File: /work/eauten2s/ec_criteria_struct/chia/input/chia_text_half/NCT02384850_exc.txt wurde erfolgreich geladen.
Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nadequately controlled with appropriate therapy or would compromise the patient\'s ability to tolerate this therapy; 2. Treatment with any systemic anticancer therapy ≤ 3 weeks prior to cycle 1 day 1 3. Uncontrolled active infection (Hepatitis B and C infection are NOT exclusion criteria) and/or known HIV infection; 4. Renal failure requiring haemodialysis or peritoneal dialysis; 5. Patients who are pregnant or breast-feeding; 6. Patients with significantly diseased or obstructed gastrointestinal tract, malabsorption, uncontrolled vomiting or diarrhea resulting in inability to swallow oral medications; 7. Presence of symptomatic CNS metastasis 8. Unresolved toxicity from previous anti-cancer therapy or incomplete recovery from surgery, in particular oxaliplatin-induced peripheral neuropathy > grade 1. \n9. Any of the following within the 12 months prior to study drug administration: myocardial infarction, severe/unstable angina, coronary/peripheral artery bypass graft, symptomatic congestive heart failure, cerebrovascular accident or transient ischemic attack, pulmonary embolism, deep vein thrombosis, or other thromboembolic event.       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\n  -  Informed consent is obtained from the participant.\n  -  The participant is clinically diagnosed with colorectal cancer, and the disease is confirmed by histopathological or cytological examination.\n  -  The participant is a planned recipient of FOLFIRI or FOLFOX for neoadjuvant or adjuvant chemotherapy.\n  -  The participant is a planned recipient of surgical resection of the primary tumor.\n  -  The participant has a life expectancy of > 12 months.\n  -  The participant has an Eastern Cooperative Oncology Group (ECOG) performance status score of 0-2.\n  -  The participant does not have any other serious disease or medical condition that is likely to prevent the participant from complying with any aspect of the protocol, or that may put the participant at unacceptable risk.\nExclusion Criteria:\n  -  The participant has received any prior treatment for colorectal cancer, including cytotoxic drug therapy, targeted drug therapy, or hormonal therapy.\n  -  The participant has had prior exposure to anlotinib or has known allegies to any of the excipients, Inadequately controlled systemic hypertension with or without current antihypertensive medications;\n  -  History of myocardial infarction, or unstable angina, or New York Heart Association (NYHA) Grade III-IV within 6 months prior to Day 1.\n  -  History of abdominal fistula or gastrointestinal perforation within 28 days prior to Day 1\n  -  Major surgical procedure within 28 days prior to Day 1, Serious, non-healing wound, active ulcer, bowel obstruction within 28 days prior to Day 1\n  -  Symptomatic central nervous system (CNS) metastasis\n  -  Pregnant or lactating women. Documentation of a negative pregnancy test must be available for women of childbearing potential.\n  -  Women of childbearing potential are premenopausal women with intact reproductive organs and women less than two years after menopause.\n  -  Lab values that in the opinion of the primary surgeon would prevent surgical resection of the primary tumor.\n  -  Any current use of anticoagulants, anti-platelet agents, or non-steroidal anti-inflammatory drugs (NSAIDs) that may interfere with anlotinib\'s pharmacological activity\n  -  Any known allergies to anlotinib, oxaliplatin, fluorouracil, and/or leucovorin\n  -  Lactation\n  -  Pregnant women\n  -  Women of child-bearing potential not using highly effective methods of contraception\nOther protocol defined inclusion/exclusion criteria could apply\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\n - Informed consent is obtained from the participant.\n - The participant is clinically diagnosed with colorectal cancer, [AND] and the disease is confirmed by histopathological [OR] or cytological examination.\n - The participant is a planned recipient of FOLFIRI [OR] or FOLFOX for neoadjuvant [OR] or adjuvant chemotherapy.\n - The participant is a planned recipient of surgical resection of the primary tumor.\n - The participant has a life expectancy of > 12 months.\n - The participant has an Eastern Cooperative Oncology Group (ECOG) performance status score of 0-2.\n - The participant does [NOT] not have any other serious disease [OR] or medical condition that is likely to [NOT] prevent the participant from complying with any aspect of the protocol, [OR] or that may put the participant at unacceptable risk.\nExclusion Criteria:\n - The participant has received any prior treatment for colorectal cancer, including cytotoxic drug therapy, [OR] targeted drug therapy, [OR] or hormonal therapy.\n - The participant has had prior exposure to anlotinib [OR] or has known allegies to any of the excipients, Inadequately controlled systemic hypertension [AND] with or [NOT] without current antihypertensive medications;\n - History of myocardial infarction, [OR] or unstable angina, [OR] or New York Heart Association (NYHA) Grade III-IV within 6 months prior to Day 1.\n - History of abdominal fistula [OR] or gastrointestinal perforation within 28 days prior to Day 1\n - Major surgical procedure within 28 days prior to Day 1, Serious, [NOT] non-healing wound, active ulcer, [OR] bowel obstruction within 28 days prior to Day 1\n - Symptomatic central nervous system (CNS) metastasis\n - Pregnant [OR] or lactating women. Documentation of a negative pregnancy test must be available for women of childbearing potential.\n - Women of childbearing potential [AND] are premenopausal women [AND] with intact reproductive organs [AND] and women less than two years after menopause.\n - Lab values that in the opinion of the primary surgeon would [NOT] prevent surgical resection of the primary tumor.\n - Any current use of anticoagulants, [OR] anti-platelet agents, [OR] or non-steroidal anti-inflammatory drugs (NSAIDs) that may interfere with anlotinib\'s pharmacological activity\n - Any known allergies to anlotinib, [OR] oxaliplatin, [OR] fluorouracil, [OR] and/or leucovorin\n - Lactation\n - Pregnant women\n - Women [AND] of child-bearing potential [NOT] not using highly effective methods of contraception\nOther protocol defined inclusion/exclusion criteria could apply<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
  -  Informed consent is obtained from the participant.
  -  The participant is clinically diagnosed with colorectal cancer, and the disease is confirmed by histopathological or cytological examination.
  -  The participant is a planned recipient of FOLFIRI or FOLFOX for neoadjuvant or adjuvant chemotherapy.
  -  The participant is a planned recipient of surgical resection of the primary tumor.
  -  The participant has a life expectancy of > 12 months.
  -  The participant has an Eastern Cooperative Oncology Group (ECOG) performance status score of 0-2.
  -  The participant does not have any other serious disease or medical condition that is likely to prevent the participant from complying with any aspect of the protocol, or that may put the participant at unacceptable risk.
Exclusion Criteria:
  -  The participant has received any prior treatment for colorectal cancer, including cytotoxic drug therapy, targeted drug therapy, or hormonal therapy.
  -  The participant has had prior exposure to anlotinib or has known allegies to any of the excipients, Inadequately controlled systemic hypertension with or without current antihypertensive medications;
  -  History of myocardial infarction, or unstable angina, or New York Heart Association (NYHA) Grade III-IV within 6 months prior to Day 1.
  -  History of abdominal fistula or gastrointestinal perforation within 28 days prior to Day 1
  -  Major surgical procedure within 28 days prior to Day 1, Serious, non-healing wound, active ulcer, bowel obstruction within 28 days prior to Day 1
  -  Symptomatic central nervous system (CNS) metastasis
  -  Pregnant or lactating women. Documentation of a negative pregnancy test must be available for women of childbearing potential.
  -  Women of childbearing potential are premenopausal women with intact reproductive organs and women less than two years after menopause.
  -  Lab values that in the opinion of the primary surgeon would prevent surgical resection of the primary tumor.
  -  Any current use of anticoagulants, anti-platelet agents, or non-steroidal anti-inflammatory drugs (NSAIDs) that may interfere with anlotinib's pharmacological activity
  -  Any known allergies to anlotinib, oxaliplatin, fluorouracil, and/or leucovorin
  -  Lactation
  -  Pregnant women
  -  Women of child-bearing potential not using highly effective methods of contraception
Other protocol defined inclusion/exclusion criteria could apply
