Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nHistory of prostate, bladder, or rectal cancer \nHistory of transurethral resection of the prostate (TURP), open prostate surgery, or radiofrequency or microwave therapies \nHistory of open bladder, rectosigmoid colon, or other pelvic surgery \nPatient is unwilling to discontinue alpha blockers 1 month after study treatment \nPatient is unwilling to discontinue 5-alph reductase inhibitors 1 month after study treatment \nNeurogenic bladder or other neurologic disorder impacting bladder function such as Parkinson\'s disease, multiple sclerosis, cerebral vascular accident or diabetes \nAny other confounding bladder or urethral pathology, including urethral stricture, bladder neck contracture, or bladder atonia \nActive prostatitis or urinary tract infection \nCystolithiasis within the past 3 months \nSerum creatinine > 1.7mg/dL \nInability to discontinue oral anticoagulant 2-5 days prior to study treatment \nCoagulation disturbances not normalized by medical treatment \nIodinated contrast allergy that, in the opinion of the Investigator, cannot be adequately premedicated \nGelatin allergy \nKnown severe peripheral vascular disease or major iliac arterial occlusive disease \nInterest in future fertility \nClinically significant cardiac arrhythmia or other cardiac disease (including congestive heart failure), uncontrolled diabetes mellitus, clinically significant respiratory disease, or known immunosuppression \nOther condition that the Investigator believes puts the patient at risk for a complication during the procedure       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nHistory of prostate, [OR] bladder, [OR] or rectal cancer \nHistory of transurethral resection of the prostate (TURP), open prostate surgery, [OR] or radiofrequency [OR] or microwave therapies \nHistory of open bladder, [OR] rectosigmoid colon, [OR] or other pelvic surgery \nPatient is unwilling to [NOT] discontinue alpha blockers 1 month after study treatment \nPatient is unwilling to [NOT] discontinue 5-alph reductase inhibitors 1 month after study treatment \nNeurogenic bladder [OR] or other neurologic disorder impacting bladder function such as Parkinson\'s disease, [OR] multiple sclerosis, [OR] cerebral vascular accident [OR] or diabetes \nAny other confounding bladder [OR] or urethral pathology, including urethral stricture, [OR] bladder neck contracture, [OR] or bladder atonia \nActive prostatitis [OR] or urinary tract infection \nCystolithiasis within the past 3 months \nSerum creatinine > 1.7mg/dL \nInability to [NOT] discontinue oral anticoagulant 2-5 days prior to study treatment \nCoagulation disturbances [NOT] not normalized by medical treatment \nIodinated contrast allergy that, in the opinion of the Investigator, [NOT] cannot be adequately premedicated \nGelatin allergy \nKnown severe peripheral vascular disease [OR] or major iliac arterial occlusive disease \nInterest in future fertility \nClinically significant cardiac arrhythmia [OR] or other cardiac disease (including congestive heart failure), uncontrolled diabetes mellitus, clinically significant respiratory disease, [OR] or known immunosuppression \nOther condition that the Investigator believes puts the patient at risk for a complication during the procedure<|eot_id|>']
Response: History of prostate, [OR] bladder, [OR] or rectal cancer 
History of transurethral resection of the prostate (TURP), open prostate surgery, [OR] or radiofrequency [OR] or microwave therapies 
History of open bladder, [OR] rectosigmoid colon, [OR] or other pelvic surgery 
Patient is unwilling to [NOT] discontinue alpha blockers 1 month after study treatment 
Patient is unwilling to [NOT] discontinue 5-alph reductase inhibitors 1 month after study treatment 
Neurogenic bladder [OR] or other neurologic disorder impacting bladder function such as Parkinson's disease, [OR] multiple sclerosis, [OR] cerebral vascular accident [OR] or diabetes 
Any other confounding bladder [OR] or urethral pathology, including urethral stricture, [OR] bladder neck contracture, [OR] or bladder atonia 
Active prostatitis [OR] or urinary tract infection 
Cystolithiasis within the past 3 months 
Serum creatinine > 1.7mg/dL 
Inability to [NOT] discontinue oral anticoagulant 2-5 days prior to study treatment 
Coagulation disturbances [NOT] not normalized by medical treatment 
Iodinated contrast allergy that, in the opinion of the Investigator, [NOT] cannot be adequately premedicated 
Gelatin allergy 
Known severe peripheral vascular disease [OR] or major iliac arterial occlusive disease 
Interest in future fertility 
Clinically significant cardiac arrhythmia [OR] or other cardiac disease (including congestive heart failure), uncontrolled diabetes mellitus, clinically significant respiratory disease, [OR] or known immunosuppression 
Other condition that the Investigator believes puts the patient at risk for a complication during the procedure
