File: NCT02396420_inc 

Das File: /work/eauten2s/ec_criteria_struct/chia/input/chia_text_half/NCT02396420_inc.txt wurde erfolgreich geladen.
Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nPatient has provided signed informed consent \nPatient is aged greater than or equal to 40 and less than or equal to 89 years of age \nPatient has a prostate size between 90g and 200g, as determined by MRI \nPatient has experienced lower urinary tract symptoms (LUTS) for at least 6 months prior to study enrollment \nPatient has an IPSS score of at least 13 at baseline \nPatient is either: refractory to medical treatment, contraindicated to medical treatment, OR refuses medical treatment \nPatient either: refuses surgical treatment OR is contraindicated for surgical treatment \nPatient meets ONE of the following criteria: baseline PSA < 4.0ng/mL (no prostate biopsy required) OR baseline PSA >/= 4 ng/mL AND a negative prostate biopsy (minimum 12 core biopsy) within the prior 12 months \n\n\n### Response:\nPatient has provided signed informed consent \nPatient is aged greater than or equal to 40 [AND] and less than or equal to 89 years of age \nPatient has a prostate size between 90g [AND] and 200g, as determined by MRI \nPatient has experienced lower urinary tract symptoms (LUTS) for at least 6 months prior to study enrollment \nPatient has an IPSS score of at least 13 at baseline \nPatient is either: refractory to medical treatment, [OR] contraindicated to medical treatment, [OR] OR refuses medical treatment \nPatient either: [NOT] refuses surgical treatment [OR] OR is [NOT] contraindicated for surgical treatment \nPatient meets ONE of the following criteria: baseline PSA < 4.0ng/mL ([NOT] no prostate biopsy required) [OR] OR baseline PSA >/= 4 ng/mL [AND] AND a negative prostate biopsy (minimum 12 core biopsy) within the prior 12 months<|eot_id|>']
Response: Patient has provided signed informed consent 
Patient is aged greater than or equal to 40 [AND] and less than or equal to 89 years of age 
Patient has a prostate size between 90g [AND] and 200g, as determined by MRI 
Patient has experienced lower urinary tract symptoms (LUTS) for at least 6 months prior to study enrollment 
Patient has an IPSS score of at least 13 at baseline 
Patient is either: refractory to medical treatment, [OR] contraindicated to medical treatment, [OR] OR refuses medical treatment 
Patient either: [NOT] refuses surgical treatment [OR] OR is [NOT] contraindicated for surgical treatment 
Patient meets ONE of the following criteria: baseline PSA < 4.0ng/mL ([NOT] no prostate biopsy required) [OR] OR baseline PSA >/= 4 ng/mL [AND] AND a negative prostate biopsy (minimum 12 core biopsy) within the prior 12 months
