Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nAge: 20-70 years old;\nGender: male or female;\nclinical or pathological diagnosis of hepatocellular carcinoma (HCC) in previously untreated patients;\nThe expected survival> 3 months;\nChild-Pugh grade in A-level;\nKPS score with 50-100 points;\nBCLC stage of 0-B;\nconform to the indications of hepatectomy;\nViable tumor resection confirmed by two highly qualified surgical doctors;\nNo other surgical contraindications.\nwomen in the reproductive period must be completely contraception in 28 days before treatment, during the treatment process and in 28 days after treatment;\nMen must be completely contraception and prohibited donation and sperm donation during the treatment process and in 28 days after treatment;\nAll patients must be prohibited donation during the treatment process and in 28 days after treatment;\nIn addition to the subjects, prohibitting other people taking this product.\npatients have a good understanding and could coordinate with investigators for the trial.\nPatients enrolled in the trial should sign an informed consent form, to indicate understanding the purpose and procedure of the trial, and patients volunteering to participate in the trial.\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nAge: 20-70 years old;\nGender: male [OR] or female;\nclinical [OR] or pathological diagnosis of hepatocellular carcinoma (HCC) in previously [NOT] untreated patients;\nThe expected survival> 3 months;\nChild-Pugh grade in A-level;\n KPS score with 50-100 points;\n BCLC stage of 0-B;\nconform to the indications of hepatectomy;\nViable tumor resection confirmed by two highly qualified surgical doctors;\n [NOT] No other surgical contraindications.\nwomen [AND] in the reproductive period must be completely contraception in 28 days before treatment, during the treatment process and in 28 days after treatment;\nMen must be completely contraception [AND] and [NOT] prohibited donation [AND] and sperm donation during the treatment process and in 28 days after treatment;\nAll patients must be [NOT] prohibited donation during the treatment process and in 28 days after treatment;\nIn addition to the subjects, [NOT] prohibitting other people taking this product.\npatients have a good understanding and could coordinate with investigators for the trial.\nPatients enrolled in the trial should sign an informed consent form, to indicate understanding the purpose and procedure of the trial, and patients volunteering to participate in the trial.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Age: 20-70 years old;
Gender: male [OR] or female;
clinical [OR] or pathological diagnosis of hepatocellular carcinoma (HCC) in previously [NOT] untreated patients;
The expected survival> 3 months;
Child-Pugh grade in A-level;
 KPS score with 50-100 points;
 BCLC stage of 0-B;
conform to the indications of hepatectomy;
Viable tumor resection confirmed by two highly qualified surgical doctors;
 [NOT] No other surgical contraindications.
women [AND] in the reproductive period must be completely contraception in 28 days before treatment, during the treatment process and in 28 days after treatment;
Men must be completely contraception [AND] and [NOT] prohibited donation [AND] and sperm donation during the treatment process and in 28 days after treatment;
All patients must be [NOT] prohibited donation during the treatment process and in 28 days after treatment;
In addition to the subjects, [NOT] prohibitting other people taking this product.
patients have a good understanding and could coordinate with investigators for the trial.
Patients enrolled in the trial should sign an informed consent form, to indicate understanding the purpose and procedure of the trial, and patients volunteering to participate in the trial.
