Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nCentral + mixed apneas > 25% of the total apnea-hypopnea index (AHI)\nAny anatomical finding that would compromise the performance of upper airway stimulation, such as the presence of complete concentric collapse of the soft palate\nAny condition or procedure that has compromised neurological control of the upper airway\nPatients who are unable or do not have the necessary assistance to operate the patient remote\nPatients who are pregnant or plan to become pregnant\nPatients who will require magnetic resonance imaging (MRI)\nPatients with an implantable device that may be susceptible to unintended interaction with the Inspire system.\nBody Mass Index (BMI) of > 32\nAny chronic medical illness or condition that contraindicates a surgical procedure under general anesthesia, as judged by the clinical study Investigator\nHas a terminal illness with life expectancy < 12 months\nActive psychiatric disease (psychotic illness, major depression, or acute anxiety attacks) which prevents subject compliance with the requirements of the investigational study testing\nAny other reason the investigator deems subject is unfit for participation in the study\n\n\n### Response:\nCentral [OR] + mixed apneas > 25% of the total apnea-hypopnea index (AHI)\nAny anatomical finding that would compromise the performance of upper airway stimulation, such as the presence of complete concentric collapse of the soft palate\nAny condition [OR] or procedure that has compromised neurological control of the upper airway\nPatients who are unable or do not have the necessary assistance to operate the patient remote\nPatients who are pregnant [OR] or plan to become pregnant\nPatients who will require magnetic resonance imaging (MRI)\nPatients with an implantable device that may be susceptible to unintended interaction with the Inspire system.\nBody Mass Index (BMI) of > 32\nAny chronic medical illness [OR] or condition that contraindicates a surgical procedure under general anesthesia, as judged by the clinical study Investigator\nHas a terminal illness [AND] with life expectancy < 12 months\nActive psychiatric disease (psychotic illness, [OR] major depression, [OR] or acute anxiety attacks) which [NOT] prevents subject compliance with the requirements of the investigational study testing\nAny other reason the investigator deems subject is unfit for participation in the study<|eot_id|>']
Response: Central [OR] + mixed apneas > 25% of the total apnea-hypopnea index (AHI)
Any anatomical finding that would compromise the performance of upper airway stimulation, such as the presence of complete concentric collapse of the soft palate
Any condition [OR] or procedure that has compromised neurological control of the upper airway
Patients who are unable or do not have the necessary assistance to operate the patient remote
Patients who are pregnant [OR] or plan to become pregnant
Patients who will require magnetic resonance imaging (MRI)
Patients with an implantable device that may be susceptible to unintended interaction with the Inspire system.
Body Mass Index (BMI) of > 32
Any chronic medical illness [OR] or condition that contraindicates a surgical procedure under general anesthesia, as judged by the clinical study Investigator
Has a terminal illness [AND] with life expectancy < 12 months
Active psychiatric disease (psychotic illness, [OR] major depression, [OR] or acute anxiety attacks) which [NOT] prevents subject compliance with the requirements of the investigational study testing
Any other reason the investigator deems subject is unfit for participation in the study
