ently implanted, and to use the patient remote to activate the stimulation\nWilling and capable to return for all follow-up visits and conduct sleep studies at home, including the evaluation procedures and filling out questionnaires\nWilling and capable of providing informed consent\n\n\n### Response:\nLikely suffer moderate- [OR] to-severe OSA based on history [OR] and physical [OR] or have an established diagnosis of OSA (20=AHI=65) based on a prior in-lab Polysomnography\nDocumentation the subject [NOT] not effectively treated with CPAP therapy. (Examples include non-compliance, discomfort, undesirable side effects, symptoms persist [AND] despite use). Subjects who have been prescribed, [AND] but refuse to try CPAP would be considered intolerant.\nAge 22 or above\nWilling [AND] and capable to have stimulation hardware permanently implanted, [AND] and to use the patient remote to activate the stimulation\nWilling [AND] and capable to return for all follow-up visits [AND] and conduct sleep studies at home, including the evaluation procedures and filling out questionnaires\nWilling and capable of providing informed consent<|eot_id|>']
