Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nSigned informed consent form (ICF)\nAge 18 to 55 years old (inclusive) as of the date the ICF is signed\nDiagnosis of MS according to the McDonald criteria 2010 and cranial MRI scan demonstrating white matter lesions attributable to MS within 10 years before Screening\nOnset of MS symptoms (as determined by a neurologist, either at present or retrospectively) within 10 years of the date the ICF is signed\nEDSS score 0.0 to 5.0 (inclusive) at Screening\nPatients with (highly) active RRMS disease course indicated to receive alemtuzumab according to the following conditions (at least 1 out of 3 conditions has to be fulfilled): 1. =2 MS relapses within 24 months, 2. clinical (=1 relapse) or MRI (new gadolinium enhancing lesions) disease activity under therapy with other diseasemodifying therapies, 3. severe relapse with high disease activity (=9 T2 hyperintense Lesions and =1 gadolinium enhancing lesion) on MRI.\nCompletion of all vaccinations required by the applicable immunization guidelines published by "ständige Impfkommission" (STIKO)\nHistory of chickenpox or positive test for antibodies against varicella zoster virus (VZV)\n\n\n### Response:\nSigned informed consent form (ICF)\nAge 18 to 55 years old (inclusive) as of the date the ICF is signed\nDiagnosis of MS according to the McDonald criteria 2010 [AND] and cranial MRI scan demonstrating white matter lesions attributable to MS within 10 years before Screening\nOnset of MS symptoms (as determined by a neurologist, either at present [OR] or retrospectively) within 10 years of the date the ICF is signed\nEDSS score 0.0 to 5.0 (inclusive) at Screening\nPatients with (highly) active RRMS disease course indicated to receive alemtuzumab according to the following conditions (at least 1 out of 3 conditions has to be fulfilled): 1. =2 MS relapses within 24 months, 2. clinical (=1 relapse) [OR] or MRI (new gadolinium enhancing lesions) disease activity under therapy with other diseasemodifying therapies, 3. severe relapse [AND] with high disease activity (=9 T2 hyperintense Lesions [AND] and =1 gadolinium enhancing lesion) on MRI.\nCompletion of all vaccinations required by the applicable immunization guidelines published by "ständige Impfkommission" (STIKO)\nHistory of chickenpox [OR] or positive test for antibodies against varicella zoster virus (VZV)<|eot_id|>']
Response: Signed informed consent form (ICF)
Age 18 to 55 years old (inclusive) as of the date the ICF is signed
Diagnosis of MS according to the McDonald criteria 2010 [AND] and cranial MRI scan demonstrating white matter lesions attributable to MS within 10 years before Screening
Onset of MS symptoms (as determined by a neurologist, either at present [OR] or retrospectively) within 10 years of the date the ICF is signed
EDSS score 0.0 to 5.0 (inclusive) at Screening
Patients with (highly) active RRMS disease course indicated to receive alemtuzumab according to the following conditions (at least 1 out of 3 conditions has to be fulfilled): 1. =2 MS relapses within 24 months, 2. clinical (=1 relapse) [OR] or MRI (new gadolinium enhancing lesions) disease activity under therapy with other diseasemodifying therapies, 3. severe relapse [AND] with high disease activity (=9 T2 hyperintense Lesions [AND] and =1 gadolinium enhancing lesion) on MRI.
Completion of all vaccinations required by the applicable immunization guidelines published by "ständige Impfkommission" (STIKO)
History of chickenpox [OR] or positive test for antibodies against varicella zoster virus (VZV)
