Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nSubjects with poor-controlled arterial hypertension (systolic blood pressure> 140 mmHg and diastolic blood pressure > 90 mm Hg) despite standard medical management; Coronary heart disease greater than ClassII; II-level arrhythmia (including QT interval prolongation, for man = 450 ms, for woman = 470 ms) together with Class II cardiac dysfunction;\nFactors that could have an effect on oral medication (such as inability to swallow, chronic diarrhea and intestinal obstruction);\nSubjects with high gastrointestinal bleeding risk, including the following conditions: local active ulcer lesions with positive fecal occult blood test (++); history of black stool, or vomiting blood in the past 3 months;unresected primary lesion in stomach with positive fecal occult blood test (+), ulcerated gastric carcinoma with massive alimentary tract bleeding risk judged by PIs based on gastric endoscopy result;\nAbnormal Coagulation (INR>1.5<U+3001>APTT>1.5 UNL), with tendency of bleed;\nAssociated with CNS (central nervous system) metastases;\nPregnant or lactating women;\nOther conditions regimented at investigators\' discretion.\n\n\n### Response:\nSubjects with poor-controlled arterial hypertension (systolic blood pressure> 140 mmHg [AND] and diastolic blood pressure > 90 mm Hg) [AND] despite standard medical management; Coronary heart disease greater than ClassII; II-level arrhythmia (including QT interval prolongation, for man = 450 ms, for woman = 470 ms) together with Class II cardiac dysfunction;\nFactors that could have an effect on oral medication (such as [NOT] inability to swallow, chronic diarrhea [OR] and intestinal obstruction);\nSubjects with high gastrointestinal bleeding risk, including the following conditions: local active ulcer lesions [AND] with positive fecal occult blood test (++); history of black stool, [OR] or vomiting blood in the past 3 months;unresected primary lesion in stomach [AND] with positive fecal occult blood test (+), ulcerated gastric carcinoma [AND] with massive alimentary tract bleeding risk judged by PIs based on gastric endoscopy result;\nAbnormal Coagulation (INR>1.5<U+3001>APTT>1.5 UNL), with tendency of bleed;\nAssociated with CNS (central nervous system) metastases;\nPregnant [OR] or lactating women;\nOther conditions regimented at investigators\' discretion.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Subjects with poor-controlled arterial hypertension (systolic blood pressure> 140 mmHg [AND] and diastolic blood pressure > 90 mm Hg) [AND] despite standard medical management; Coronary heart disease greater than ClassII; II-level arrhythmia (including QT interval prolongation, for man = 450 ms, for woman = 470 ms) together with Class II cardiac dysfunction;
Factors that could have an effect on oral medication (such as [NOT] inability to swallow, chronic diarrhea [OR] and intestinal obstruction);
Subjects with high gastrointestinal bleeding risk, including the following conditions: local active ulcer lesions [AND] with positive fecal occult blood test (++); history of black stool, [OR] or vomiting blood in the past 3 months;unresected primary lesion in stomach [AND] with positive fecal occult blood test (+), ulcerated gastric carcinoma [AND] with massive alimentary tract bleeding risk judged by PIs based on gastric endoscopy result;
Abnormal Coagulation (INR>1.5<U+3001>APTT>1.5 UNL), with tendency of bleed;
Associated with CNS (central nervous system) metastases;
Pregnant [OR] or lactating women;
Other conditions regimented at investigators' discretion.
