Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nAge: 18 to75 years old;\nPathologically diagnosed with advanced gastric cancer (including adenocarcinoma of the gastroesophageal junction) with measurable metastases outside the stomach (measuring = 10mm on spiral CT scan, satisfying the criteria in RECIST 1.1);\nFailure of prior therapy (during or after treatment) in patients who have received at least two prior chemotherapy regimens;\nECOG PS of 0-2;\nHB = 90g / L\nANC = 1.5 × 109 / L\nPLT = 80 × 109 / L\nBilirubin <1.25 times the upper limit of normal (ULN)\nALT and AST <2.5 × ULN; liver metastases, if any, the ALT and AST<5 × ULN\nSerum Cr = 1 × ULN endogenous creatinine clearance>50ml/min (Cockcroft-Gault formula)\nAn expected survival of = 3 months;\nPatient received apatinib treatment regimen at investigators\' discretion;\nPatient has to voluntarily join the study and sign the Informed Consent Form for the study;\nPregnancy test (serum or urine) has to be performed for woman of childbearing age within 7 days before enrolment and the test result must be negative. They shall take appropriate methods for contraception during the study until the 8th week post the last administration of study drug. For men, (previous surgical sterilization accepted), shall agree to take appropriate methods of contraception during the study until the 8th week post the last administration of study drug.\n\n\n### Response:\nAge: 18 to75 years old;\nPathologically diagnosed with advanced gastric cancer (including adenocarcinoma of the gastroesophageal junction) [AND] with measurable metastases [NOT] outside the stomach (measuring = 10mm on spiral CT scan, satisfying the criteria in RECIST 1.1);\nFailure of prior therapy (during [OR] or after treatment) in patients [AND] who have received at least two prior chemotherapy regimens;\nECOG PS of 0-2;\nHB = 90g / L\n ANC = 1.5 × 109 / L\n PLT = 80 × 109 / L\nBilirubin <1.25 times the upper limit of normal (ULN)\n ALT [AND] and AST <2.5 × ULN; liver metastases, if any, the ALT [AND] and AST<5 × ULN\nSerum Cr = 1 × ULN endogenous creatinine clearance>50ml/min (Cockcroft-Gault formula)\nAn expected survival of = 3 months;\nPatient received apatinib treatment regimen at investigators\' discretion;\nPatient has to voluntarily join the study and sign the Informed Consent Form for the study;\nPregnancy test (serum [OR] or urine) has to be performed for woman of childbearing age within 7 days before enrolment and the test result must be negative. They shall take appropriate methods for contraception during the study until the 8th week post the last administration of study drug. For men, (previous surgical sterilization accepted), shall agree to take appropriate methods of contraception during the study until the 8th week post the last administration of study drug.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Age: 18 to75 years old;
Pathologically diagnosed with advanced gastric cancer (including adenocarcinoma of the gastroesophageal junction) [AND] with measurable metastases [NOT] outside the stomach (measuring = 10mm on spiral CT scan, satisfying the criteria in RECIST 1.1);
Failure of prior therapy (during [OR] or after treatment) in patients [AND] who have received at least two prior chemotherapy regimens;
ECOG PS of 0-2;
HB = 90g / L
 ANC = 1.5 × 109 / L
 PLT = 80 × 109 / L
Bilirubin <1.25 times the upper limit of normal (ULN)
 ALT [AND] and AST <2.5 × ULN; liver metastases, if any, the ALT [AND] and AST<5 × ULN
Serum Cr = 1 × ULN endogenous creatinine clearance>50ml/min (Cockcroft-Gault formula)
An expected survival of = 3 months;
Patient received apatinib treatment regimen at investigators' discretion;
Patient has to voluntarily join the study and sign the Informed Consent Form for the study;
Pregnancy test (serum [OR] or urine) has to be performed for woman of childbearing age within 7 days before enrolment and the test result must be negative. They shall take appropriate methods for contraception during the study until the 8th week post the last administration of study drug. For men, (previous surgical sterilization accepted), shall agree to take appropriate methods of contraception during the study until the 8th week post the last administration of study drug.
