suspected disorders of immunoglobulin synthesis.\nLeukemia, lymphomas of any type, melanoma, or other malignant neoplasms affecting the bone marrow or lymphatic systems.\nHas been diagnosed with cancer and who will be undergoing chemotherapy or radiation therapy during the vaccination healing time.\nIs a transplant recipient (except for corneal transplant).\nIs pregnant, planning pregnancy or breast feeding (female subjects of childbearing potential must have negative pregnancy test prior to vaccination).\nHousehold or other close/intimate contact(s) under the age of 12 months.\nHistory of allergies to phenol, any of the antibiotics listed in the vaccine content, or any other component of ACAM2000 or its diluents.\nSubjects with kidney disease (except kidney stones).\nSubjects with abnormal EKG at screening (if applicable). To mitigate the risk of enrolling at risk subjects and potentially jeopardizing subject safety an EKG will be performed prior to vaccination with ACAM2000 smallpox vaccine in all potential subjects =50 years old and for all potential subjects <50 with two cardiac risk factors as listed immediately below including; severely or morbidly obese or higher obesity classification (BMI =36); high blood pressure; high blood cholesterol; diabetes or high blood sugar; a first degree relative who had a heart condition before the age of 50; and current tobacco smokers.\nSeverely or morbidly obese or higher obesity classification (BMI =36)\nHigh blood pressure diagnosed by a doctor\nHigh blood cholesterol diagnosed by a doctor\nDiabetes or high blood sugar diagnosed by a doctor\nA first degree relative (for example, mother, father, brother, sister) who had a heart condition before the age of 50\nCurrently smokes tobacco (cigarettes)\nArrhythmia\nSyncope related to cardiac disease\nPrevious myocardial infarction\nAngina\nCoronary artery disease\nCongestive heart failure\nCardiomyopathy\nStroke or transient ischemic attack\nMyocarditis\nPericarditis\nChest pain or shortness of breath with activity (such as climbing stairs), peripheral edema, heart palpitations, dry cough, irregular heartbeat, excessive fatigue, unexplained syncope\nOther heart conditions being treated by a physician\n\n\n### Response:\nHistory of severe related adverse event(s) from previous participation in VA-001 [OR] or VA-006 trials [OR] or to any smallpox vaccination.\nEczema, history of eczema, [OR] exfoliative skin conditions, [OR] wounds, [OR] burns, [OR] or other skin conditions at the investigator\'s discretion.\nA history of immunodeficiency.\nCurrently [OR] or has recently received radiotherapy [OR] or chemotherapy, [OR] adrenocorticotropic hormone (ACTH), [OR] corticosteroids, [OR] or immunosuppressive drugs.\nEye disease treated with topical steroids.\nKnown [OR] or suspected disorders of immunoglobulin synthesis.\nLeukemia, [OR] lymphomas of any type, [OR] melanoma, [OR] or other malignant neoplasms affecting the bone marrow [OR] or lymphatic systems.\nHas been diagnosed with cancer [AND] and who will be undergoing chemotherapy [OR] or radiation therapy during the vaccination healing time.\nIs a transplant recipient (except for corneal transplant).\nIs pregnant, [OR] planning pregnancy [OR] or breast feeding (female subjects of childbearing potential must have negative pregnancy test prior to vaccination).\nHousehold [OR] or other close/ [OR] intimate contact(s) under the age of 12 months.\nHistory of allergies to phenol, any of the antibiotics listed in the vaccine content, [OR] or any other component of ACAM2000 [OR] or its diluents.\nSubjects with kidney disease (except kidney stones).\n Subjects with abnormal EKG at screening (if applicable). To mitigate the risk of enrolling at risk subjects and potentially jeopardizing subject safety an EKG will be performed prior to vaccination with ACAM2000 smallpox vaccine in all potential subjects =50 years old [AND] and for all potential subjects <50 [AND] with two cardiac risk factors as listed immediately below including; severely [OR] or morbidly obese [OR] or higher obesity classification (BMI =36); high blood pressure; high blood cholesterol; diabetes [OR] or high blood sugar; a first degree relative [AND] who had a heart condition before the age of 50; and current tobacco smokers.\nSeverely [OR] or morbidly obese [OR] or higher obesity classification (BMI =36)\nHigh blood pressure diagnosed by a doctor\n High blood cholesterol diagnosed by a doctor\n Diabetes [OR] or high blood sugar diagnosed by a doctor\n A first degree relative (for example, mother, [OR] father, [OR] brother, [OR] sister) who had a heart condition before the age of 50\n Currently smokes tobacco (cigarettes)\n Arrhythmia\n Syncope related to cardiac disease\n Previous myocardial infarction\n Angina\n Coronary artery disease\n Congestive heart failure\n Cardiomyopathy\n Stroke [OR] or transient ischemic attack\n Myocarditis\n Pericarditis\n Chest pain [OR] or shortness of breath [AND] with activity (such as climbing stairs), peripheral edema, [OR] heart palpitations, [OR] dry cough, [OR] irregular heartbeat, [OR] excessive fatigue, [OR] unexplained syncope\n Other heart conditions being treated by a physician<|eot_id|>']
