Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nParents refusal\nCognitive impairment\nDifficulty in communication due to language issues\nPsychiatric disorder\nSevere systematic disorder\nKnown allergy to any drug used\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nSevere Pre-Eclampsia defined by\n  -  Symptoms of central nervous system dysfunction (New onset cerebral [OR] or visual disturbance, such as: Photopsia, [OR] scotomata, [OR] cortical blindness, [OR] retinal vasospasm)\n  -  Severe headache\n  -  Fatigue\n  -  Nausea [OR] and vomiting\n  -  Abdominal pain\n  -  Severe blood pressure elevation Systolic blood pressure ≥160 mmHg [OR] or diastolic blood pressure ≥110 mmHg on two occasions at least four hours apart while the patient is on bedrest (unless the patient is on antihypertensive therapy)\n  -  Thrombocytopenia (<100,000 platelets/microL)\n  -  Renal failure (creatinine >1.1 mg/dL [OR] or doubling of serum creatinine concentration in the absence of other renal disease)\n  -  Pulmonary edema\n     1. Patients with more than one of the above criteria\n     2. Patients with any contraindication to Magnesium Sulfate including severe renal impairment or myasthenia gravis.\nExclusion Criteria:\n- Patients with more than one contraindication to Magnesium Sulfate\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nSevere Pre-Eclampsia defined by\n - Symptoms of central nervous system dysfunction (New onset cerebral [OR] or visual disturbance, such as: Photopsia, [OR] scotomata, [OR] cortical blindness, [OR] retinal vasospasm)\n - Severe headache\n - Fatigue\n - Nausea [OR] and vomiting\n - Abdominal pain\n - Severe blood pressure elevation Systolic blood pressure  ≥160 mmHg [OR] or diastolic blood pressure ≥110 mmHg on two occasions at least four hours apart while the patient is on bedrest (unless the patient is on antihypertensive therapy)\n - Thrombocytopenia (<100,000 platelets/microL)\n - Renal failure (creatinine >1.1 mg/dL [OR] or doubling of serum creatinine concentration in the [NOT] absence of other renal disease)\n - Pulmonary edema\n 1. Patients with more than one of the above criteria\n 2. Patients with any contraindication to Magnesium Sulfate including severe renal impairment [OR] or myasthenia gravis.\nExclusion Criteria:\n- Patients with more than one contraindication to Magnesium Sulfate<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Severe Pre-Eclampsia defined by
  -  Symptoms of central nervous system dysfunction (New onset cerebral [OR] or visual disturbance, such as: Photopsia, [OR] scotomata, [OR] cortical blindness, [OR] retinal vasospasm)
  -  Severe headache
  -  Fatigue
  -  Nausea [OR] and vomiting
  -  Abdominal pain
  -  Severe blood pressure elevation Systolic blood pressure ≥160 mmHg [OR] or diastolic blood pressure ≥110 mmHg on two occasions at least four hours apart while the patient is on bedrest (unless the patient is on antihypertensive therapy)
  -  Thrombocytopenia (<100,000 platelets/microL)
  -  Renal failure (creatinine >1.1 mg/dL [OR] or doubling of serum creatinine concentration in the absence of other renal disease)
  -  Pulmonary edema
     1. Patients with more than one of the above criteria
     2. Patients with any contraindication to Magnesium Sulfate including severe renal impairment or myasthenia gravis.
Exclusion Criteria:
- Patients with more than one contraindication to Magnesium Sulfate
