Das File: /work/eauten2s/ec_criteria_struct/chia/input/chia_text_half/NCT02462590_exc.txt wurde erfolgreich geladen.
Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInvasively mechanically ventilated >72 hours at the time of screening;\nPatients at potential increased risk of iatrogenic probiotic infection (see Section 2.6 for detailed explanation) including specific immunocompromised populations (HIV <200 CD4 cells/µL, those receiving chronic immunosuppressive medications (e.g., azathioprine, cyclosporine, cyclophosphamide, tacrolimus, methotrexate, mycofenolate, Anti-IL2), previous transplantation (including stem cell) at any time, malignancy requiring chemotherapy in the last 3 months, neutropenia [absolute neutrophil count < 500]). However, patients receiving corticosteroids previously or presently or projected to receive corticosteroids are not excluded;\nPatients at risk for endovascular infection (previously documented rheumatic heart disease, congenital valve disease, surgically repaired congenital heart disease, unrepaired cyanotic congenital heart disease, any intracardiac repair with prosthetic material [mechanical or bio-prosthetic cardiac valves], previous or current endocarditis, permanent endovascular devices (e.g., endovascular grafts [e.g., aortic aneurysm repair, stents involving large arteries such as aorta, femorals and carotids], inferior vena cava filters, dialysis vascular grafts), tunnelled (not short-term) hemodialysis catheters, pacemakers or defibrillators. Patients with temporary central venous catheters, central venous dialysis catheters or peripherally inserted central catheters (PICCs) are not excluded and patients with coronary artery stents, coronary artery bypass grafts (CABG) or neurovascular coils are not excluded; patients with mitral valve prolapse or bicuspid aortic valve are not excluded providing they have no other exclusion criteria;\nPatients with a primary diagnosis of severe acute pancreatitis, without reference to a Ranson score [Ranson 1974]). However, patients with mild or moderate pancreatitis are not excluded;\nPatients with percutaneous gastric or jejunal feeding tubes already in situ as per Health Canada guidance;\nStrict contraindication or inability to receive enteral medications;\nIntent to withdraw advanced life support as per the ICU physician;\nPrevious enrolment in this or current enrolment in a potentially confounding tria\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nInvasively mechanically ventilated >72 hours at the time of screening;\nPatients at potential increased risk of iatrogenic probiotic infection (see Section 2.6 for detailed explanation) including specific immunocompromised populations (HIV <200 CD4 cells/µL, those receiving chronic immunosuppressive medications (e.g., azathioprine, [OR] cyclosporine, [OR] cyclophosphamide, [OR] tacrolimus, [OR] methotrexate, [OR] mycofenolate, [OR] Anti-IL2), previous transplantation (including stem cell) at any time, malignancy requiring chemotherapy in the last 3 months, [OR] neutropenia [absolute neutrophil count < 500]). However, patients receiving corticosteroids previously [OR] or presently [OR] or projected to receive corticosteroids are [NOT] not [NOT] excluded;\nPatients at risk for endovascular infection (previously documented rheumatic heart disease, [OR] congenital valve disease, [OR] surgically repaired congenital heart disease, [OR] unrepaired cyanotic congenital heart disease, any intracardiac repair with prosthetic material [mechanical [OR] or bio-prosthetic cardiac valves], previous [OR] or current endocarditis, permanent endovascular devices (e.g., endovascular grafts [e.g., aortic aneurysm repair, [OR] stents involving large arteries such as aorta, [OR] femorals [OR] and carotids], inferior vena cava filters, [OR] dialysis vascular grafts), tunnelled ([NOT] not short-term) hemodialysis catheters, [OR] pacemakers [OR] or defibrillators. Patients with temporary central venous catheters, [OR] central venous dialysis catheters [OR] or peripherally inserted central catheters (PICCs) are [NOT] not [NOT] excluded and patients with coronary artery stents, [OR] coronary artery bypass grafts (CABG) [OR] or neurovascular coils are [NOT] not [NOT] excluded; patients with mitral valve prolapse [OR] or bicuspid aortic valve are [NOT] not [NOT] excluded providing they have [NOT] no other exclusion criteria;\nPatients with a primary diagnosis of severe acute pancreatitis, [NOT] without reference to a Ranson score [Ranson 1974]). However, patients with mild [OR] or moderate pancreatitis are [NOT] not [NOT] excluded;\nPatients with percutaneous gastric [OR] or jejunal feeding tubes already in situ as per Health Canada guidance;\nStrict contraindication [OR] or [NOT] inability to receive enteral medications;\nIntent to [NOT] withdraw advanced life support as per the ICU physician;\nPrevious enrolment in this or current enrolment in a potentially confounding trial<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Invasively mechanically ventilated >72 hours at the time of screening;
Patients at potential increased risk of iatrogenic probiotic infection (see Section 2.6 for detailed explanation) including specific immunocompromised populations (HIV <200 CD4 cells/µL, those receiving chronic immunosuppressive medications (e.g., azathioprine, [OR] cyclosporine, [OR] cyclophosphamide, [OR] tacrolimus, [OR] methotrexate, [OR] mycofenolate, [OR] Anti-IL2), previous transplantation (including stem cell) at any time, malignancy requiring chemotherapy in the last 3 months, [OR] neutropenia [absolute neutrophil count < 500]). However, patients receiving corticosteroids previously [OR] or presently [OR] or projected to receive corticosteroids are [NOT] not [NOT] excluded;
Patients at risk for endovascular infection (previously documented rheumatic heart disease, [OR] congenital valve disease, [OR] surgically repaired congenital heart disease, [OR] unrepaired cyanotic congenital heart disease, any intracardiac repair with prosthetic material [mechanical [OR] or bio-prosthetic cardiac valves], previous [OR] or current endocarditis, permanent endovascular devices (e.g., endovascular grafts [e.g., aortic aneurysm repair, [OR] stents involving large arteries such as aorta, [OR] femorals [OR] and carotids], inferior vena cava filters, [OR] dialysis vascular grafts), tunnelled ([NOT] not short-term) hemodialysis catheters, [OR] pacemakers [OR] or defibrillators. Patients with temporary central venous catheters, [OR] central venous dialysis catheters [OR] or peripherally inserted central catheters (PICCs) are [NOT] not [NOT] excluded and patients with coronary artery stents, [OR] coronary artery bypass grafts (CABG) [OR] or neurovascular coils are [NOT] not [NOT] excluded; patients with mitral valve prolapse [OR] or bicuspid aortic valve are [NOT] not [NOT] excluded providing they have [NOT] no other exclusion criteria;
Patients with a primary diagnosis of severe acute pancreatitis, [NOT] without reference to a Ranson score [Ranson 1974]). However, patients with mild [OR] or moderate pancreatitis are [NOT] not [NOT] excluded;
Patients with percutaneous gastric [OR] or jejunal feeding tubes already in situ as per Health Canada guidance;
Strict contraindication [OR] or [NOT] inability to receive enteral medications;
Intent to [NOT] withdraw advanced life support as per the ICU physician;
Previous enrolment in this or current enrolment in a potentially confounding trial
