File: NCT02478346_exc 

Das File: /work/eauten2s/ec_criteria_struct/chia/input/chia_text_half/NCT02478346_exc.txt wurde erfolgreich geladen.
Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nNA\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\n  -  1. Refractory or relapsed AML which will include:\n       -  Refractory disease will be defined as at least 1 prior treatment with no remission.\n       -  Relapsed disease will be defined as 5% or more blasts in bone marrow seen after remission.\n       -  Patients with AML arising from myelodysplastic syndromes (including CMML) or myeloproliferative neoplasms (secondary AML, ts-AML) are also eligible.\n  -  2. Circulating blast count ≤ 200/μL within 10 days prior to first cycle of treatment. Hydroxyurea should be used to keep the peripheral blast count ≤ 200/μL until the first day of protocol treatment, to the extent that this is possible\n  -  3. ECOG ≤ 2\n  -  4. Estimated creatinine clearance ≥ 50 mL/min\n  -  5. AST and ALT ≤ 3.0 x ULN\n  -  6. Bilirubin ≤ 3.0 x ULN\nExclusion Criteria:\n  -  1. Active CNS Leukemia.\n  -  2. Known HIV infection or known hepatitis B or hepatitis C infection (with a detectable viral load).\n  -  3. Participant has received strong and/or moderate CYP3A inducers within 7 days prior to the initiation of study treatment.\n  -  4. Have received prior radiation to maximally tolerated levels to any critical normal organ.\n  -  5. Clinically significant cardiac disease.\n  -  6. Active, uncontrolled serious infection.\n  -  7. Have other non-myeloid malignancy within 2 years of entry (with exceptions).\n  -  8. Psychiatric disorder that would preclude study participation\n  -  9. Previous solid organ transplant (prior treatment with SCT is allowed but not if patient has GVHD or is still receiving immunosuppression/GVHD therapy).\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\n - 1. Refractory [OR] or relapsed AML which will include:\n - Refractory disease will be defined as at least 1 prior treatment [AND] with [NOT] no remission.\n - Relapsed disease will be defined as 5% or more blasts in bone marrow seen after remission.\n - Patients with AML arising from myelodysplastic syndromes (including CMML) [OR] or myeloproliferative neoplasms (secondary AML, [OR] ts-AML) are also eligible.\n - 2. Circulating blast count ≤ 200/μL within 10 days prior to first cycle of treatment. Hydroxyurea should be used to keep the peripheral blast count ≤ 200/μL until the first day of protocol treatment, to the extent that this is possible\n - 3. ECOG ≤ 2\n - 4. Estimated creatinine clearance ≥ 50 mL/min\n - 5. AST [AND] and ALT ≤ 3.0 x ULN\n - 6. Bilirubin ≤ 3.0 x ULN\nExclusion Criteria:\n - 1. Active CNS Leukemia.\n - 2. Known HIV infection [OR] or known hepatitis B [OR] or hepatitis C infection (with a detectable viral load).\n - 3. Participant has received strong [OR] and/or moderate CYP3A inducers within 7 days prior to the initiation of study treatment.\n - 4. Have received prior radiation to maximally tolerated levels to any critical normal organ.\n - 5. Clinically significant cardiac disease.\n - 6. Active, uncontrolled serious infection.\n - 7. Have other [NOT] non-myeloid malignancy within 2 years of entry (with exceptions).\n - 8. Psychiatric disorder that would [NOT] preclude study participation\n - 9. Previous solid organ transplant (prior treatment with SCT is allowed [AND] but [NOT] not if patient has GVHD [OR] or is still receiving immunosuppression/ [OR] GVHD therapy).<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
  -  1. Refractory or relapsed AML which will include:
       -  Refractory disease will be defined as at least 1 prior treatment with no remission.
       -  Relapsed disease will be defined as 5% or more blasts in bone marrow seen after remission.
       -  Patients with AML arising from myelodysplastic syndromes (including CMML) or myeloproliferative neoplasms (secondary AML, ts-AML) are also eligible.
  -  2. Circulating blast count ≤ 200/μL within 10 days prior to first cycle of treatment. Hydroxyurea should be used to keep the peripheral blast count ≤ 200/μL until the first day of protocol treatment, to the extent that this is possible
  -  3. ECOG ≤ 2
  -  4. Estimated creatinine clearance ≥ 50 mL/min
  -  5. AST and ALT ≤ 3.0 x ULN
  -  6. Bilirubin ≤ 3.0 x ULN
Exclusion Criteria:
  -  1. Active CNS Leukemia.
  -  2. Known HIV infection or known hepatitis B or hepatitis C infection (with a detectable viral load).
  -  3. Participant has received strong and/or moderate CYP3A inducers within 7 days prior to the initiation of study treatment.
  -  4. Have received prior radiation to maximally tolerated levels to any critical normal organ.
  -  5. Clinically significant cardiac disease.
  -  6. Active, uncontrolled serious infection.
  -  7. Have other non-myeloid malignancy within 2 years of entry (with exceptions).
  -  8. Psychiatric disorder that would preclude study participation
  -  9. Previous solid organ transplant (prior treatment with SCT is allowed but not if patient has GVHD or is still receiving immunosuppression/GVHD therapy).
