Das File: /work/eauten2s/ec_criteria_struct/chia/input/chia_text_half/NCT02502734_exc.txt wurde erfolgreich geladen.
Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nA history of life-threatening asthma defined for this protocol as an asthma episode that required intubation, hypercapnea requiring non-invasive ventilatory support, respiratory arrest, hypoxic seizures or asthma-related syncopal episode(s). \nSubjects with a history of asthma exacerbation requiring the use of systemic corticosteroids (tablets, suspension, or injection) for at least 3 days or a depot corticosteroid injection or emergency room attendance (within 3 months) or requiring hospitalization for asthma (within 6 months) prior to screening. \nSignificant, non-reversible active pulmonary disease (e.g. cystic fibrosis, bronchiectasis, tuberculosis). \nCulture-documented or suspected bacterial or viral infection of the upper or lower respiratory tract, sinus or middle ear that is not resolved within 4 weeks of Visit 1 and led to a change in asthma management or, in the opinion of the Investigator, is expected to affect the subject\'s asthma status or the subject\'s ability to participate in the study. \nAny fracture in the leg to be measured within 6 months prior to the screening visit. \nAny metabolic disorders or other diseases that may impact on normal growth patterns. \nNo major surgery requiring general anaesthesia for at least 3 months prior to the screening visit. \nNo febrile illnesses with temperature >39 degree celsius for more than five consecutive days within the week preceding the Screening Visit. \nAny significant abnormality or medical condition identified at the screening medical assessment (including serious psychological disorder) that in the Investigator\'s opinion, preclude entry into the study due to risk to the subject or that may interfere with the outcome of the study. \nClinical visual evidence of candidiasis at Visit 1 (Screening). \nUse of any of the prohibited medications listed in protocol. \nStrenuous physical exercise within 3 hours of Visit 1 (Screening) \nDrug allergies: Any adverse reaction including immediate or delayed hypersensitivity to any intranasal, inhaled, or systemic corticosteroid therapy. Known or suspected sensitivity to the constituents of the ELLIPTA Inhaler (i.e., lactose, FF). \nMilk Protein Allergy: History of severe milk protein allergy. \nThe subject has participated in a clinical trial and has received an investigational product within the following time period prior to the first dosing day in the current study: 30 days, 5 half-lives or twice the duration of the biological effect of the investigational product (whichever is longer). \nExposure to more than 4 investigational medicinal products within 12 months prior to the first dosing day. \nUnable to use the ELLIPTA inhaler and peak flow meter correctly. \nAn affiliation with the Investigator site: the parents/guardians or child is an immediate family member of the participating Investigator, sub-Investigator, study coordinator, or employee of the participating Investigator. \nThe Parent or Guardian has a history of psychiatric disease, intellectual deficiency, substance abuse or other condition (e.g. inability to read, comprehend or write) which may affect: validity of consent to participate in the study; adequate supervision of the subject during the study; compliance of subject with study medication and study procedures (e.g. completion of daily diary, attending scheduled clinic visits); subject safety and well-being. \nChildren in care: Children who are wards of the government or state are not eligible for participation in this study.       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nA history of life-threatening asthma defined for this protocol as an asthma episode that required intubation, [OR] hypercapnea requiring [NOT] non-invasive ventilatory support, [OR] respiratory arrest, [OR] hypoxic seizures [OR] or asthma-related syncopal episode(s). \nSubjects with a history of asthma exacerbation requiring the use of systemic corticosteroids (tablets, [OR] suspension, [OR] or injection) for at least 3 days [OR] or a depot corticosteroid injection [OR] or emergency room attendance (within 3 months) [OR] or requiring hospitalization for asthma (within 6 months) prior to screening. \nSignificant, [NOT] non-reversible active pulmonary disease (e.g. cystic fibrosis, [OR] bronchiectasis, [OR] tuberculosis). \nCulture-documented [OR] or suspected bacterial [OR] or viral infection of the upper [OR] or lower respiratory tract, [OR] sinus [OR] or middle ear that is [NOT] not resolved within 4 weeks of Visit 1 [AND] and led to a change in asthma management [OR] or, in the opinion of the Investigator, is expected to affect the subject\'s asthma status [OR] or the subject\'s ability to participate in the study. \nAny fracture in the leg to be measured within 6 months prior to the screening visit. \nAny metabolic disorders [OR] or other diseases that may impact on normal growth patterns. \n [NOT] No major surgery requiring general anaesthesia for at least 3 months prior to the screening visit. \n [NOT] No febrile illnesses [AND] with temperature >39 degree celsius for more than five consecutive days within the week preceding the Screening Visit. \nAny significant abnormality [OR] or medical condition identified at the screening medical assessment (including serious psychological disorder) that in the Investigator\'s opinion, [NOT] preclude entry into the study due to risk to the subject [OR] or that may interfere with the outcome of the study. \nClinical visual evidence of candidiasis at Visit 1 (Screening). \nUse of any of the prohibited medications listed in protocol. \nStrenuous physical exercise within 3 hours of Visit 1 (Screening) \nDrug allergies: Any adverse reaction including immediate [OR] or delayed hypersensitivity to any intranasal, [OR] inhaled, [OR] or systemic corticosteroid therapy. Known [OR] or suspected sensitivity to the constituents of the ELLIPTA Inhaler (i.e., lactose, [OR] FF). \nMilk Protein Allergy: History of severe milk protein allergy. \nThe subject has participated in a clinical trial [AND] and has received an investigational product within the following time period prior to the first dosing day in the current study: 30 days, 5 half-lives [OR] or twice the duration of the biological effect of the investigational product (whichever is longer). \nExposure to more than 4 investigational medicinal products within 12 months prior to the first dosing day. \nUnable to use the ELLIPTA inhaler [AND] and peak flow meter correctly. \nAn affiliation with the Investigator site: the parents/guardians [OR] or child is an immediate family member of the participating Investigator, sub-Investigator, study coordinator, [OR] or employee of the participating Investigator. \nThe Parent [OR] or Guardian has a history of psychiatric disease, [OR] intellectual deficiency, [OR] substance abuse [OR] or other condition (e.g. [NOT] inability to read, comprehend [OR] or write) which may affect: validity of consent to participate in the study; adequate supervision of the subject during the study; compliance of subject with study medication [AND] and study procedures (e.g. completion of daily diary, [AND] attending scheduled clinic visits); subject safety [AND] and well-being. \nChildren in care: Children [AND] who are wards of the government [OR] or state are [NOT] not eligible for participation in this study.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
A history of life-threatening asthma defined for this protocol as an asthma episode that required intubation, [OR] hypercapnea requiring [NOT] non-invasive ventilatory support, [OR] respiratory arrest, [OR] hypoxic seizures [OR] or asthma-related syncopal episode(s). 
Subjects with a history of asthma exacerbation requiring the use of systemic corticosteroids (tablets, [OR] suspension, [OR] or injection) for at least 3 days [OR] or a depot corticosteroid injection [OR] or emergency room attendance (within 3 months) [OR] or requiring hospitalization for asthma (within 6 months) prior to screening. 
Significant, [NOT] non-reversible active pulmonary disease (e.g. cystic fibrosis, [OR] bronchiectasis, [OR] tuberculosis). 
Culture-documented [OR] or suspected bacterial [OR] or viral infection of the upper [OR] or lower respiratory tract, [OR] sinus [OR] or middle ear that is [NOT] not resolved within 4 weeks of Visit 1 [AND] and led to a change in asthma management [OR] or, in the opinion of the Investigator, is expected to affect the subject's asthma status [OR] or the subject's ability to participate in the study. 
Any fracture in the leg to be measured within 6 months prior to the screening visit. 
Any metabolic disorders [OR] or other diseases that may impact on normal growth patterns. 
 [NOT] No major surgery requiring general anaesthesia for at least 3 months prior to the screening visit. 
 [NOT] No febrile illnesses [AND] with temperature >39 degree celsius for more than five consecutive days within the week preceding the Screening Visit. 
Any significant abnormality [OR] or medical condition identified at the screening medical assessment (including serious psychological disorder) that in the Investigator's opinion, [NOT] preclude entry into the study due to risk to the subject [OR] or that may interfere with the outcome of the study. 
Clinical visual evidence of candidiasis at Visit 1 (Screening). 
Use of any of the prohibited medications listed in protocol. 
Strenuous physical exercise within 3 hours of Visit 1 (Screening) 
Drug allergies: Any adverse reaction including immediate [OR] or delayed hypersensitivity to any intranasal, [OR] inhaled, [OR] or systemic corticosteroid therapy. Known [OR] or suspected sensitivity to the constituents of the ELLIPTA Inhaler (i.e., lactose, [OR] FF). 
Milk Protein Allergy: History of severe milk protein allergy. 
The subject has participated in a clinical trial [AND] and has received an investigational product within the following time period prior to the first dosing day in the current study: 30 days, 5 half-lives [OR] or twice the duration of the biological effect of the investigational product (whichever is longer). 
Exposure to more than 4 investigational medicinal products within 12 months prior to the first dosing day. 
Unable to use the ELLIPTA inhaler [AND] and peak flow meter correctly. 
An affiliation with the Investigator site: the parents/guardians [OR] or child is an immediate family member of the participating Investigator, sub-Investigator, study coordinator, [OR] or employee of the participating Investigator. 
The Parent [OR] or Guardian has a history of psychiatric disease, [OR] intellectual deficiency, [OR] substance abuse [OR] or other condition (e.g. [NOT] inability to read, comprehend [OR] or write) which may affect: validity of consent to participate in the study; adequate supervision of the subject during the study; compliance of subject with study medication [AND] and study procedures (e.g. completion of daily diary, [AND] attending scheduled clinic visits); subject safety [AND] and well-being. 
Children in care: Children [AND] who are wards of the government [OR] or state are [NOT] not eligible for participation in this study.
