File: NCT02510404_inc 

Das File: /work/eauten2s/ec_criteria_struct/chia/input/chia_text_half/NCT02510404_inc.txt wurde erfolgreich geladen.
Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\n1. Diagnosis of primary immunodeficiency with established plan to undergo myeloablative or non-myeloablative allogeneic hematopoietic stem cell transplant for treatment thereof or diagnosis of a form of primary immunodeficiency for which hematopoietic stem cell transplantation is not indicated. \n2. Active infection with EBV, CMV, and/or Adenovirus, unable to be successfully controlled with standard therapy. \n3. Steroids less than 0.5 mg/kg/day prednisone \n4. Karnofsky/Lansky score of ≥ 50 \n5. ANC greater than 500/µL. \n6. Bilirubin <2x, AST <3x, Serum creatinine <2x upper limit of normal, Hgb >8.0 \n7. Pulse oximetry of > 90% on room air \n8. Negative pregnancy test (if female of childbearing potential) \n9. Patient or parent/guardian capable of providing informed consent. \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\n 1. Diagnosis of primary immunodeficiency [AND] with established plan to undergo myeloablative [OR] or [NOT] non-myeloablative allogeneic hematopoietic stem cell transplant for treatment thereof [OR] or diagnosis of a form of primary immunodeficiency for which hematopoietic stem cell transplantation is [NOT] not indicated. \n 2. Active infection with EBV, [OR] CMV, [OR] and/or Adenovirus, [NOT] unable to be successfully controlled with standard therapy. \n 3. Steroids less than 0.5 mg/kg/day prednisone \n 4. Karnofsky/ [OR] Lansky score of ≥ 50 \n 5. ANC greater than 500/µL. \n 6. Bilirubin <2x, AST <3x, Serum creatinine <2x upper limit of normal, Hgb >8.0 \n 7. Pulse oximetry of > 90% on room air \n 8. Negative pregnancy test (if female of childbearing potential) \n 9. Patient or parent/guardian capable of providing informed consent.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
 1. Diagnosis of primary immunodeficiency [AND] with established plan to undergo myeloablative [OR] or [NOT] non-myeloablative allogeneic hematopoietic stem cell transplant for treatment thereof [OR] or diagnosis of a form of primary immunodeficiency for which hematopoietic stem cell transplantation is [NOT] not indicated. 
 2. Active infection with EBV, [OR] CMV, [OR] and/or Adenovirus, [NOT] unable to be successfully controlled with standard therapy. 
 3. Steroids less than 0.5 mg/kg/day prednisone 
 4. Karnofsky/ [OR] Lansky score of ≥ 50 
 5. ANC greater than 500/µL. 
 6. Bilirubin <2x, AST <3x, Serum creatinine <2x upper limit of normal, Hgb >8.0 
 7. Pulse oximetry of > 90% on room air 
 8. Negative pregnancy test (if female of childbearing potential) 
 9. Patient or parent/guardian capable of providing informed consent.
