Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nPatients will be excluded if they have had exposure to a total daily dose of MET 1000 mg bid for at least 2 weeks in the past 3 months;\nPatients will be excluded if they could not tolerate MET during the recommended titration schedule outlined in the protocol;\nMajor neurological or medical illnesses that affect weight gain (e.g., unstable thyroid disease) or require a systemic medication that might impact weight or glucose regulation (e.g., diabetes mellitus [insulin], chronic renal failure [steroids]);\nFasting glucose = 126 mg/dL on 2 occasions during screening indicating need for prompt treatment;\nIf lab results are available in the last 6 months, then a serum creatinine =1.3 mg/dL on 2 occasions during screening and/or follow-up, indicating potential impairment of renal functioning;\nPregnant or breast feeding;\nChildren and caregivers who are unable to complete assessments for any reason;\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nPatients will be included if they have had exposure to a total daily dose of MET 1000 mg bid for less than 2 weeks in the past 3 months;\nPatients will be included if they could tolerate MET during the recommended titration schedule outlined in the protocol;\nMajor neurological [OR] or medical illnesses that [NOT] do [NOT] not affect weight gain (e.g., unstable thyroid disease) [OR] or require a systemic medication that might impact weight [OR] or glucose regulation (e.g., diabetes mellitus [insulin], chronic renal failure [steroids]);\nFasting glucose = 126 mg/dL on 2 occasions during screening indicating need for prompt treatment;\nIf lab results are available in the last 6 months, then a serum creatinine =1.3 mg/dL on 2 occasions during screening [OR] and/or follow-up, indicating potential impairment of renal functioning;\nPregnant [OR] or breast feeding;\nChildren [OR] and caregivers who are unable to complete assessments for any reason;<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Patients will be included if they have had exposure to a total daily dose of MET 1000 mg bid for less than 2 weeks in the past 3 months;
Patients will be included if they could tolerate MET during the recommended titration schedule outlined in the protocol;
Major neurological [OR] or medical illnesses that [NOT] do [NOT] not affect weight gain (e.g., unstable thyroid disease) [OR] or require a systemic medication that might impact weight [OR] or glucose regulation (e.g., diabetes mellitus [insulin], chronic renal failure [steroids]);
Fasting glucose = 126 mg/dL on 2 occasions during screening indicating need for prompt treatment;
If lab results are available in the last 6 months, then a serum creatinine =1.3 mg/dL on 2 occasions during screening [OR] and/or follow-up, indicating potential impairment of renal functioning;
Pregnant [OR] or breast feeding;
Children [OR] and caregivers who are unable to complete assessments for any reason;
