Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nInpatient or outpatient age 8-19 years inclusive; participants must live with a parent, guardian, or caregiver;\nFluent in English;\nDiagnosed or told by a clinician that they have any of the following bipolar spectrum disorders (BSD): bipolar I, bipolar II, unspecified bipolar and related disorders, Disruptive Mood Dysregulation Disorder (DMDD), cyclothymic disorder, other specified bipolar and related disorders, as well as mood disorder not otherwise specified (if diagnosed in the past as per DSM-IV);\nBody mass index >85%ile for age and sex by standard growth charts;\nReceived a new or ongoing prescription for at least one SGA (i.e., olanzapine, clozapine, risperidone, quetiapine, aripiprazole, ziprasidone, iloperidone, lurasidone, paliperidone, brexpiprazole or cariprazine) that is not prescribed as a PRN medication;\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nInpatient [OR] or outpatient age 8-19 years inclusive; participants must live with a parent, guardian, [OR] or caregiver;\nFluent in English;\nDiagnosed [OR] or told by a clinician that they have any of the following bipolar spectrum disorders (BSD): bipolar I, [OR] bipolar II, [OR] unspecified bipolar [OR] and related disorders, [OR] Disruptive Mood Dysregulation Disorder (DMDD), [OR] cyclothymic disorder, other specified bipolar [OR] and related disorders, as well as mood disorder not otherwise specified (if diagnosed in the past as per DSM-IV);\nBody mass index >85%ile for age and sex by standard growth charts;\nReceived a new [OR] or ongoing prescription for at least one SGA (i.e., olanzapine, [OR] clozapine, [OR] risperidone, [OR] quetiapine, [OR] aripiprazole, [OR] ziprasidone, [OR] iloperidone, [OR] lurasidone, [OR] paliperidone, [OR] brexpiprazole [OR] or cariprazine) that is [NOT] not prescribed as a PRN medication;<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Inpatient [OR] or outpatient age 8-19 years inclusive; participants must live with a parent, guardian, [OR] or caregiver;
Fluent in English;
Diagnosed [OR] or told by a clinician that they have any of the following bipolar spectrum disorders (BSD): bipolar I, [OR] bipolar II, [OR] unspecified bipolar [OR] and related disorders, [OR] Disruptive Mood Dysregulation Disorder (DMDD), [OR] cyclothymic disorder, other specified bipolar [OR] and related disorders, as well as mood disorder not otherwise specified (if diagnosed in the past as per DSM-IV);
Body mass index >85%ile for age and sex by standard growth charts;
Received a new [OR] or ongoing prescription for at least one SGA (i.e., olanzapine, [OR] clozapine, [OR] risperidone, [OR] quetiapine, [OR] aripiprazole, [OR] ziprasidone, [OR] iloperidone, [OR] lurasidone, [OR] paliperidone, [OR] brexpiprazole [OR] or cariprazine) that is [NOT] not prescribed as a PRN medication;
