Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nMajor depressive disorder with psychotic features\nTraumatic Brain Injury (TBI) with a clear impact on activities of daily living\nDevelopmental delay, intellectual deficit, and/or severe educational disability resulting in some dependence for activities of daily living\nOngoing substance use disorder with significant impact on activities of daily living. Difficult or impossible to determine whether cognitive or functional decline is due to substance use or HIV, or both\nEvidence of intoxication or withdrawal during the screening evaluation\nCentral nervous system (CNS) infections or opportunistic conditions: brain abscess (bacterial, mycobacterial, fungal or Toxoplasma), meningitis with persistent neurologic impairment, primary CNS lymphoma, progressive multifocal leukoencephalopathy (PML), or another structural brain lesion with neurological sequelae\nOther CNS conditions: non-opportunistic primary or metastatic brain tumors, uncontrolled seizure disorder, progressive multiple sclerosis, stroke with neurological sequelae, or dementia due to causes other than HIV (eg, Alzheimer\'s disease)\nConstitutional illness (eg, persistent unexplained fever, diarrhea, significant weight loss, disabling weakness) within 30 days of screening\nKnown untreated B12 deficiency or malnutrition (body mass index [BMI] less than 18) at screening\nEvidence of current hepatitis C virus infection (HCV) (ie, HCV antibody [Ab] positive within 90 days prior to study entry unless also shown to be plasma HCV RNA negative within the same time period)\nUnstable and advanced liver disease (as defined by the presence of at least one of the following: ascites, encephalopathy, coagulopathy, hypoalbuminemia, esophageal or gastric varices, or persistent jaundice)\nPrior or current use of any CCR5 antagonist (such as MVC and cenicriviroc [CVC]) and integrase inhibitor (such as RAL, DTG, and elvitegravir [EVG])\nCurrent use of any medication, including antiretrovirals, prohibited in the study (refer to the A5324 protocol-specific web page [PSWP] for the prohibited medications)\nBreastfeeding\nPresence of an AIDS-defining opportunistic infection within 6 months prior to entry. Note: Refer to the A5324 Manual of Operations (MOPS) for the list of AIDS-defining opportunistic infections.\nActive syphilis or treatment for syphilis within 90 days prior to study entry. NOTE: Active syphilis is defined as four-fold increase in serum rapid plasma reagin (RPR) or venereal disease research laboratory (VDRL) tests in an individual with past syphilis, or newly reactive serum RPR or VDRL with a reactive confirmatory test (enzyme immunoassays [EIA] or chemiluminescent assay [CIA], T. pallidum particle agglutination [TP-PA], or fluorescent treponemal antibody absorbed [FTA-ABS]).\nKnown allergy/sensitivity or any hypersensitivity to components of study drugs or their formulation\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\n  -  Major depressive disorder [AND] with psychotic features\n  -  Traumatic Brain Injury (TBI) [AND] with a clear impact on activities of daily living\n  -  Developmental delay, [OR] intellectual deficit, [OR] and/or severe educational disability resulting in some dependence for activities of daily living\n  -  Ongoing substance use disorder [AND] with significant impact on activities of daily living. Difficult [OR] or [NOT] impossible to determine whether cognitive [OR] or functional decline is due to substance use [OR] or HIV, [OR] or both\nExclusion Criteria:\n  -  Evidence of intoxication [OR] or withdrawal during the screening evaluation\n  -  Central nervous system (CNS) infections [OR] or opportunistic conditions: brain abscess (bacterial, [OR] mycobacterial, [OR] fungal [OR] or Toxoplasma), meningitis [AND] with persistent neurologic impairment, primary CNS lymphoma, [OR] progressive multifocal leukoencephalopathy (PML), [OR] or another structural brain lesion [AND] with neurological sequelae\n  -  Other CNS conditions: [NOT] non-opportunistic primary [OR] or metastatic brain tumors, uncontrolled seizure disorder, [OR] progressive multiple sclerosis, [OR] stroke [AND] with neurological sequelae, [OR] or dementia due to causes other than HIV (eg, Alzheimer\'s disease)\n  -  Constitutional illness (eg, persistent unexplained fever, [OR] diarrhea, significant weight loss, disabling weakness) within 30 days of screening\n  -  Known [NOT] untreated B12 deficiency [OR] or malnutrition (body mass index [BMI] less than 18) at screening\n  -  Evidence of current hepatitis C virus infection (HCV) (ie, HCV antibody [Ab] positive within 90 days prior to study entry unless also shown to be plasma HCV RNA negative within the same time period)\n  -  Unstable [OR] and advanced liver disease (as defined by the presence of at least one of the following: ascites, [OR] encephalopathy, [OR] coagulopathy, [OR] hypoalbuminemia, [OR] esophageal [OR] or gastric varices, [OR] or persistent jaundice)\n  -  Prior [OR] or current use of any CCR5 antagonist (such as MVC [OR] and cenicriviroc [CVC]) [OR] and integrase inhibitor (such as RAL, [OR] DTG, [OR] and elvitegravir [EVG])\n  -  Current use of any medication, including antiretrovirals, [NOT] prohibited in the study (refer to the A5324 protocol-specific web page [PSWP] for the prohibited medications)\n  -  Breastfeeding\n  -  Presence of an AIDS-defining opportunistic infection within 6 months prior to entry. Note: Refer to the A5324 Manual of Operations (MOPS) for the list of AIDS-defining opportunistic infections.\n  -  Active syphilis [OR] or treatment for syphilis within 90 days prior to study entry. NOTE: Active syphilis is defined as four-fold increase in serum rapid plasma reagin (RPR) [OR] or venereal disease research laboratory (VDRL) tests in an individual with past syphilis, [OR] or newly reactive serum RPR [OR] or VDRL with a reactive confirmatory test (enzyme immunoassays [EIA] [OR] or chemiluminescent assay [CIA], T. pallidum particle agglutination [TP-PA], [OR] or fluorescent treponemal antibody absorbed [FTA-ABS]).\n  -  Known allergy/ [OR] sensitivity [OR] or any hypersensitivity to components of study drugs [OR] or their formulation<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
  -  Major depressive disorder [AND] with psychotic features
  -  Traumatic Brain Injury (TBI) [AND] with a clear impact on activities of daily living
  -  Developmental delay, [OR] intellectual deficit, [OR] and/or severe educational disability resulting in some dependence for activities of daily living
  -  Ongoing substance use disorder [AND] with significant impact on activities of daily living. Difficult [OR] or [NOT] impossible to determine whether cognitive [OR] or functional decline is due to substance use [OR] or HIV, [OR] or both
Exclusion Criteria:
  -  Evidence of intoxication [OR] or withdrawal during the screening evaluation
  -  Central nervous system (CNS) infections [OR] or opportunistic conditions: brain abscess (bacterial, [OR] mycobacterial, [OR] fungal [OR] or Toxoplasma), meningitis [AND] with persistent neurologic impairment, primary CNS lymphoma, [OR] progressive multifocal leukoencephalopathy (PML), [OR] or another structural brain lesion [AND] with neurological sequelae
  -  Other CNS conditions: [NOT] non-opportunistic primary [OR] or metastatic brain tumors, uncontrolled seizure disorder, [OR] progressive multiple sclerosis, [OR] stroke [AND] with neurological sequelae, [OR] or dementia due to causes other than HIV (eg, Alzheimer's disease)
  -  Constitutional illness (eg, persistent unexplained fever, [OR] diarrhea, significant weight loss, disabling weakness) within 30 days of screening
  -  Known [NOT] untreated B12 deficiency [OR] or malnutrition (body mass index [BMI] less than 18) at screening
  -  Evidence of current hepatitis C virus infection (HCV) (ie, HCV antibody [Ab] positive within 90 days prior to study entry unless also shown to be plasma HCV RNA negative within the same time period)
  -  Unstable [OR] and advanced liver disease (as defined by the presence of at least one of the following: ascites, [OR] encephalopathy, [OR] coagulopathy, [OR] hypoalbuminemia, [OR] esophageal [OR] or gastric varices, [OR] or persistent jaundice)
  -  Prior [OR] or current use of any CCR5 antagonist (such as MVC [OR] and cenicriviroc [CVC]) [OR] and integrase inhibitor (such as RAL, [OR] DTG, [OR] and elvitegravir [EVG])
  -  Current use of any medication, including antiretrovirals, [NOT] prohibited in the study (refer to the A5324 protocol-specific web page [PSWP] for the prohibited medications)
  -  Breastfeeding
  -  Presence of an AIDS-defining opportunistic infection within 6 months prior to entry. Note: Refer to the A5324 Manual of Operations (MOPS) for the list of AIDS-defining opportunistic infections.
  -  Active syphilis [OR] or treatment for syphilis within 90 days prior to study entry. NOTE: Active syphilis is defined as four-fold increase in serum rapid plasma reagin (RPR) [OR] or venereal disease research laboratory (VDRL) tests in an individual with past syphilis, [OR] or newly reactive serum RPR [OR] or VDRL with a reactive confirmatory test (enzyme immunoassays [EIA] [OR] or chemiluminescent assay [CIA], T. pallidum particle agglutination [TP-PA], [OR] or fluorescent treponemal antibody absorbed [FTA-ABS]).
  -  Known allergy/ [OR] sensitivity [OR] or any hypersensitivity to components of study drugs [OR] or their formulation
