thin 30 days prior to the current agitation episode must be excluded.\nPatients who are considered by the investigator, for any reason, to be unable to self-administer the inhalation device.\n\n\n### Response:\nPatient diagnosed with dementia.\nPatients with serious [OR] and unstable illnesses including current hepatic, [OR] renal, [OR] gastroenterologic, [OR] respiratory, [OR] cardiovascular (including ischemic heart disease [OR] and congestive heart failure), endocrinologic, [OR] neurologic (including stroke, [OR] transient ischemic attack, [OR] subarachnoidal bleeding, [OR] brain tumor, [OR] encephalopathy, [OR] and meningitis).\nPatients with a history of allergic reactions to loxapine [OR] or amoxapine\nPatients who have received an investigational drug within 30 days prior to the current agitation episode must be [NOT] excluded.\nPatients who are considered by the investigator, for any reason, to be [NOT] unable to self-administer the inhalation device.<|eot_id|>']
