a index of less than 5 h-1 [OR] or greater than 30 h-1.\nPredominance of central apneas [OR] and hypopneas, defined as more than 25% of all respiratory events.\nProfessional drivers, risk profession [OR] or respiratory failure (according to criteria of the clinical pathway for diagnosis and treatment of sleep-disordered breathing).\nVery excessive daytime sleepiness (Epworth Sleepiness Scale> 18).\nMorbid obesity (BMI> 40 kg / m2).\nPrior treatment with CPAP.<|eot_id|>']
