Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nPatients posing a serious suicidal risk and/or violence as judged by the investigator;\nDelirium\nDementia\nAmnestic and other cognitive disorder;\nPatients with a history of hypothyroidism unless taking a stable dose of thyroid medication and asymptomatic or euthyroid for 6 months;\nPatients who meet DSM-IV-TR criteria for any significant current substance abuse;\nhepatic insufficiency (three times the upper limit of normal (ULN) for aspartate aminotransferase (AST) and/or alanine aminotransferase (ALT)); liver transplant recipient; cirrhosis of the liver;\nmalignancy (except basal cell carcinoma) and/or chemotherapy within 1 year prior to screening; malignancy more than 1 year prior to screening must have been local and without metastasis and/or recurrence, and if treated with chemotherapy, without nervous system complications;\nsignificant unstable medical condition or life threatening disease with anticipated survival of less than 6 months;\nneed for therapies that may obscure the results of treatment and/or of the study\nParticipation in another clinical trial within 30 days of the screening visit;\nAnticipated inability to attend scheduled study visits;\nPatients who in the judgment of the Investigator may be unreliable or uncooperative with the evaluation procedure outlined in this protocol;\nPatients with a history of prior pharmacogenomic testing;\nAny change in psychotropic medication (including change in dosage) between screening and baseline;\nPatients who are known to be pregnant or lactating;\nPatients with a history of gastric bypass surgery.\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nPatients posing a serious suicidal risk [OR] and/or violence as judged by the investigator;\nDelirium\nDementia\nAmnestic and other cognitive disorder;\nPatients with a history of hypothyroidism unless taking a stable dose of thyroid medication [AND] and asymptomatic [OR] or euthyroid for 6 months;\nPatients who meet DSM-IV-TR criteria for any significant current substance abuse;\nhepatic insufficiency (three times the upper limit of normal (ULN) for aspartate aminotransferase (AST) [OR] and/or alanine aminotransferase (ALT)); liver transplant recipient; cirrhosis of the liver;\nmalignancy (except basal cell carcinoma) [OR] and/or chemotherapy within 1 year prior to screening; malignancy more than 1 year prior to screening must have been local [AND] and [NOT] without metastasis [OR] and/or recurrence, [AND] and if treated with chemotherapy, [NOT] without nervous system complications;\nsignificant unstable medical condition [OR] or life threatening disease [AND] with anticipated survival of less than 6 months;\nneed for therapies that may obscure the results of treatment [OR] and/or of the study\nParticipation in another clinical trial within 30 days of the screening visit;\nAnticipated [NOT] inability to attend scheduled study visits;\nPatients who in the judgment of the Investigator may be unreliable [OR] or uncooperative with the evaluation procedure outlined in this protocol;\nPatients with a history of prior pharmacogenomic testing;\nAny change in psychotropic medication (including change in dosage) between screening and baseline;\nPatients who are known to be pregnant [OR] or lactating;\nPatients with a history of gastric bypass surgery.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Patients posing a serious suicidal risk [OR] and/or violence as judged by the investigator;
Delirium
Dementia
Amnestic and other cognitive disorder;
Patients with a history of hypothyroidism unless taking a stable dose of thyroid medication [AND] and asymptomatic [OR] or euthyroid for 6 months;
Patients who meet DSM-IV-TR criteria for any significant current substance abuse;
hepatic insufficiency (three times the upper limit of normal (ULN) for aspartate aminotransferase (AST) [OR] and/or alanine aminotransferase (ALT)); liver transplant recipient; cirrhosis of the liver;
malignancy (except basal cell carcinoma) [OR] and/or chemotherapy within 1 year prior to screening; malignancy more than 1 year prior to screening must have been local [AND] and [NOT] without metastasis [OR] and/or recurrence, [AND] and if treated with chemotherapy, [NOT] without nervous system complications;
significant unstable medical condition [OR] or life threatening disease [AND] with anticipated survival of less than 6 months;
need for therapies that may obscure the results of treatment [OR] and/or of the study
Participation in another clinical trial within 30 days of the screening visit;
Anticipated [NOT] inability to attend scheduled study visits;
Patients who in the judgment of the Investigator may be unreliable [OR] or uncooperative with the evaluation procedure outlined in this protocol;
Patients with a history of prior pharmacogenomic testing;
Any change in psychotropic medication (including change in dosage) between screening and baseline;
Patients who are known to be pregnant [OR] or lactating;
Patients with a history of gastric bypass surgery.
