ing physician\nReduced left ventricular ejection fraction (<50%)\n [NOT] Non-reversible airway obstruction (post-bronchodilator FEV1/ [OR] FVC < 0.7 [AND] and FEV1 < 80 %)\nRespiratory muscle weakness (Pi,max < 70cmH2O)\nPersistent dyspnea on daily life (Baseline Dyspnea Index focal score <or= 8).<|eot_id|>']
