ensated HF, moderate or greater valvular disease, significant cardiac arrhythmias, pericardial disease, congenital heart disease, primary pulmonary hypertension\n\n\n### Response:\nExclusion Criteria: coronary artery disease, [OR] diabetes mellitus, [OR] contraindications to cardiac magnetic resonance imaging (CMR), weight >350 lbs, [NOT] inability to lie flat for imaging, [OR] anemia, contraindications to regadenoson [OR] or aminophylline\nHEALTHY: known cardiovascular disease, [OR] cardiac risk factors [OR] or use of cardiac medications\nHYPERTENSIVE: known cardiovascular disease [OR] or risk factors aside from hypertension [OR] or use of cardiac medications\nHFpEF: prior history of LVEF below 50%, acute decompensated HF, [OR] moderate [OR] or greater valvular disease, significant cardiac arrhythmias, [OR] pericardial disease, [OR] congenital heart disease, [OR] primary pulmonary hypertension<|eot_id|>']
Response: Exclusion Criteria: coronary artery disease, [OR] diabetes mellitus, [OR] contraindications to cardiac magnetic resonance imaging (CMR), weight >350 lbs, [NOT] inability to lie flat for imaging, [OR] anemia, contraindications to regadenoson [OR] or aminophylline
HEALTHY: known cardiovascular disease, [OR] cardiac risk factors [OR] or use of cardiac medications
HYPERTENSIVE: known cardiovascular disease [OR] or risk factors aside from hypertension [OR] or use of cardiac medications
HFpEF: prior history of LVEF below 50%, acute decompensated HF, [OR] moderate [OR] or greater valvular disease, significant cardiac arrhythmias, [OR] pericardial disease, [OR] congenital heart disease, [OR] primary pulmonary hypertension
