Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nHIV infection at screening\nparticipation in previous or concurrent HIV vaccine trials\nlactating, pregnant or planning pregnancy\nrenal function impairment (serum creatinine >1.5 mg/dl), Fanconi syndrome\nabnormal liver function tests (AST/ALT > 43 U/L), liver disease, viral hepatitis, hepatitis B virus (HBV) infection\nserum phosphorus <2.2mg/dl, osteoporosis\nknown sensitivity to components of the Truvada® formulation\nany immunosuppressive treatment, such as systemic corticosteroids\nassumption of medication that interacts with Truvada®\nhigh likelihood of poor adherence to PREP and clinic attendance\nany condition that in the opinion of the attending physician could endanger the health of the participant or render her unsuitable to participate in the trial\n\n\n### Response:\nHIV infection at screening\nparticipation in previous [OR] or concurrent HIV vaccine trials\nlactating, [OR] pregnant [OR] or planning pregnancy\nrenal function impairment (serum creatinine >1.5 mg/dl), Fanconi syndrome\nabnormal liver function tests (AST/ [OR] ALT > 43 U/L), liver disease, [OR] viral hepatitis, [OR] hepatitis B virus (HBV) infection\nserum phosphorus <2.2mg/dl, [OR] osteoporosis\nknown sensitivity to components of the Truvada® formulation\nany immunosuppressive treatment, such as systemic corticosteroids\nassumption of medication that interacts with Truvada®\nhigh likelihood of poor adherence to PREP [AND] and clinic attendance\nany condition that in the opinion of the attending physician could endanger the health of the participant [OR] or render her unsuitable to participate in the trial<|eot_id|>']
Response: HIV infection at screening
participation in previous [OR] or concurrent HIV vaccine trials
lactating, [OR] pregnant [OR] or planning pregnancy
renal function impairment (serum creatinine >1.5 mg/dl), Fanconi syndrome
abnormal liver function tests (AST/ [OR] ALT > 43 U/L), liver disease, [OR] viral hepatitis, [OR] hepatitis B virus (HBV) infection
serum phosphorus <2.2mg/dl, [OR] osteoporosis
known sensitivity to components of the Truvada® formulation
any immunosuppressive treatment, such as systemic corticosteroids
assumption of medication that interacts with Truvada®
high likelihood of poor adherence to PREP [AND] and clinic attendance
any condition that in the opinion of the attending physician could endanger the health of the participant [OR] or render her unsuitable to participate in the trial
