Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\n1. Diagnosed with symptomatic sacral perineurial cysts(e.g., lumbosacral or perineal pain, fecal or urinary functions change, sexual function change, lower limb radiation pain, muscle abate, paresthesia, etc)\n2. Visual analog scale more than or equal to 4\n3. Signed the informed consent\n4. Years, range 18-60\n5. Self-rating anxiety scale (SAS) and self-rating depression scale (SDS) scores < 50\n6. No Congenital,Mental and other Nervous system diseases\n7. No Serious Cardiac,Pulmonary,Hepatic and Nephritic disease\n8. No history of drug allergy\n9. No pain(including dysmenorrhea) or drug use (e.g., antipyretics,sleeping pills) within the last month\n10. MRI finding of sacral perineurial cysts, but without any clinical symptoms, included in the negative control group\n11. MRI finding healthy volunteers don\'t have sacral perineurial cysts, included in the negative control groupblank control group\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\n 1. Diagnosed with symptomatic sacral perineurial cysts(e.g., lumbosacral [OR] or perineal pain, [OR] fecal [OR] or urinary functions change, [OR] sexual function change, [OR] lower limb radiation pain, [OR] muscle abate, [OR] paresthesia, etc)\n 2. Visual analog scale more than or equal to 4\n 3. Signed the informed consent\n 4. Years, range 18-60\n 5. Self-rating anxiety scale (SAS) [AND] and self-rating depression scale (SDS) scores < 50\n 6. [NOT] No Congenital, [OR] Mental [OR] and other Nervous system diseases\n 7. [NOT] No Serious Cardiac, [OR] Pulmonary, [OR] Hepatic [OR] and Nephritic disease\n 8. [NOT] No history of drug allergy\n 9. [NOT] No pain(including dysmenorrhea) [OR] or drug use (e.g., antipyretics, [OR] sleeping pills) within the last month\n 10. MRI finding of sacral perineurial cysts, [NOT] but [NOT] without any clinical symptoms, included in the negative control group\n 11. MRI finding healthy volunteers [NOT] don\'t have sacral perineurial cysts, included in the negative control groupblank control group<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
 1. Diagnosed with symptomatic sacral perineurial cysts(e.g., lumbosacral [OR] or perineal pain, [OR] fecal [OR] or urinary functions change, [OR] sexual function change, [OR] lower limb radiation pain, [OR] muscle abate, [OR] paresthesia, etc)
 2. Visual analog scale more than or equal to 4
 3. Signed the informed consent
 4. Years, range 18-60
 5. Self-rating anxiety scale (SAS) [AND] and self-rating depression scale (SDS) scores < 50
 6. [NOT] No Congenital, [OR] Mental [OR] and other Nervous system diseases
 7. [NOT] No Serious Cardiac, [OR] Pulmonary, [OR] Hepatic [OR] and Nephritic disease
 8. [NOT] No history of drug allergy
 9. [NOT] No pain(including dysmenorrhea) [OR] or drug use (e.g., antipyretics, [OR] sleeping pills) within the last month
 10. MRI finding of sacral perineurial cysts, [NOT] but [NOT] without any clinical symptoms, included in the negative control group
 11. MRI finding healthy volunteers [NOT] don't have sacral perineurial cysts, included in the negative control groupblank control group
