Need for long-term treatment with a low molecular weight heparin, [OR] vitamin K antagonists [OR] or NOAC, for an indication other than the index PE episode, [OR] or for antiplatelet agents except acetylsalicylic acid at a dosage =100 mg/day;
Active bleeding [OR] or known significant bleeding risk (e.g., gastrointestinal ulcer, [OR] malignant neoplasms, [OR] injuries [OR] or recent surgeries of the brain, [OR] spinal cord [OR] or eyes, recent intracranial bleedings, known [OR] or suspected esophagus varices, [OR] aneurysms [OR] or intraspinal [OR] or intracranial vascular abnormalities)
Artificial heart valves requiring treatment with an anticoagulant
Renal insufficiency [AND] with estimated creatinine clearance <30 ml/min/1.73 m2
Chronic liver disease [AND] with aminotransferase levels two times or more above the local upper limit of normal range
Concomitant administration of strong inhibitors of P-glycoprotein like ketoconazole, [OR] cyclosporin, [OR] itraconazole [OR] or dronedarone
Unwillingness [OR] or [NOT] inability to adhere to treatment [OR] or to the follow-up visits
Life expectancy less than 6 months
