Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\n1. A medical condition, other than PBC, that in the investigator\'s opinion would preclude full participation in the study or confound its results (e.g., cancer on active treatment) \n2. AST or ALT > 3 × ULN \n3. Total bilirubin > 2 × ULN \n4. Auto-immune hepatitis \n5. Primary sclerosing cholangitis \n6. Known history of alpha-1-Antitrypsin deficiency \n7. Known history of chronic viral hepatitis \n8. Creatine kinase above ULN \n9. Serum creatinine above ULN \n10. For females, pregnancy or breast-feeding \n11. Use of colchicine, methotrexate, azathioprine, or systemic steroids in the two months preceding screening \n12. Current use of fibrates, including fenofibrates, or simvastatin \n13. Use of an experimental treatment for PBC \n14. Use of experimental or unapproved immunosuppressant \n15. Any other condition(s) that would compromise the safety of the subject or compromise the quality of the clinical study, as judged by the Investigator       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\n1. A medical condition, other than PBC, that in the investigator\'s opinion would [NOT] preclude full participation in the study [OR] or confound its results (e.g., cancer [AND] on active treatment) \n2. AST [OR] or ALT > 3 × ULN \n3. Total bilirubin > 2 × ULN \n4. Auto-immune hepatitis \n5. Primary sclerosing cholangitis \n6. Known history of alpha-1-Antitrypsin deficiency \n7. Known history of chronic viral hepatitis \n 8. Creatine kinase above ULN \n9. Serum creatinine above ULN \n10. For females, pregnancy [OR] or breast-feeding \n11. Use of colchicine, [OR] methotrexate, [OR] azathioprine, [OR] or systemic steroids in the two months preceding screening \n12. Current use of fibrates, [OR] including fenofibrates, [OR] or simvastatin \n13. Use of an experimental treatment for PBC \n14. Use of experimental [OR] or unapproved immunosuppressant \n15. Any other condition(s) that would compromise the safety of the subject [OR] or compromise the quality of the clinical study, as judged by the Investigator<|eot_id|>']
Response: 1. A medical condition, other than PBC, that in the investigator's opinion would [NOT] preclude full participation in the study [OR] or confound its results (e.g., cancer [AND] on active treatment) 
2. AST [OR] or ALT > 3 × ULN 
3. Total bilirubin > 2 × ULN 
4. Auto-immune hepatitis 
5. Primary sclerosing cholangitis 
6. Known history of alpha-1-Antitrypsin deficiency 
7. Known history of chronic viral hepatitis 
 8. Creatine kinase above ULN 
9. Serum creatinine above ULN 
10. For females, pregnancy [OR] or breast-feeding 
11. Use of colchicine, [OR] methotrexate, [OR] azathioprine, [OR] or systemic steroids in the two months preceding screening 
12. Current use of fibrates, [OR] including fenofibrates, [OR] or simvastatin 
13. Use of an experimental treatment for PBC 
14. Use of experimental [OR] or unapproved immunosuppressant 
15. Any other condition(s) that would compromise the safety of the subject [OR] or compromise the quality of the clinical study, as judged by the Investigator
