Das File: /work/eauten2s/ec_criteria_struct/chia/input/chia_text_half/NCT02609048_inc.txt wurde erfolgreich geladen.
Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\n1. Must have given written informed consent (signed and dated) and any authorizations required by local law \n2. 18 to 75 years old (inclusive) \n3. Male or female with a diagnosis of PBC, by at least two of the following criteria: \nHistory of AP above ULN for at least six months \nPositive Anti-Mitochondrial Antibodies (AMA) titers (>1/40 on immunofluorescence or M2 positive by enzyme linked immunosorbent assay (ELISA) or positive PBC-specific antinuclear antibodies \nDocumented liver biopsy result consistent with PBC \n4. On a stable and recommended dose of UDCA for the past twelve months \n5. AP ≥ 1.67 × ULN \n6. For females of reproductive potential, use of at least one barrier contraceptive and a second effective birth control method during the study and for at least two weeks after the last dose. For male subjects, use of appropriate contraception (e.g., condoms), so their female partners of reproductive potential do not become pregnant during the study and for at least two weeks after the last dose \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\n 1. Must have given written informed consent (signed and dated) and any authorizations required by local law \n 2. 18 to 75 years old (inclusive) \n 3. Male [OR] or female [AND] with a diagnosis of PBC, by at least two of the following criteria: \nHistory of AP above ULN for at least six months \n Positive Anti-Mitochondrial Antibodies (AMA) titers (>1/40 on immunofluorescence [OR] or M2 positive by enzyme linked immunosorbent assay (ELISA) [OR] or positive PBC-specific antinuclear antibodies \n Documented liver biopsy result consistent with PBC \n 4. On a stable [AND] and recommended dose of UDCA for the past twelve months \n 5. AP ≥ 1.67 × ULN \n 6. For females [AND] of reproductive potential, use of at least one barrier contraceptive [AND] and a second effective birth control method during the study [AND] and for at least two weeks after the last dose. For male subjects, use of appropriate contraception (e.g., condoms), so their female partners [AND] of reproductive potential do [NOT] not become pregnant during the study [AND] and for at least two weeks after the last dose<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
 1. Must have given written informed consent (signed and dated) and any authorizations required by local law 
 2. 18 to 75 years old (inclusive) 
 3. Male [OR] or female [AND] with a diagnosis of PBC, by at least two of the following criteria: 
History of AP above ULN for at least six months 
 Positive Anti-Mitochondrial Antibodies (AMA) titers (>1/40 on immunofluorescence [OR] or M2 positive by enzyme linked immunosorbent assay (ELISA) [OR] or positive PBC-specific antinuclear antibodies 
 Documented liver biopsy result consistent with PBC 
 4. On a stable [AND] and recommended dose of UDCA for the past twelve months 
 5. AP ≥ 1.67 × ULN 
 6. For females [AND] of reproductive potential, use of at least one barrier contraceptive [AND] and a second effective birth control method during the study [AND] and for at least two weeks after the last dose. For male subjects, use of appropriate contraception (e.g., condoms), so their female partners [AND] of reproductive potential do [NOT] not become pregnant during the study [AND] and for at least two weeks after the last dose
