Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nType 1 diabetes (autoantibody positive).\nAny history of receiving GLP-1 analogues or dipeptidyl peptidase inhibitors within 6 months\nKnown severe heart failure, classified as NYHA 4.\nActive myocarditis; malfunctioning artificial heart valve.\nHistory of ventricular tachycardia within 3 months before study entry; second- or third-degree atrioventricular block.\nSupine systolic blood pressure <85 mm Hg or >200 mm Hg at screening.\nPrimary renal impairment, creatinine clearance < 45 ml/min if treated with metformin.\nUncorrected hypokalemia or hyperkalemia (potassium <3.5 mmol/l or >5.5 mmol/l).\nSignificant anemia (Hb < 90 g/l)\nSevere gastrointestinal disease, including gastroparesis. As judged by the Investigator.\nBody mass index (BMI) > 45 kg/m2.\nMalignant neoplasm requiring chemotherapy, surgery, radiation or palliative therapy in the previous 5 years. Patients with intraepithelial squamous cell carcinoma of the skin treated with topical 5FU and subjects with basal cell skin cancer are allowed to enter the trial.\nFemales of child bearing potential who are pregnant, breast-feeding or intend to become pregnant.\nCurrent drug and alcohol abuse.\nHistory of acute or chronic pancreatitis\nSubjects considered by the Investigator to be unsuitable for the study.\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nType 1 diabetes (autoantibody positive).\nAny history of receiving GLP-1 analogues [OR] or dipeptidyl peptidase inhibitors within 6 months\nKnown severe heart failure, classified as NYHA 4.\nActive myocarditis; malfunctioning artificial heart valve.\nHistory of ventricular tachycardia within 3 months before study entry; second- [OR] or third-degree atrioventricular block.\nSupine systolic blood pressure <85 mm Hg [OR] or >200 mm Hg at screening.\nPrimary renal impairment, [OR] creatinine clearance < 45 ml/min if treated with metformin.\nUncorrected hypokalemia [OR] or hyperkalemia (potassium <3.5 mmol/l [OR] or >5.5 mmol/l).\nSignificant anemia (Hb < 90 g/l)\nSevere gastrointestinal disease, including gastroparesis. As judged by the Investigator.\nBody mass index (BMI) > 45 kg/m2.\nMalignant neoplasm requiring chemotherapy, [OR] surgery, [OR] radiation [OR] or palliative therapy in the previous 5 years. Patients with intraepithelial squamous cell carcinoma of the skin treated with topical 5FU and subjects with basal cell skin cancer are allowed to enter the trial.\nFemales [AND] of child bearing potential [AND] who are pregnant, [OR] breast-feeding [OR] or intend to become pregnant.\nCurrent drug [OR] and alcohol abuse.\nHistory of acute [OR] or chronic pancreatitis\nSubjects considered by the Investigator to be unsuitable for the study.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Type 1 diabetes (autoantibody positive).
Any history of receiving GLP-1 analogues [OR] or dipeptidyl peptidase inhibitors within 6 months
Known severe heart failure, classified as NYHA 4.
Active myocarditis; malfunctioning artificial heart valve.
History of ventricular tachycardia within 3 months before study entry; second- [OR] or third-degree atrioventricular block.
Supine systolic blood pressure <85 mm Hg [OR] or >200 mm Hg at screening.
Primary renal impairment, [OR] creatinine clearance < 45 ml/min if treated with metformin.
Uncorrected hypokalemia [OR] or hyperkalemia (potassium <3.5 mmol/l [OR] or >5.5 mmol/l).
Significant anemia (Hb < 90 g/l)
Severe gastrointestinal disease, including gastroparesis. As judged by the Investigator.
Body mass index (BMI) > 45 kg/m2.
Malignant neoplasm requiring chemotherapy, [OR] surgery, [OR] radiation [OR] or palliative therapy in the previous 5 years. Patients with intraepithelial squamous cell carcinoma of the skin treated with topical 5FU and subjects with basal cell skin cancer are allowed to enter the trial.
Females [AND] of child bearing potential [AND] who are pregnant, [OR] breast-feeding [OR] or intend to become pregnant.
Current drug [OR] and alcohol abuse.
History of acute [OR] or chronic pancreatitis
Subjects considered by the Investigator to be unsuitable for the study.
