Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nType 1 diabetes\nKnown peripheral artery disease\nLiver enzymes equal or more than 1.5 times the upper limit of normal\nChronic heart failure NYHA class III or IV\nCurrent haemodialysis or peritoneal dialysis\nEnd stage liver disease, defined as acute or chronic liver disease and recent history of one of the following: ascites, encephalopathy, variceal bleeding, bilirubin equal or greater than 2.0 mg/dL, albumin equal or less than 3.5 g/ dL, prothrombin time greater or equal to 4 seconds, INR greater than or equal to 1.7 or prior liver transplant\nKnown or suspected hypersensitivity to trial products or related products\nFemale of child-bearing potential who is pregnant, breast-feeding or intends to become pregnant or is not using adequate contraceptive methods as required by law or local practice.\nExpected simultaneous participation in any other clinical trial of an investigational medicinal product.\nReceipt of any investigational medicinal product within 30 days before randomization\nCurrent or past (within the last 5 years) malignant neoplasms (except basal cell and squamous cell skin carcinoma)\nAny condition that in the investigator\'s opinion would make the subject unable to adhere to the trial visit schedule and procedures\nKnown history of non-compliance to treatment.\n\n\n### Response:\nType 1 diabetes\nKnown peripheral artery disease\nLiver enzymes equal or more than 1.5 times the upper limit of normal\nChronic heart failure NYHA class III or IV\nCurrent haemodialysis [OR] or peritoneal dialysis\nEnd stage liver disease, defined as acute [OR] or chronic liver disease [AND] and recent history of one of the following: ascites, [OR] encephalopathy, [OR] variceal bleeding, [OR] bilirubin equal or greater than 2.0 mg/dL, albumin equal or less than 3.5 g/ dL, prothrombin time greater or equal to 4 seconds, [OR] INR greater than or equal to 1.7 [OR] or prior liver transplant\nKnown [OR] or suspected hypersensitivity to trial products [OR] or related products\nFemale [AND] of child-bearing potential [AND] who is pregnant, [OR] breast-feeding [OR] or intends to become pregnant [OR] or is [NOT] not using adequate contraceptive methods as required by law [OR] or local practice.\nExpected simultaneous participation in any other clinical trial of an investigational medicinal product.\nReceipt of any investigational medicinal product within 30 days before randomization\nCurrent [OR] or past (within the last 5 years) malignant neoplasms (except basal cell [OR] and squamous cell skin carcinoma)\nAny condition that in the investigator\'s opinion would make the subject [NOT] unable to adhere to the trial visit schedule [AND] and procedures\nKnown history of [NOT] non-compliance to treatment.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Type 1 diabetes
Known peripheral artery disease
Liver enzymes equal or more than 1.5 times the upper limit of normal
Chronic heart failure NYHA class III or IV
Current haemodialysis [OR] or peritoneal dialysis
End stage liver disease, defined as acute [OR] or chronic liver disease [AND] and recent history of one of the following: ascites, [OR] encephalopathy, [OR] variceal bleeding, [OR] bilirubin equal or greater than 2.0 mg/dL, albumin equal or less than 3.5 g/ dL, prothrombin time greater or equal to 4 seconds, [OR] INR greater than or equal to 1.7 [OR] or prior liver transplant
Known [OR] or suspected hypersensitivity to trial products [OR] or related products
Female [AND] of child-bearing potential [AND] who is pregnant, [OR] breast-feeding [OR] or intends to become pregnant [OR] or is [NOT] not using adequate contraceptive methods as required by law [OR] or local practice.
Expected simultaneous participation in any other clinical trial of an investigational medicinal product.
Receipt of any investigational medicinal product within 30 days before randomization
Current [OR] or past (within the last 5 years) malignant neoplasms (except basal cell [OR] and squamous cell skin carcinoma)
Any condition that in the investigator's opinion would make the subject [NOT] unable to adhere to the trial visit schedule [AND] and procedures
Known history of [NOT] non-compliance to treatment.
