Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nRenal disease unrelated to SLE (e.g. diabetes mellitus, other glomerular or tubulointerstitial disease, renovascular disease), or transplanted kidney.\nEstimated glomerular filtration rate (eGFR by MDRD) =20 mL/min per 1.73 m2 or serum creatinine >300 micromol/L (3.39 mg/dL) at screening.\nRenal biopsy showing cellular or fibrocellular crescent in more than 25% of glomeruli.\nCNS or other severe organ manifestation of lupus that necessitate aggressive immunosuppressive therapy on its own.\nCo-morbidities that require corticosteroid therapy (e.g. asthma, inflammatory bowel disease).\nTreatment with prednisolone (or prednisone, or equivalent) at >20 mg/D for over 4 weeks within the past 3 months.\nTreatment with MMF at >1.5 g/D for over 4 weeks within the past 3 months.\nKnown hypersensitivity or intolerability to prednisolone (or prednisone, or equivalent), TAC, or MMF at a dose of 1.25 g or below per day.\nSubjects who are already on treatment with TAC, cyclosporine or any other calcineurin inhibitor for over 4 weeks within the past 12 months.\nTreatment with cyclophosphamide, leflunomide, or methotrexate for over 2 weeks, or use of biological agent(s) regardless of duration, within the past 6 months (Note: prior use of azathioprine, mizoribine, intravenous immunoglobulins and anti-malarials is allowed).\nUncontrolled hypertension with systolic BP >160 mmHg or diastolic BP >95 mmHg.\nWomen who are pregnant or breastfeeding.\nWomen with childbearing potential or their male partners, who refuse to use an effective birth control method\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\n  -  Renal disease unrelated to SLE (e.g. diabetes mellitus, [OR] other glomerular [OR] or tubulointerstitial disease, [OR] renovascular disease), [OR] or transplanted kidney.\n  -  Estimated glomerular filtration rate (eGFR by MDRD) =20 mL/min per 1.73 m2 [OR] or serum creatinine >300 micromol/L (3.39 mg/dL) at screening.\n  -  Renal biopsy showing cellular [OR] or fibrocellular crescent in more than 25% of glomeruli.\n  -  CNS [OR] or other severe organ manifestation of lupus that necessitate aggressive immunosuppressive therapy on its own.\n  -  Co-morbidities that require corticosteroid therapy (e.g. asthma, [OR] inflammatory bowel disease).\n  -  Treatment with prednisolone [OR] (or prednisone, [OR] or equivalent) at >20 mg/D for over 4 weeks within the past 3 months.\n  -  Treatment with MMF at >1.5 g/D for over 4 weeks within the past 3 months.\nExclusion Criteria:\n  -  Known hypersensitivity [OR] or intolerability to prednisolone [OR] (or prednisone, [OR] or equivalent), TAC, [OR] or MMF at a dose of 1.25 g or below per day.\n  -  Subjects who are already on treatment with TAC, [OR] cyclosporine [OR] or any other calcineurin inhibitor for over 4 weeks within the past 12 months.\n  -  Treatment with cyclophosphamide, [OR] leflunomide, [OR] or methotrexate for over 2 weeks, [OR] or use of biological agent(s) regardless of duration, within the past 6 months (Note: prior use of azathioprine, [OR] mizoribine, [OR] intravenous immunoglobulins [OR] and anti-malarials is allowed).\n  -  Uncontrolled hypertension [AND] with systolic BP >160 mmHg [OR] or diastolic BP >95 mmHg.\n  -  Women [AND] who are pregnant [OR] or breastfeeding.\n  -  Women [AND] with childbearing potential [OR] or their male partners, [AND] who refuse to use an effective birth control method<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
  -  Renal disease unrelated to SLE (e.g. diabetes mellitus, [OR] other glomerular [OR] or tubulointerstitial disease, [OR] renovascular disease), [OR] or transplanted kidney.
  -  Estimated glomerular filtration rate (eGFR by MDRD) =20 mL/min per 1.73 m2 [OR] or serum creatinine >300 micromol/L (3.39 mg/dL) at screening.
  -  Renal biopsy showing cellular [OR] or fibrocellular crescent in more than 25% of glomeruli.
  -  CNS [OR] or other severe organ manifestation of lupus that necessitate aggressive immunosuppressive therapy on its own.
  -  Co-morbidities that require corticosteroid therapy (e.g. asthma, [OR] inflammatory bowel disease).
  -  Treatment with prednisolone [OR] (or prednisone, [OR] or equivalent) at >20 mg/D for over 4 weeks within the past 3 months.
  -  Treatment with MMF at >1.5 g/D for over 4 weeks within the past 3 months.
Exclusion Criteria:
  -  Known hypersensitivity [OR] or intolerability to prednisolone [OR] (or prednisone, [OR] or equivalent), TAC, [OR] or MMF at a dose of 1.25 g or below per day.
  -  Subjects who are already on treatment with TAC, [OR] cyclosporine [OR] or any other calcineurin inhibitor for over 4 weeks within the past 12 months.
  -  Treatment with cyclophosphamide, [OR] leflunomide, [OR] or methotrexate for over 2 weeks, [OR] or use of biological agent(s) regardless of duration, within the past 6 months (Note: prior use of azathioprine, [OR] mizoribine, [OR] intravenous immunoglobulins [OR] and anti-malarials is allowed).
  -  Uncontrolled hypertension [AND] with systolic BP >160 mmHg [OR] or diastolic BP >95 mmHg.
  -  Women [AND] who are pregnant [OR] or breastfeeding.
  -  Women [AND] with childbearing potential [OR] or their male partners, [AND] who refuse to use an effective birth control method
