LN [AND] with proteinuria  (urine protein/creatinine ratio >1.0 [OR] or 24-hr urine protein >1.0 g at baseline), [AND] with or [NOT] without hematuria.\nBoth \'incident\' (i.e. new) patients [OR] and \'flare\' patients can be included.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Biopsy-proven LN Class III/IV±V (ISN/RPS 2003), with biopsy performed within 12 weeks of randomization.
Positive anti-dsDNA.
Active LN [AND] with proteinuria  (urine protein/creatinine ratio >1.0 [OR] or 24-hr urine protein >1.0 g at baseline), [AND] with or [NOT] without hematuria.
Both 'incident' (i.e. new) patients [OR] and 'flare' patients can be included.
