restricted diet\nhas ever taken Xyrem / sodium oxybate / GHB at any time\nclaustrophobia\nmetal implants / objects in the body that may interfere with MRI\nsuccinic semialdehyde dehydrogenase deficiency\n\n\n### Response:\nuse of any sedative hypnotics, [OR] tranquilizers, [OR] anticonvulsants, [OR] antihistamines (except [NOT] non-sedating), [OR] benzodiazepines, [OR] clonidine [OR] or any medication known to affect dopamine at start of baseline period\nsignificant unstable [OR] or uncontrolled medical/ [OR] psychiatric disease\nsignificant history of head trauma/ [OR] surgery [OR] or seizure disorder\nradiation exposure exceeding 20mSv in last 12 months\npregnancy\nsubstance abuse/ [OR] dependence (including alcohol)\nhave sleep apnea, [OR] or are shift workers\non a sodium-restricted diet\nhas ever taken Xyrem [OR] / sodium oxybate [OR] / GHB at any time\nclaustrophobia\nmetal implants [OR] / objects in the body that may interfere with MRI\nsuccinic semialdehyde dehydrogenase deficiency<|eot_id|>']
