Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nAmiodarone\nP-glycoprotein (P-gp) inducers (e.g., rifampin, St. John\'s wort)\nLiver biopsy at any time showing mHAI stage 4 or higher fibrosis OR\nFibroScan within 12 months demonstrating liver stiffness of =9.5 kilo Pascal or\nAST to platelet ratio index (APRI) =2.0 and Fibrosis-4 (FIB-4) =3.25\nNOTE: If APRI and FIB-4 are discordant one of the other forms of fibrosis staging must be used.\nKnown allergy/sensitivity or any hypersensitivity to components of study drugs or their formulation.\nHemochromatosis\nAlpha-1 antitrypsin deficiency\nWilson\'s disease\nAutoimmune hepatitis\nAlcoholic liver disease\nDrug-related liver disease\nSevere NC confounding conditions (stroke, head injury, or developmental learning disability).\nRegular use of anti-inflammatory drugs.\nCurrent or recent treatment with pegylated interferon (PEG-IFN).\nOther active inflammatory process (major infection, malignancy, rheumatoid arthritis/autoimmune disorder) within the prior 28 days.\nContraindications to magnetic resonance imaging (MRI).\nBleeding diathesis, thrombocytopenia, or use of anticoagulants that would contraindicate lumbar puncture.\nUncontrolled or active depression or other psychiatric disorder that in the opinion of the site investigator might preclude adherence to study requirements or impact NC functioning and assessments.\nActive drug or alcohol use or dependence that, in the opinion of the site investigator, would interfere with adherence to study requirements.\nPresence of active or acute AIDS-defining opportunistic infections within 12 weeks prior to study entry.\n\n\n### Response:\nAmiodarone\nP-glycoprotein (P-gp) inducers (e.g., rifampin, [OR] St. John\'s wort)\nLiver biopsy at any time showing mHAI stage 4 or higher fibrosis [OR] OR\nFibroScan within 12 months demonstrating liver stiffness of =9.5 kilo Pascal [OR] or\nAST [AND] to platelet ratio index (APRI) =2.0 [AND] and Fibrosis-4 (FIB-4) =3.25\nNOTE: If APRI [AND] and FIB-4 are discordant one of the other forms of fibrosis staging must be used.\nKnown allergy/ [OR] sensitivity [OR] or any hypersensitivity to components of study drugs [OR] or their formulation.\nHemochromatosis\nAlpha-1 antitrypsin deficiency\n Wilson\'s disease\nAutoimmune hepatitis\nAlcoholic liver disease\nDrug-related liver disease\nSevere NC confounding conditions (stroke, [OR] head injury, [OR] or developmental learning disability).\nRegular use of anti-inflammatory drugs.\nCurrent [OR] or recent treatment with pegylated interferon (PEG-IFN).\nOther active inflammatory process (major infection, [OR] malignancy, [OR] rheumatoid arthritis/ [OR] autoimmune disorder) within the prior 28 days.\nContraindications to magnetic resonance imaging (MRI).\nBleeding diathesis, [OR] thrombocytopenia, [OR] or use of anticoagulants that would contraindicate lumbar puncture.\nUncontrolled [OR] or active depression [OR] or other psychiatric disorder that, in the opinion of the site investigator, might [NOT] preclude adherence to study requirements [OR] or impact NC functioning [OR] and assessments.\nActive drug [OR] or alcohol use [OR] or dependence that, in the opinion of the site investigator, would interfere with adherence to study requirements.\nPresence of active [OR] or acute AIDS-defining opportunistic infections within 12 weeks prior to study entry.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Amiodarone
P-glycoprotein (P-gp) inducers (e.g., rifampin, [OR] St. John's wort)
Liver biopsy at any time showing mHAI stage 4 or higher fibrosis [OR] OR
FibroScan within 12 months demonstrating liver stiffness of =9.5 kilo Pascal [OR] or
AST [AND] to platelet ratio index (APRI) =2.0 [AND] and Fibrosis-4 (FIB-4) =3.25
NOTE: If APRI [AND] and FIB-4 are discordant one of the other forms of fibrosis staging must be used.
Known allergy/ [OR] sensitivity [OR] or any hypersensitivity to components of study drugs [OR] or their formulation.
Hemochromatosis
Alpha-1 antitrypsin deficiency
 Wilson's disease
Autoimmune hepatitis
Alcoholic liver disease
Drug-related liver disease
Severe NC confounding conditions (stroke, [OR] head injury, [OR] or developmental learning disability).
Regular use of anti-inflammatory drugs.
Current [OR] or recent treatment with pegylated interferon (PEG-IFN).
Other active inflammatory process (major infection, [OR] malignancy, [OR] rheumatoid arthritis/ [OR] autoimmune disorder) within the prior 28 days.
Contraindications to magnetic resonance imaging (MRI).
Bleeding diathesis, [OR] thrombocytopenia, [OR] or use of anticoagulants that would contraindicate lumbar puncture.
Uncontrolled [OR] or active depression [OR] or other psychiatric disorder that, in the opinion of the site investigator, might [NOT] preclude adherence to study requirements [OR] or impact NC functioning [OR] and assessments.
Active drug [OR] or alcohol use [OR] or dependence that, in the opinion of the site investigator, would interfere with adherence to study requirements.
Presence of active [OR] or acute AIDS-defining opportunistic infections within 12 weeks prior to study entry.
