Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\n1. Age 18 years or older \n2. Diagnosis of venous leg ulcer(s), as clinically determined by the investigator by a positive venous reflux test (venous refilling <20 seconds) using Doppler ultrasound for at least 4 weeks prior to screening day, which have not adequately responded to conventional ulcer therapy. \n3. Designated venous leg ulcer meets the following criteria at both the screening and baseline visits. If the patient has multiple ulcers, at least one ulcer must meet the following criteria at both the screening and baseline visits: \n1. Present for at least 4 weeks \n2. CEAP Classification Stage 6 \n3. Surface ulcer with an area > 15cm2 post debridement \n4. Viable, granulating wound (investigator discretion) \n4. Ulcers that extend through the epidermis but not through the muscle, tendon, or bone (Stage II or III ulcers as defined by the IAET). \n5. Female patients of childbearing potential must have a negative pregnancy test at screening and must agree to use hormonal contraceptive, intrauterine device, diaphragm with spermicide, condom with spermicide, or abstinence throughout until 2 weeks after the last administration of study drug \n6. Signed informed consent \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\n 1. Age 18 years or older \n 2. Diagnosis of venous leg ulcer(s), as clinically determined by the investigator by a positive venous reflux test (venous refilling <20 seconds) using Doppler ultrasound [AND] for at least 4 weeks prior to screening day, which have [NOT] not adequately responded to conventional ulcer therapy. \n 3. Designated venous leg ulcer meets the following criteria at both the screening [AND] and baseline visits. If the patient has multiple ulcers, at least one ulcer must meet the following criteria at both the screening [AND] and baseline visits: \n 1. Present for at least 4 weeks \n 2. CEAP Classification Stage 6 \n 3. Surface ulcer [AND] with an area > 15cm2 post debridement \n 4. Viable, granulating wound (investigator discretion) \n 4. Ulcers that extend through the epidermis [AND] but [NOT] not through the muscle, [OR] tendon, [OR] or bone (Stage II [OR] or III ulcers as defined by the IAET). \n 5. Female patients of childbearing potential must have a negative pregnancy test at screening [AND] and must agree to use hormonal contraceptive, [OR] intrauterine device, [OR] diaphragm [AND] with spermicide, [OR] condom [AND] with spermicide, [OR] or abstinence throughout until 2 weeks after the last administration of study drug \n 6. Signed informed consent<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
 1. Age 18 years or older 
 2. Diagnosis of venous leg ulcer(s), as clinically determined by the investigator by a positive venous reflux test (venous refilling <20 seconds) using Doppler ultrasound [AND] for at least 4 weeks prior to screening day, which have [NOT] not adequately responded to conventional ulcer therapy. 
 3. Designated venous leg ulcer meets the following criteria at both the screening [AND] and baseline visits. If the patient has multiple ulcers, at least one ulcer must meet the following criteria at both the screening [AND] and baseline visits: 
 1. Present for at least 4 weeks 
 2. CEAP Classification Stage 6 
 3. Surface ulcer [AND] with an area > 15cm2 post debridement 
 4. Viable, granulating wound (investigator discretion) 
 4. Ulcers that extend through the epidermis [AND] but [NOT] not through the muscle, [OR] tendon, [OR] or bone (Stage II [OR] or III ulcers as defined by the IAET). 
 5. Female patients of childbearing potential must have a negative pregnancy test at screening [AND] and must agree to use hormonal contraceptive, [OR] intrauterine device, [OR] diaphragm [AND] with spermicide, [OR] condom [AND] with spermicide, [OR] or abstinence throughout until 2 weeks after the last administration of study drug 
 6. Signed informed consent
