Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\n1. Male or female of any race, at least 18 years of age at Visit 1 Screening. \n2. Has provided verbal and written informed consent. \n3. Be able and willing to follow instructions, including participation in all study assessments and visits. \n4. Currently being treated for glaucoma using at least two medications, and be willing to continue on the same regime. \n5. Suffers from at least two of the symptoms in the GLIA™ Glaucoma Medication Ocular Side Effect Symptoms Questionnaire at a severity of 2 (moderate) or more. \n6. If a woman of childbearing potential, have a negative urine pregnancy test at Visit 1 and be using an adequate method of birth control throughout the study period. \n\n\n### Response:\n1. Male [OR] or female of any race, at least 18 years of age at Visit 1 Screening. \n2. Has provided verbal and written informed consent. \n3. Be able and willing to follow instructions, including participation in all study assessments and visits. \n4. Currently being treated for glaucoma using at least two medications, [AND] and be willing to continue on the same regime. \n5. Suffers from at least two of the symptoms in the GLIA™ Glaucoma Medication Ocular Side Effect Symptoms Questionnaire at a severity of 2 (moderate) or more. \n6. If a woman of childbearing potential, have a negative urine pregnancy test at Visit 1 [AND] and be using an adequate method of birth control throughout the study period.<|eot_id|>']
Response: 1. Male [OR] or female of any race, at least 18 years of age at Visit 1 Screening. 
2. Has provided verbal and written informed consent. 
3. Be able and willing to follow instructions, including participation in all study assessments and visits. 
4. Currently being treated for glaucoma using at least two medications, [AND] and be willing to continue on the same regime. 
5. Suffers from at least two of the symptoms in the GLIA™ Glaucoma Medication Ocular Side Effect Symptoms Questionnaire at a severity of 2 (moderate) or more. 
6. If a woman of childbearing potential, have a negative urine pregnancy test at Visit 1 [AND] and be using an adequate method of birth control throughout the study period.
