Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nExclusions Related to Cardiovascular Disease \n1. History of uncontrolled hypertension \n2. Persistent hypotension at Screening. \n3. Evidence or history of left-sided heart disease and/or clinically significant cardiac disease in which pulmonary hypertension is more likely WHO Group 2. \n4. Acute decompensated heart failure within 1 month of Screening. \n5. Recent initiation (<8 weeks from Screening) or planned initiation of cardiopulmonary rehabilitation exercise program. \nExclusions Related to Pulmonary Disease \n6. Newly diagnosed with PAH and not on PAH-specific therapy. \n7. Pulmonary hypertension due to: \n1. Uncorrected congenital systemic-to-pulmonary shunt. \n2. Pulmonary veno-occlusive disease and/or pulmonary capillary hemangiomatosis \n3. Persistent pulmonary hypertension of the newborn \n4. WHO clinical classification Groups 2-5 \n8. Evidence of significant airway and/or parenchymal lung disease. \n9. Chronic infection related to tuberculosis or fungal or mycobacterial disease. \nExclusions Based on Other Medical Conditions \n10. Chronic infections including, but not limited to tuberculosis (TB), hepatitis B virus (HBV) or hepatitis C virus (HCV). \n11. History of portal hypertension or chronic liver disease, including positive serology for infection with HCV and/or HBV. \n12. Evidence of active infection requiring intravenous or oral antibiotics within 4 weeks of Screening. \n13. Body mass index ≥35.0 at Screening. \n14. History of obstructive sleep apnea. \n15. History of malignancy within the last 5 years, except nonmelanoma skin cancer and cervical carcinoma in situ treated with curative intent. \n16. Neuropsychiatric disorders/symptoms or psychological conditions. \n17. Pregnancy or breast-feeding \n18. Prior treatment with B cell or lymphocyte-depleting agents (eg, rituximab, Campath) \nExclusions Based on Concomitant Medication Use \n19. Concurrent regular use of another leukotriene pathway inhibitor, including over-the-counter medications or herbal remedies. \nExclusions Based on Laboratory Values \n20. Significant/chronic renal insufficiency. \n21. Transaminases (alanine transaminase, aspartate transaminase) levels >3 × upper limit of normal (ULN) and/or bilirubin level >2 × ULN. \n22. Absolute neutrophil count <1500 mm3. \n23. Hemoglobin concentration <9 g/dL at Screening. \n24. Hepatic dysfunction as defined by Child-Pugh Class B or C       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nExclusion Criteria:\nExclusions Related to Cardiovascular Disease \n 1. History of uncontrolled hypertension \n 2. Persistent hypotension at Screening. \n 3. Evidence [OR] or history of left-sided heart disease [OR] and/or clinically significant cardiac disease in which pulmonary hypertension is more likely WHO Group 2. \n 4. Acute decompensated heart failure within 1 month of Screening. \n 5. Recent initiation (<8 weeks from Screening) [OR] or planned initiation of cardiopulmonary rehabilitation exercise program. \nExclusions Related to Pulmonary Disease \n 6. Newly diagnosed [AND] with PAH [AND] and [NOT] not on PAH-specific therapy. \n 7. Pulmonary hypertension due to: \n 1. Uncorrected congenital systemic-to-pulmonary shunt. \n 2. Pulmonary veno-occlusive disease [OR] and/or pulmonary capillary hemangiomatosis \n 3. Persistent pulmonary hypertension of the newborn \n 4. WHO clinical classification Groups 2-5 \n 8. Evidence of significant airway [OR] and/or parenchymal lung disease. \n 9. Chronic infection related to tuberculosis [OR] or fungal [OR] or mycobacterial disease. \nExclusions Based on Other Medical Conditions\n 10. Chronic infections including, but not limited to tuberculosis (TB), hepatitis B virus (HBV) [OR] or hepatitis C virus (HCV). \n 11. History of portal hypertension [OR] or chronic liver disease, including positive serology for infection with HCV [OR] and/or HBV. \n 12. Evidence of active infection requiring intravenous [OR] or oral antibiotics within 4 weeks of Screening. \n 13. Body mass index ≥35.0 at Screening. \n 14. History of obstructive sleep apnea. \n 15. History of malignancy [OR] within the last 5 years, except [NOT] nonmelanoma skin cancer [OR] and cervical carcinoma in situ treated with curative intent. \n 16. Neuropsychiatric disorders/ [OR] symptoms [OR] or psychological conditions. \n 17. Pregnancy [OR] or breast-feeding \n 18. Prior treatment with B cell [OR] or lymphocyte-depleting agents (eg, rituximab, [OR] Campath) \nExclusions Based on Concomitant Medication Use\n 19. Concurrent regular use of another leukotriene pathway inhibitor, including over-the-counter medications [OR] or herbal remedies. \nExclusions Based on Laboratory Values\n 20. Significant/ [OR] chronic renal insufficiency. \n 21. Transaminases (alanine transaminase, [OR] aspartate transaminase) levels >3 × upper limit of normal (ULN) [OR] and/or bilirubin level >2 × ULN. \n 22. Absolute neutrophil count <1500 mm3. \n 23. Hemoglobin concentration <9 g/dL at Screening. \n 24. Hepatic dysfunction as defined by Child-Pugh Class B [OR] or C<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Exclusion Criteria:
Exclusions Related to Cardiovascular Disease 
 1. History of uncontrolled hypertension 
 2. Persistent hypotension at Screening. 
 3. Evidence [OR] or history of left-sided heart disease [OR] and/or clinically significant cardiac disease in which pulmonary hypertension is more likely WHO Group 2. 
 4. Acute decompensated heart failure within 1 month of Screening. 
 5. Recent initiation (<8 weeks from Screening) [OR] or planned initiation of cardiopulmonary rehabilitation exercise program. 
Exclusions Related to Pulmonary Disease 
 6. Newly diagnosed [AND] with PAH [AND] and [NOT] not on PAH-specific therapy. 
 7. Pulmonary hypertension due to: 
 1. Uncorrected congenital systemic-to-pulmonary shunt. 
 2. Pulmonary veno-occlusive disease [OR] and/or pulmonary capillary hemangiomatosis 
 3. Persistent pulmonary hypertension of the newborn 
 4. WHO clinical classification Groups 2-5 
 8. Evidence of significant airway [OR] and/or parenchymal lung disease. 
 9. Chronic infection related to tuberculosis [OR] or fungal [OR] or mycobacterial disease. 
Exclusions Based on Other Medical Conditions
 10. Chronic infections including, but not limited to tuberculosis (TB), hepatitis B virus (HBV) [OR] or hepatitis C virus (HCV). 
 11. History of portal hypertension [OR] or chronic liver disease, including positive serology for infection with HCV [OR] and/or HBV. 
 12. Evidence of active infection requiring intravenous [OR] or oral antibiotics within 4 weeks of Screening. 
 13. Body mass index ≥35.0 at Screening. 
 14. History of obstructive sleep apnea. 
 15. History of malignancy [OR] within the last 5 years, except [NOT] nonmelanoma skin cancer [OR] and cervical carcinoma in situ treated with curative intent. 
 16. Neuropsychiatric disorders/ [OR] symptoms [OR] or psychological conditions. 
 17. Pregnancy [OR] or breast-feeding 
 18. Prior treatment with B cell [OR] or lymphocyte-depleting agents (eg, rituximab, [OR] Campath) 
Exclusions Based on Concomitant Medication Use
 19. Concurrent regular use of another leukotriene pathway inhibitor, including over-the-counter medications [OR] or herbal remedies. 
Exclusions Based on Laboratory Values
 20. Significant/ [OR] chronic renal insufficiency. 
 21. Transaminases (alanine transaminase, [OR] aspartate transaminase) levels >3 × upper limit of normal (ULN) [OR] and/or bilirubin level >2 × ULN. 
 22. Absolute neutrophil count <1500 mm3. 
 23. Hemoglobin concentration <9 g/dL at Screening. 
 24. Hepatic dysfunction as defined by Child-Pugh Class B [OR] or C
