Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\n1. Male or female, 18-75 years old. \n2. Has a diagnosis of WHO Group 1 PAH. \n3. Right heart catheterization performed at Screening with results that are: \n1. Mean pulmonary arterial pressure ≥25 mmHg (at rest) and \n2. Pulmonary venous hypertension (measured as pulmonary capillary wedge pressure (PCWP) ≤15 mmHg. If PCWP is not available, then mean left atrial pressure or left ventricular end-diastolic pressure ≤15 mmHg in the absence of left atrial obstruction. and \n3. Pulmonary vascular resistance (PVR) ≥300 dyn•s/cm5 (3.75 Wood units) \n4. Has WHO/NYHA-FC of II or III. \n5. Be on stable dose of at least one of the following PAH-specific therapies: endothelin receptor antagonist, an agent acting on the nitric oxide pathway (phosphodiesterase type 5 inhibitor or soluble guanylate cyclase stimulator), and/or a prostacyclin or prostacyclin analog. \n6. Has a 6-minute walk distance that is ≥150 and ≤500 meters. \n7. Have a ventilation-perfusion scan that rules out thromboembolic disease. \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\n 1. Male [OR] or female, 18-75 years old. \n 2. Has a diagnosis of WHO Group 1 PAH. \n 3. Right heart catheterization performed at Screening with results that are: \n 1. Mean pulmonary arterial pressure ≥25 mmHg (at rest) [AND] and \n 2. Pulmonary venous hypertension (measured as pulmonary capillary wedge pressure (PCWP) ≤15 mmHg. If PCWP is [NOT] not available, then mean left atrial pressure [OR] or left ventricular end-diastolic pressure ≤15 mmHg in the [NOT] absence of left atrial obstruction. [AND] and \n 3. Pulmonary vascular resistance (PVR) ≥300 dyn•s/cm5 (3.75 Wood units) \n 4. Has WHO/ [OR] NYHA-FC of II or III. \n 5. Be on stable dose of at least one of the following PAH-specific therapies: endothelin receptor antagonist, an agent acting on the nitric oxide pathway (phosphodiesterase type 5 inhibitor [OR] or soluble guanylate cyclase stimulator), [OR] and/or a prostacyclin [OR] or prostacyclin analog. \n 6. Has a 6-minute walk distance that is ≥150 [AND] and ≤500 meters. \n 7. Have a ventilation- [OR] perfusion scan that rules out thromboembolic disease.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
 1. Male [OR] or female, 18-75 years old. 
 2. Has a diagnosis of WHO Group 1 PAH. 
 3. Right heart catheterization performed at Screening with results that are: 
 1. Mean pulmonary arterial pressure ≥25 mmHg (at rest) [AND] and 
 2. Pulmonary venous hypertension (measured as pulmonary capillary wedge pressure (PCWP) ≤15 mmHg. If PCWP is [NOT] not available, then mean left atrial pressure [OR] or left ventricular end-diastolic pressure ≤15 mmHg in the [NOT] absence of left atrial obstruction. [AND] and 
 3. Pulmonary vascular resistance (PVR) ≥300 dyn•s/cm5 (3.75 Wood units) 
 4. Has WHO/ [OR] NYHA-FC of II or III. 
 5. Be on stable dose of at least one of the following PAH-specific therapies: endothelin receptor antagonist, an agent acting on the nitric oxide pathway (phosphodiesterase type 5 inhibitor [OR] or soluble guanylate cyclase stimulator), [OR] and/or a prostacyclin [OR] or prostacyclin analog. 
 6. Has a 6-minute walk distance that is ≥150 [AND] and ≤500 meters. 
 7. Have a ventilation- [OR] perfusion scan that rules out thromboembolic disease.
