Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nHistory of neuropathy\nRegularly taking prescribed analgesia\nHistory of a chronic pain condition\nHistory of severe mental illness (as their experience of symptoms may already be altered)\nCurrent use of fibrates (because of the risk of interaction with statins but will not exclude participants taking ezetimibe).\nSevere previous reaction or reaction considered immunological, such as anaphylaxis, facial swelling, severe rash, muscle ache with rise in serum creatine kinase, inflammatory myopathy, rhabdomyolysis or liver function abnormalities (aspartate transaminase (AST) or alanine transaminase (ALT) greater than 3 times upper limit or normal).\nSide-effects taking longer than 2 weeks to develop (because in such participants much longer blocks of treatment would be required, if the present study is positive such studies will be planned for the future)*.\nHistory of statin intolerance with drug interaction to antiretroviral drugs.\nHistory of statin intolerance to any other drug.\nPregnant or breast feeding.\nSide effects taking longer than 2 weeks to present.\nIn clinical judgement of study doctor, participant should not participate.\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nHistory of neuropathy\nRegularly taking prescribed analgesia\nHistory of a chronic pain condition\nHistory of severe mental illness (as their experience of symptoms may already be altered)\nCurrent use of fibrates (because of the risk of interaction with statins but will [NOT] not exclude participants taking ezetimibe).\nExclusion Criteria:\nSevere previous reaction [OR] or reaction considered immunological, such as anaphylaxis, [OR] facial swelling, severe rash, [OR] muscle ache [AND] with rise in serum creatine kinase, inflammatory myopathy, [OR] rhabdomyolysis [OR] or liver function abnormalities (aspartate transaminase (AST) [OR] or alanine transaminase (ALT) greater than 3 times upper limit of normal).\nSide-effects taking longer than 2 weeks to develop (because in such participants much longer blocks of treatment would be required, if the present study is positive such studies will be planned for the future)*.\nHistory of statin intolerance [AND] with drug interaction to antiretroviral drugs.\nHistory of statin intolerance to any other drug.\nPregnant [OR] or breast feeding.\nSide effects taking longer than 2 weeks to present.\nIn clinical judgement of study doctor, participant should [NOT] not participate.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
History of neuropathy
Regularly taking prescribed analgesia
History of a chronic pain condition
History of severe mental illness (as their experience of symptoms may already be altered)
Current use of fibrates (because of the risk of interaction with statins but will [NOT] not exclude participants taking ezetimibe).
Exclusion Criteria:
Severe previous reaction [OR] or reaction considered immunological, such as anaphylaxis, [OR] facial swelling, severe rash, [OR] muscle ache [AND] with rise in serum creatine kinase, inflammatory myopathy, [OR] rhabdomyolysis [OR] or liver function abnormalities (aspartate transaminase (AST) [OR] or alanine transaminase (ALT) greater than 3 times upper limit of normal).
Side-effects taking longer than 2 weeks to develop (because in such participants much longer blocks of treatment would be required, if the present study is positive such studies will be planned for the future)*.
History of statin intolerance [AND] with drug interaction to antiretroviral drugs.
History of statin intolerance to any other drug.
Pregnant [OR] or breast feeding.
Side effects taking longer than 2 weeks to present.
In clinical judgement of study doctor, participant should [NOT] not participate.
