may confound the outcome of the intervention\nPregnant, lactating, or planning to become pregnant during the course of the trial;\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nAge related cataract\nExclusion Criteria:\nPreexisting ocular diseases [OR] or conditions other than age related cataracts, have contraindications for cataract surgery;\nPreexisting systemic diseases [OR] or conditions that may confound the results of the study;\n Previous ocular surgery history [OR] or ocular trauma that may confound the results of the study;\n Require combined surgery that may confound the results of the study;\n Previous participation in other clinical trial within 30 days of this study start;\n Systemic [OR] or ocular medications that may confound the outcome of the intervention\nPregnant, [OR] lactating, [OR] or planning to become pregnant during the course of the trial;<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Age related cataract
Exclusion Criteria:
Preexisting ocular diseases [OR] or conditions other than age related cataracts, have contraindications for cataract surgery;
Preexisting systemic diseases [OR] or conditions that may confound the results of the study;
 Previous ocular surgery history [OR] or ocular trauma that may confound the results of the study;
 Require combined surgery that may confound the results of the study;
 Previous participation in other clinical trial within 30 days of this study start;
 Systemic [OR] or ocular medications that may confound the outcome of the intervention
Pregnant, [OR] lactating, [OR] or planning to become pregnant during the course of the trial;
