indication against ibuprofen (known or suspected allergy against ibuprofen, anaphylactic reaction against Nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drugs (NSAID), active or recurrent stomach or duodenal ulcera or bleeding, severe liver or renal insufficiency, inflammatory bowel syndrome, and pregnancy/breastfeeding)\npregnancy and breast feeding mothers\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nsimultaneous both sided extraction [OR] or only upper third molar extraction\ngeneral anesthesia\nknown [OR] or presumed abnormal coagulation status\nknown [OR] or presumed liver [OR] or renal dysfunction\ncontraindication against metamizole known [OR] or suspected (known [OR] or suspected allergy against novalgin [OR] or other pyrazolones, anaphylactic reaction against NSAIDS, decreased bone marrow function [OR] or hematopoesis, hepatic porphyria, [OR] glucose-6-phosphate dehydrogenase deficiency, [OR] and pregnancy/ [OR] breastfeeding)\ncontraindication against ibuprofen (known [OR] or suspected allergy against ibuprofen, anaphylactic reaction against Nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drugs (NSAID), active [OR] or recurrent stomach [OR] or duodenal ulcera [OR] or bleeding, severe liver [OR] or renal insufficiency, inflammatory bowel syndrome, [OR] and pregnancy/ [OR] breastfeeding)\npregnancy [OR] and breast feeding mothers<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
simultaneous both sided extraction [OR] or only upper third molar extraction
general anesthesia
known [OR] or presumed abnormal coagulation status
known [OR] or presumed liver [OR] or renal dysfunction
contraindication against metamizole known [OR] or suspected (known [OR] or suspected allergy against novalgin [OR] or other pyrazolones, anaphylactic reaction against NSAIDS, decreased bone marrow function [OR] or hematopoesis, hepatic porphyria, [OR] glucose-6-phosphate dehydrogenase deficiency, [OR] and pregnancy/ [OR] breastfeeding)
contraindication against ibuprofen (known [OR] or suspected allergy against ibuprofen, anaphylactic reaction against Nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drugs (NSAID), active [OR] or recurrent stomach [OR] or duodenal ulcera [OR] or bleeding, severe liver [OR] or renal insufficiency, inflammatory bowel syndrome, [OR] and pregnancy/ [OR] breastfeeding)
pregnancy [OR] and breast feeding mothers
