Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nFemale subjects who are pregnant or breast-feeding or considering becoming pregnant during the study\nPatients aged <18 years of age\nPatients who cannot give informed consent,\nPregnant patients or those who are breastfeeding will be deemed ineligible.\nPrior treatment with any anti-TNF agent\nContra-indication to use of GLM (Hypersensitivity to the active substance or to any of the excipients; Active tuberculosis (TB), acute or chronic Hepatitis B infection or other severe infections such as sepsis and/or opportunistic infections including HIV infection; Moderate or severe heart failure (NYHA class III/IV)\nHave symptoms or signs suggestive of current active or latent TB upon medical history, physical examination and/or chest radiograph, or positive Mycobacterium tuberculosis antigen-specific interferon-gamma release assay (IGRA)\nPatients with a history of, or at imminent risk for, colectomy; who required gastrointestinal surgery within 2 months before screening;\nHistory of colonic mucosal dysplasia or adenomatous colonic polyps that were not removed\nScreening stool study positive for enteric pathogens or Clostridium difficile toxin.\nOral corticosteroids at a dose >40 mg prednisone or its equivalent per day; receipt of cyclosporine, tacrolimus, sirolimus, or mycophenolate mofetil within 8 weeks before the first study agent injection; or use of an investigational agent within 5 half-lives of that agent before the first study agent injection.\nPatients in recent receipt of live vaccinations within 4 weeks prior to enrolment\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nFemale subjects [AND] who are pregnant [OR] or breast-feeding [OR] or considering becoming pregnant during the study\nPatients aged <18 years of age\nPatients who cannot give informed consent,\nPregnant  patients [OR] or those  who are breastfeeding will be deemed ineligible.\nPrior treatment with any anti-TNF agent\nContra-indication to use of GLM (Hypersensitivity to the active substance [OR] or to any of the excipients; Active tuberculosis (TB), acute [OR] or chronic Hepatitis B infection [OR] or other severe infections such as sepsis [OR] and/or opportunistic infections including HIV infection; Moderate [OR] or severe heart failure (NYHA class III/IV)\nHave symptoms [OR] or signs suggestive of current active [OR] or latent TB upon medical history, physical examination [OR] and/or chest radiograph, [OR] or positive Mycobacterium tuberculosis antigen-specific interferon-gamma release assay (IGRA)\nPatients with a history of, [OR] or at imminent risk for, colectomy; [AND] who required gastrointestinal surgery within 2 months before screening;\nHistory of colonic mucosal dysplasia [OR] or adenomatous colonic polyps [AND] that were [NOT] not removed\nScreening stool study positive for enteric pathogens [OR] or Clostridium difficile toxin.\nOral corticosteroids at a dose >40 mg prednisone [OR] or its equivalent per day; receipt of cyclosporine, [OR] tacrolimus, [OR] sirolimus, [OR] or mycophenolate mofetil within 8 weeks before the first study agent injection; [OR] or use of an investigational agent within 5 half-lives of that agent before the first study agent injection.\nPatients in recent receipt of live vaccinations within 4 weeks prior to enrolment<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Female subjects [AND] who are pregnant [OR] or breast-feeding [OR] or considering becoming pregnant during the study
Patients aged <18 years of age
Patients who cannot give informed consent,
Pregnant  patients [OR] or those  who are breastfeeding will be deemed ineligible.
Prior treatment with any anti-TNF agent
Contra-indication to use of GLM (Hypersensitivity to the active substance [OR] or to any of the excipients; Active tuberculosis (TB), acute [OR] or chronic Hepatitis B infection [OR] or other severe infections such as sepsis [OR] and/or opportunistic infections including HIV infection; Moderate [OR] or severe heart failure (NYHA class III/IV)
Have symptoms [OR] or signs suggestive of current active [OR] or latent TB upon medical history, physical examination [OR] and/or chest radiograph, [OR] or positive Mycobacterium tuberculosis antigen-specific interferon-gamma release assay (IGRA)
Patients with a history of, [OR] or at imminent risk for, colectomy; [AND] who required gastrointestinal surgery within 2 months before screening;
History of colonic mucosal dysplasia [OR] or adenomatous colonic polyps [AND] that were [NOT] not removed
Screening stool study positive for enteric pathogens [OR] or Clostridium difficile toxin.
Oral corticosteroids at a dose >40 mg prednisone [OR] or its equivalent per day; receipt of cyclosporine, [OR] tacrolimus, [OR] sirolimus, [OR] or mycophenolate mofetil within 8 weeks before the first study agent injection; [OR] or use of an investigational agent within 5 half-lives of that agent before the first study agent injection.
Patients in recent receipt of live vaccinations within 4 weeks prior to enrolment
