 (rifaxamin, nitazoxanide, tigecycline) after enrollment.\n\n\n### Response:\nPatients with severe-complicated disease that would compromise oral therapy (hypotenstion [OR] or shock, [OR] ileus [OR] or bowel obstruction, [OR] megacolon).\nPatients with an allergy to oral vancomycin [OR] or fidaxomicin.\nPatients anticipated to receive metronidazole after enrollment.\nPatients who already received oral vancomycin [OR] or metronidazole (either oral [OR] or intravenous) for > 24 hours within the preceding 72 hours at the time of enrollment.\nPatients anticipated to receive adjunctive C. difficile therapy (rifaxamin, [OR] nitazoxanide, [OR] tigecycline) after enrollment.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Patients with severe-complicated disease that would compromise oral therapy (hypotenstion [OR] or shock, [OR] ileus [OR] or bowel obstruction, [OR] megacolon).
Patients with an allergy to oral vancomycin [OR] or fidaxomicin.
Patients anticipated to receive metronidazole after enrollment.
Patients who already received oral vancomycin [OR] or metronidazole (either oral [OR] or intravenous) for > 24 hours within the preceding 72 hours at the time of enrollment.
Patients anticipated to receive adjunctive C. difficile therapy (rifaxamin, [OR] nitazoxanide, [OR] tigecycline) after enrollment.
