Acute critical limb ischemia
Severe critical limb ischemia (Rutherford category 6)
Major bleeding history within prior 2 months
Known hypersensitivity [OR] or contraindication to any of the following medications: heparin, [OR] aspirin, [OR] clopidogrel [OR] or contrast agents
Age > 85 years
Severe hepatic dysfunction (> 3 times normal reference values)
Significant renal dysfunction (Serum creatinine > 2.0 mg/dl
 Significant leucopenia, [OR] neutropenia, [OR] thrombocytopenia, [OR] anemia, [OR] or known bleeding diathesis
 LVEF <40% [OR] or clinically overt congestive heart failure
Pregnant women [OR] or women [AND] with potential childbearing
Life expectancy <1 year due to comorbidity
Previous bypass surgery [OR] or stenting of the superficial femoral artery
Untreated inflow disease [AND] of the ipsilateral pelvic arteries (more than 50%stenosis [OR] or or occlusion
Popliteal artery stenosis >50% at P2 [OR] or P3 segment
