Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] before a comma "," and before "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "to", "who", "in addition", "for", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having", "of", "on", "may", "as", "within", "by", "requiring", "should", "must have", "during", "have", "must", "are", "due", "according", "corresponding", "including".\n- Always write an [AND] after "history of".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "do not", "other than", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "besides", "prevent", "Inability", "absence", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nPsychiatric disorders other than insomnia, PTSD and specific phobias; including bipolar and psychotic disorders and meeting criteria for DSM-5 moderate alcohol or drug use disorders within the past year.\nDiagnosis of a sleep disorder other than insomnia including PSG findings of apnea/hypopnea or periodic limb movement indices > 10/hour;\nMedical conditions that require consistent use of medication or compromise sleep;\nHistory of moderate to severe traumatic brain injury or mild traumatic brain injury with ongoing post-concussive symptoms;\nSuicidal ideation with intent to act or with specific plan and intent in the past 6 months (Type 4 - 5 ideation on the Columbia Suicide Severity Rating Scale) or a concerning history of prior suicidal behavior.\nCaffeine use exceeding 5 cups of coffee per day or its equivalent;\nHabitual bedtimes after 3 AM, habitual rise times after 10 AM, or habitual napping > 1hour/day;\nPregnancy or breastfeeding, or expecting to conceive while in study;\nPositive urine toxicology.\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\n  -  Psychiatric disorders other than insomnia, [OR] PTSD [OR] and specific phobias; including bipolar [OR] and psychotic disorders [AND] and meeting criteria for DSM-5 moderate alcohol [OR] or drug use disorders within the past year.\n  -  Diagnosis of a sleep disorder other than insomnia including PSG findings of apnea/ [OR] hypopnea [OR] or periodic limb movement indices > 10/hour;\n  -  Medical conditions that require consistent use of medication [OR] or compromise sleep;\n  -  History of moderate to severe traumatic brain injury [OR] or mild traumatic brain injury [AND] with ongoing post-concussive symptoms;\n  -  Suicidal ideation [AND] with intent to act [OR] or with specific plan [AND] and intent in the past 6 months (Type 4 - 5 ideation on the Columbia Suicide Severity Rating Scale) [OR] or a concerning history of prior suicidal behavior.\n  -  Caffeine use exceeding 5 cups of coffee per day [OR] or its equivalent;\n  -  Habitual bedtimes after 3 AM, habitual rise times after 10 AM, [OR] or habitual napping > 1hour/day;\n  -  Pregnancy [OR] or breastfeeding, [OR] or expecting to conceive while in study;\n  -  Positive urine toxicology.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
  -  Psychiatric disorders other than insomnia, [OR] PTSD [OR] and specific phobias; including bipolar [OR] and psychotic disorders [AND] and meeting criteria for DSM-5 moderate alcohol [OR] or drug use disorders within the past year.
  -  Diagnosis of a sleep disorder other than insomnia including PSG findings of apnea/ [OR] hypopnea [OR] or periodic limb movement indices > 10/hour;
  -  Medical conditions that require consistent use of medication [OR] or compromise sleep;
  -  History of moderate to severe traumatic brain injury [OR] or mild traumatic brain injury [AND] with ongoing post-concussive symptoms;
  -  Suicidal ideation [AND] with intent to act [OR] or with specific plan [AND] and intent in the past 6 months (Type 4 - 5 ideation on the Columbia Suicide Severity Rating Scale) [OR] or a concerning history of prior suicidal behavior.
  -  Caffeine use exceeding 5 cups of coffee per day [OR] or its equivalent;
  -  Habitual bedtimes after 3 AM, habitual rise times after 10 AM, [OR] or habitual napping > 1hour/day;
  -  Pregnancy [OR] or breastfeeding, [OR] or expecting to conceive while in study;
  -  Positive urine toxicology.
