rgically removed basal or squamous cell carcinoma of the skin\nKnown or suspected hepatic, symptomatic biliary disease (this includes moderate to severe chronic hepatic impairment)\nPatients with clinically significant laboratory abnormalities / disorders other than prostate cancer\nPatient with Hepatitis B Virus (HBV), Hepatitis C Virus (HCV) and Human Immunodeficiency Virus (HIV) infections\n\n\n### Response:\nPrevious [OR] or concurrent hormonal management of prostate cancer\nContraindication for prescription of Firmagon®\nConcurrent treatment with a 5-a-reductase inhibitor\nConsidered as a candidate for curative therapy\nHistory of severe [NOT] untreated asthma, [OR] anaphylactic reactions [OR] or severe urticaria [OR] and/or angioedema\nQTc interval over 450 msec [OR] or risk factors for torsades de pointes [OR] or on Class IA [OR] and Class III anti arrhythmic medications\nCancer within the last 5 years except prostate cancer [OR] and surgically removed basal [OR] or squamous cell carcinoma of the skin\nKnown [OR] or suspected hepatic, symptomatic biliary disease (this includes moderate [OR] to severe chronic hepatic impairment)\nPatients with clinically significant laboratory abnormalities [OR] / disorders other than prostate cancer\nPatient with Hepatitis B Virus (HBV), [OR] Hepatitis C Virus (HCV) [OR] and Human Immunodeficiency Virus (HIV) infections<|eot_id|>']
