ety (HAM-A >24)\nSignificant suicide or violence risk\nCurrently taking any psychotropic medications\nLegally mandated to participate in treatment\nHistory of prior treatment with disulfiram\nSufficiently socially unstable as to preclude participation (e.g. homeless)\nContraindications to disulfiram treatment (liver disease, kidney disease, cardiac disease, seizure disorder, hypothyroidism, diabetes mellitus, pregnancy or lactation, allergy to disulfiram or thiuran derivatives)\nNeurological or medical conditions that would interfere with MRI scanning (e.g. history of stroke, seizure, brain tumor, brain infection, traumatic brain injury, multiple sclerosis, dementia, metal device in body, pregnancy, claustrophobia, color blindness, severe hearing impairment, weight>300 lbs., wheelchair-bound)\nCurrently taking medications containing alcohol, metronidazole, isoniazid, paraldehyde, phenytoin, warfarin, or theophylline.\nSignificant alcohol withdrawal (CIWA>8) at screening, after confirming a blood alcohol level of zero.\n\n\n### Response:\nRisk of severe alcohol withdrawal (e.g. history of seizures [OR] or delirium tremens)\nCurrent Moderate [OR] or Severe Substance Use Disorder, other than Alcohol, [OR] Nicotine [OR] or Caffeine Use Disorders\nLifetime history of Bipolar Disorder, [OR] Schizophrenia [OR] or Schizoaffective Disorder\nAny current psychiatric disorder, other than Alcohol Use Disorder, that, in the judgment of the investigator, will require treatment that will interfere with study participation.\nCurrent severe depression (HAM-D >24) [OR] or anxiety (HAM-A >24)\nSignificant suicide [OR] or violence risk\nCurrently taking any psychotropic medications\nLegally mandated to participate in treatment\nHistory of prior treatment with disulfiram\nSufficiently socially unstable as to [NOT] preclude participation (e.g. homeless)\nContraindications to disulfiram treatment (liver disease, [OR] kidney disease, [OR] cardiac disease, [OR] seizure disorder, [OR] hypothyroidism, [OR] diabetes mellitus, [OR] pregnancy [OR] or lactation, allergy to disulfiram [OR] or thiuran derivatives)\nNeurological [OR] or medical conditions that would interfere with MRI scanning (e.g. history of stroke, [OR] seizure, [OR] brain tumor, [OR] brain infection, [OR] traumatic brain injury, [OR] multiple sclerosis, [OR] dementia, [OR] metal device in body, pregnancy, [OR] claustrophobia, [OR] color blindness, severe hearing impairment, weight>300 lbs., wheelchair-bound)\nCurrently taking medications containing alcohol, [OR] metronidazole, [OR] isoniazid, [OR] paraldehyde, [OR] phenytoin, [OR] warfarin, [OR] or theophylline.\nSignificant alcohol withdrawal (CIWA>8) at screening, after confirming a blood alcohol level of zero.<|eot_id|>']
